t["subzone:webwinder-path"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,242,26.465.0,31.145.0,32.195.0,31.166.0,33.205.0",["h"]="777266",["n"]="Senda de las Tejedoras",["s"]="Senda de las Tejedoras. La Senda de las Tejedoras es un sinuoso camino montañoso en Sierra Espolón que conecta el puesto de avanzada trol de Malaka'jin con el Lago Mirkfallon. Atraviesa riscos escarpados y densos bosques de tierras altas habitados por arácnidos agresivos y bestias autóctonas. Discurriendo desde el asentamiento de la Horda de Malaka'jin hacia el Lago Mirkfallon, la Senda de las Tejedoras sirve como una de las principales vías que surcan la parte baja de Sierra Espolón. Fiel a su nombre, la ruta es tristemente célebre por las gruesas telarañas tendidas en lo alto del dosel arbóreo y a lo largo de los escarpados acantilados. Los viajeros que recorren este sinuoso tramo deben vigilar constantemente por dónde pisan, compartiendo el camino trillado con arañas de montaña al acecho, agresivos lagartos trueno y carneros territoriales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The path is home to robust thunder lizards, sturdy mountain rams, and venomous web-spinners, making it an excellent trail for scouting and taming Stonetalon beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="The path is a crucial overland artery right on the doorstep of Malaka'jin, connecting your scouts to the deeper valleys of Stonetalon."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Webwinder Path stretches between the Darkspear troll outpost of Malaka'jin in the south and Mirkfallon Lake further up the mountain to the north.",["al"]={"webwinder path location","where is webwinder path","what does webwinder path connect"},["q"]="Where does Webwinder Path lead?"},{["a"]="The road earns its name from the sheer abundance of arachnids inhabiting the region. Spiders spin vast labyrinths of glittering silk high in the trees and along rocky ledges flanking the roadway.",["al"]={"why webwinder","why is it called webwinder"},["q"]="Why is it called Webwinder Path?"},{["a"]="Aside from the venomous spiders that weave webs above the road, travelers frequently encounter roaming thunder lizards, highland rams, and ordinary mountain critters.",["al"]={"what lives here","webwinder path beasts","mobs on webwinder path"},["q"]="What creatures wander the path?"},{["a"]="It is far from safe. The local predators are fierce and territorial, and the road passes directly past the Horde camp at Malaka'jin, making it perilous for Alliance wayfarers venturing up from the Barrens.",["al"]={"is webwinder path dangerous","can alliance travel webwinder path"},["q"]="Is Webwinder Path safe to travel?"}},["kw"]={"malaka'jin","mirkfallon lake","road","spiders","stonetalon","webwinder","webwinder path"},["n"]="Webwinder Path",["s"]="Webwinder Path is a winding mountainous road in the Stonetalon Mountains connecting the troll outpost of Malaka'jin to Mirkfallon Lake. It cuts through rugged crags and dense highland woods inhabited by aggressive arachnids and native beasts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running from the Horde settlement of Malaka'jin toward Mirkfallon Lake, Webwinder Path serves as one of the primary roadways carving through the lower Stonetalon Mountains. True to its name, the route is notorious for the thick cobwebs strung high among the canopy and jagged cliff sides. Travelers along this winding stretch must constantly watch their step, sharing the beaten path with prowling mountain spiders, aggressive thunder lizards, and territorial rams.",["t"]="A Treacherous Thoroughfare"}}}}}
t["subzone:wellspring-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,384,16.584.0,33.127.0,45.193.0,49.252.0,38.161.0",["h"]="ac19b2",["n"]="Lago Primigenio",["s"]="Lago Primigenio. El Lago Primigenio es una serena masa de agua dulce que descansa en lo alto de las ramas de Teldrassil, situada al noreste de Darnassus. Alimentadas por manantiales naturales procedentes de lo más profundo del Árbol del Mundo, sus aguas nutren el serpenteante Río Primigenio. Lo que antaño fuera un retiro pacífico para los pescadores elfos de la noche, ahora ve sus orillas víctimas de la creciente corrupción que perturba a la fauna de Teldrassil. Ubicado bajo el dosel arbóreo entre Darnassus y El Claro del Oráculo, el Lago Primigenio fue durante mucho tiempo muy apreciado por los kaldorei como un tranquilo remanso para la pesca y la contemplación. Sus aguas transparentes provienen de manantiales subterráneos que recorren las colosales ramas del Árbol del Mundo, los cuales desaguan luego hacia el norte a través del Río Primigenio. En tiempos recientes, sin embargo, una insidiosa plaga ha comenzado a apoderarse de la naturaleza circundante. Arañas agresivas, sables de la noche al acecho y agitados timberlings merodean ahora por las orillas, convirtiendo lo que antaño fue un estanque idílico en un lugar traicionero para los viajeros incautos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids study the agitated timberlings and beasts near Wellspring Lake to understand the source of the unnatural sickness spreading through Teldrassil's waters and soil.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the degradation of peaceful groves like Wellspring Lake into dangerous monster dens is a painful reminder that something has gone deeply wrong with their young World Tree."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Wellspring Lake lies in northern Teldrassil, northeast of the capital city of Darnassus and just southeast of the Oracle Glade.",["al"]={"where is wellspring lake","wellspring lake location","how to get to wellspring lake"},["q"]="Where is Wellspring Lake located?"},{["a"]="The lake is fed by natural springs rising deep from within the roots and wood of Teldrassil itself. The excess water drains into the Wellspring River, which flows north to the edge of the tree.",["al"]={"where does wellspring lake drain","wellspring river source","wellspring lake water source"},["q"]="Where does the lake's water come from and go?"},{["a"]="While it was previously a tranquil spot favored by Kaldorei anglers, the spreading corruption across the World Tree has driven local beasts mad. Prowling nightsabers, giant webwood spiders, and corrupted timberling bark-spirits now stalk the shoreline.",["al"]={"what lives at wellspring lake","wellspring lake mobs","why is wellspring lake hostile"},["q"]="Why is the area around Wellspring Lake dangerous?"},{["a"]="Local night elven fishermen often visited the lake for quiet reflection and angling before the recent blight agitated the wildlife and made the shores hazardous.",["al"]={"wellspring lake history","night elf fishermen lake"},["q"]="Who used to gather at Wellspring Lake?"}},["kw"]={"darnassus","kaldorei","nightsaber","oracle glade","teldrassil","timberlings","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},["n"]="Wellspring Lake",["s"]="Wellspring Lake is a serene body of fresh water resting high within the boughs of Teldrassil, situated northeast of Darnassus. Fed by natural springs originating from deep within the World Tree, its waters feed the winding Wellspring River. Once a peaceful retreat for night elf fishermen, the lake's shores have fallen prey to the growing corruption unsettling Teldrassil's wildlife.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled beneath the canopy between Darnassus and the Oracle Glade, Wellspring Lake was long cherished by the Kaldorei as a quiet haven for fishing and contemplation. Its clear waters originate from subterranean springs running through the colossal boughs of the World Tree, which then drain northward through the Wellspring River. In recent times, however, an insidious blight has begun to seize the surrounding wilds. Aggressive spiders, prowling nightsabers, and agitated timberlings now roam the banks, making what was once an idyllic pond a treacherous place for unwary travelers.",["t"]="A Tainted Refuge"}}}}}
t["subzone:wellspring-river"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,318,24.486.0,37.221.0,57.249.0,44.173.0",["h"]="06a57e",["n"]="Río Primigenio",["s"]="Río Primigenio. El Río Primigenio mana de un manantial natural dentro de Teldrassil, fluyendo hacia el norte desde el Lago Primigenio hasta precipitarse desde las ramas en una imponente cascada hacia el océano que se encuentra muy por debajo. En su día una fuente pacífica de agua dulce para el ecosistema del Árbol del Mundo, sus orillas se han vuelto peligrosas debido a la agitada fauna local. Alimentado por los profundos manantiales naturales cobijados en las ramas de Teldrassil, el Río Primigenio transporta agua hacia el norte desde el Lago Primigenio a través del verde suelo del bosque antes de precipitarse de forma espectacular sobre el borde del gran árbol hacia el mar. A pesar del entorno sereno, las riberas del río son cada vez más inseguras. Los briznados que habitan a lo largo del agua han enloquecido y se han vuelto hostiles, atacando violentamente a los viajeros y druidas que intentan acercarse a la orilla del río.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The corrupted and maddened state of the river's native timberlings is an unsettling sign of the growing sickness creeping through Teldrassil's ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="The freshwater waterways flowing from the heart of Teldrassil represent the vitality of the Kaldorei's new home, making the unrest along their banks deeply concerning."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Wellspring River flows northward out of Wellspring Lake. Eventually, it reaches the rim of Teldrassil's canopy and plunges over the edge in an enormous waterfall that drops all the way down into the surrounding ocean.",["al"]={"where does river flow","wellspring river destination","where does wellspring river go"},["q"]="Where does the Wellspring River lead?"},{["a"]="The timberlings along the Wellspring River have become erratic and crazed, turning on anyone who wanders nearby. This aggression is part of a broader disturbance spreading through Teldrassil's natural wildlife, alarming the local night elven druids.",["al"]={"why are timberlings aggressive","crazed timberlings wellspring","why timberlings hostile"},["q"]="Why are the timberlings along the river attacking people?"},{["a"]="The river is fed directly by Wellspring Lake, which itself is sustained by a natural freshwater spring rising deep from within the living trunk and boughs of the World Tree.",["al"]={"wellspring water source","where does wellspring water come from"},["q"]="Where does the water in the river come from?"}},["kw"]={"kaldorei","teldrassil","timberlings","waterfall","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},["n"]="Wellspring River",["s"]="The Wellspring River flows from a natural spring within Teldrassil, coursing north out of Wellspring Lake until it plummets off the boughs in a towering waterfall to the ocean far below. Once a peaceful source of fresh water for the World Tree's ecosystem, its banks have grown perilous due to agitated local wildlife.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nourished by the deep natural springs nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, the Wellspring River carries water north from Wellspring Lake across the verdant forest floor before cascading dramatically over the edge of the great tree down into the sea below. Despite the serene surroundings, the riverbanks are increasingly unsafe. The timberlings that dwell along the water have grown crazed and hostile, violently attacking travelers and druids who attempt to draw near the river's edge.",["t"]="Waters of the World Tree"}}}}}
t["subzone:westbrook-garrison"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,300,25.608.0,27.516.0,42.261.0,34.192.0,36.176.0,52.187.0",["h"]="7f55c1",["n"]="Cuartel Arroyoeste",["s"]="Cuartel Arroyoeste. El Cuartel Arroyoeste es un puesto avanzado de la guardia de Ventormenta situado en el extremo occidental del Bosque de Elwynn, cerca de la frontera con los Páramos de Poniente. Atendido por una dotación mínima, sobrecargada de trabajo y desabastecida bajo el mando del Ayudante del alguacil Rainer, sirve como primera línea de defensa del reino contra el avance de los gnolls Zarparrío y los bandidos errantes. Ubicado donde el Bosque de Elwynn comienza a clarear hacia los Páramos de Poniente, el Cuartel Arroyoeste se erige como un punto de vigilancia vital pero en apuros. Con gran parte del ejército de Ventormenta comprometido en el extranjero o atado por la inercia política en la capital, el puesto se ha quedado en una situación crítica por falta de personal. El Ayudante del alguacil Rainer y su puñado de guardias deben patrullar los caminos occidentales mientras repelen a ladrones envalentonados y a los despiadados gnolls Zarparrío, que han invadido los bosques del sur. Incapaz de conseguir refuerzos oficiales del Alguacil Dughan en Villadorada, el cuartel depende casi por completo de los aventureros de paso para asegurar el camino principal.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="The beleaguered guards at Westbrook represent an overstretched kingdom holding back wilderness predators with sheer grit, offering plenty of straightforward, brutal work clearing gnoll war bands.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions setting out from Elwynn toward Westfall, securing Westbrook's perimeter and claiming the bounty on Hogger is essential to keeping the heartland's western borders secure."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The bulk of the Stormwind Army is deployed abroad, and political indecision within the capital's House of Nobles has starved regional garrisons of fresh troops and supplies. Westbrook's commanders must rely heavily on wandering adventurers to pick up the slack.",["al"]={"why so few guards","westbrook reinforcements","deputy rainer lacking troops"},["q"]="Why is Westbrook Garrison so understaffed?"},{["a"]="Deputy Rainer oversees operations at Westbrook Garrison. He answers directly to Marshal Dughan stationed at Goldshire, though his requests for additional soldiers have largely gone unanswered.",["al"]={"who leads westbrook garrison","deputy rainer role","westbrook commander"},["q"]="Who is in command at the garrison?"},{["a"]="The garrison deals with wandering bandits spilling out of Westfall and the ferocious Riverpaw gnolls who camp in the surrounding woods, led by their dangerous chieftain Hogger.",["al"]={"threats to westbrook","gnolls westbrook","who attacks westbrook garrison"},["q"]="What threats does the garrison face?"},{["a"]="Westbrook Garrison is the final outpost in Elwynn Forest along the western road before crossing the bridge into Westfall, guarding the border against the lawlessness rising from the west.",["al"]={"is westbrook in westfall","border to westfall"},["q"]="What is the relation between Westbrook and Westfall?"}},["kw"]={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","forest's edge","hogger","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison","westfall"},["n"]="Westbrook Garrison",["s"]="Westbrook Garrison is a Stormwind Guard outpost situated on the western edge of Elwynn Forest near the Westfall border. Manned by an overworked, under-supplied skeleton crew under Deputy Rainer, it serves as the realm's first line of defense against the encroaching Riverpaw gnolls and rogue bandits.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned where Elwynn Forest begins to thin toward Westfall, Westbrook Garrison stands as a vital but struggling watchpoint. With much of the Stormwind Army committed abroad or tied down by political inertia in the capital, the outpost has been left critically shorthanded. Deputy Rainer and his handful of guards must patrol the western roads while fending off emboldened thieves and the vicious Riverpaw gnolls who have overrun the southern woods. Unable to secure formal reinforcements from Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, the garrison relies almost entirely on traveling adventurers to secure the highway.",["t"]="A Beleaguered Border Post"},{["b"]="The primary threat facing Westbrook is the swelling gnoll presence centered around the south of Forest's Edge. The packs have grown bold enough to stage raids directly on supply lines and homesteads, organized under the fearsome gnoll chieftain known as Hogger. Outnumbered and overwhelmed by the brute strength of Hogger's forces, the garrison has posted a high bounty across its grounds, desperately seeking capable fighters willing to venture into the hills and bring down the beast before he pushes farther east.",["t"]="The Menace of Forest's Edge"}}}}}
t["subzone:westfall-lighthouse"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,333,20.561.0,17.438.1,41.213.0,23.244.0,20.183.0,35.184.0",["h"]="074915",["n"]="Faro de Poniente",["s"]="Faro de Poniente. Encaramado en un islote rocoso frente a la costa suroccidental de Páramos de Poniente, el Faro de Poniente antaño advertía a los barcos de los peligrosos bajíos de Mare Magnum. Hoy en día, sus guardianes vivos han desaparecido, aniquilados en un brutal asalto liderado por el infame múrloc Viejo Ojosombrío, dejando solo al espíritu del Capitán Grisillo para vigilar la llama. Construido a lo largo de los traicioneros acantilados del suroeste de Páramos de Poniente, el faro proporcionó durante mucho tiempo un paso seguro a los barcos que navegaban por la costa cercana a Ventormenta. Sin embargo, a medida que la ley y el orden se desmoronaban en la región y las patrullas reales mermaban, los peligros costeros aumentaron sin control. En su origen, una familia de guardianes cuidaba de la baliza, pero las agresivas tribus de múrlocs los obligaron a retirarse tierra adentro. Aunque regresaron valientemente para volver a encender la torre, el infame asaltante múrloc Viejo Ojosombrío reunió a los suyos para una segunda e implacable embestida, masacrando a la familia y extinguiendo la baliza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The lighthouse stands as a stark symbol of Stormwind's failing reach, where isolated kingdom servants were abandoned to savage coastal beasts without military support."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The human family that tended the lighthouse was driven out by local murlocs. When they returned to relight the beacon, Old Murk-Eye led a second raid that massacred the entire family before Captain Grayson's eyes.",["al"]={"what happened to the keepers","who lived at the lighthouse","why is it ruined"},["q"]="Why is the Westfall Lighthouse abandoned?"},{["a"]="Captain Grayson is a ghost haunting the island outside the lighthouse. Bound by guilt and duty after witnessing the keepers' deaths, he tasks brave travelers with gathering oil to keep the beacon lit and hunting the coastal murlocs responsible.",["al"]={"ghost at lighthouse","who is the ghost","captain grayson lore"},["q"]="Who is Captain Grayson?"},{["a"]="Old Murk-Eye is an unusually cunning and vicious murloc chieftain who stalks the Westfall shoreline. He rallied the coastal tribes to overrun the lighthouse and slaughter the keepers.",["al"]={"murk eye","murloc boss","who killed the keepers"},["q"]="Who is Old Murk-Eye?"},{["a"]="The mechanical lantern still functions, projecting a sweeping beam of light across the ocean at night, while Captain Grayson asks travelers for the oil needed to keep the fire burning.",["al"]={"does the light turn on","beacon working"},["q"]="Does the lighthouse still function?"}},["kw"]={"beacon","captain grayson","coast","flame","lighthouse","murloc","old murk-eye","westfall"},["n"]="Westfall Lighthouse",["s"]="Perched on a rocky isle off the southwestern shore of Westfall, the Westfall Lighthouse once warned vessels away from the perilous shallows of the Great Sea. Today, its living keepers are gone, wiped out in a brutal assault led by the notorious murloc Old Murk-Eye, leaving only the spirit of Captain Grayson to watch over the flame.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built along the treacherous southwestern bluffs of Westfall, the lighthouse long provided safe passage for ships navigating the coastline near Stormwind. However, as law and order collapsed across the region and royal patrols dwindled, coastal dangers surged unchecked. A family of keepers originally tended the beacon, but aggressive murloc tribes drove them inland. Though they bravely returned to relight the tower, the infamous murloc raider Old Murk-Eye rallied his kin for a second, merciless onslaught, butchering the family and extinguishing the beacon.",["t"]="A Beacon in the Mist"},{["b"]="Following the tragedy, the beacon did not remain entirely abandoned. The specter of Captain Grayson now lingers on the rocky outcrop, bound to the site where he helplessly witnessed the family's demise. Unable to rest while the beacon is dark and the shore crawls with monsters, Grayson enlists passing adventurers to gather oil from the harvest golems to keep the flame burning and to hunt down Old Murk-Eye to avenge the fallen keepers.",["t"]="The Ghostly Watch"}}}}}
t["subzone:whispering-forest"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,273,15.481.0,28.542.1,39.205.0,42.216.0,28.197.0,52.261.0,19.221.0",["h"]="9043ac",["n"]="Bosque Susurrante",["s"]="Bosque Susurrante. El Bosque Susurrante es un bosque montañoso y apartado, enclavado tras los escarpados acantilados al oeste de Camposanto. Prácticamente aislado del resto de los Claros de Tirisfal, alberga una fauna insólita, un misterioso círculo de hadas y una profunda corrupción que duerme bajo el suelo. Escondido tras Roca de la Cara Norte y el Castillo de Bandarion, el Bosque Susurrante parece completamente ajeno al reino azotado por la plaga que lo rodea. Aunque en él habitan ciervos afligidos y depredadores errantes, también cuenta con un lago apacible y un extraño círculo de setas gigantes que brillan con una energía insólita bajo una nube flotante de niebla. El fantasmal Knight of Mourning vaga por el círculo de hadas, atado a él por juramento, en medio de una magia natural que parece desafiar la tierra asolada por la Plaga.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The glowing faerie ring stands out as one of the few pulses of natural magic remaining within blighted Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="Nestled just past Deathknell and overseen by Tyr's Watch at Bandarion Keep, the secluded woodland hides forgotten dangers that pose a silent threat right on the Undercity's doorstep."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The forest lies in the mountains of western Tirisfal Glades, positioned just west of Deathknell and south of Tyr's Fall. It is walled off by Northface Rock, the steep ridge upon which Bandarion Keep rests.",["al"]={"whispering forest location","where is whispering forest","how to get to whispering forest"},["q"]="Where is the Whispering Forest located?"},{["a"]="The ring of giant mushrooms glows with a strange energy beneath a hovering cloud of mist. The ghostly Knight of Mourning wanders the circle, bound there by an oath, but what the ring's magic truly is remains unknown.",["al"]={"mushroom circle tirisfal","faerie dragon ring","fairy ring ritual"},["q"]="What happens at the giant mushroom circle?"},{["a"]="The overlooking heights of Bandarion Keep are held by Tyr's Watch, an order of Forsaken paladins. Near the fairy circle itself, the spectral Knight of Mourning is bound by oath to wander the woods.",["al"]={"who guards whispering forest","bandarion keep whispering forest"},["q"]="Who watches over the forest?"},{["a"]="When the high elves originally landed on Lordaeron's shores, they attempted to build a settlement in Tirisfal. Within a few years, an unsettling presence buried deep underground began eroding their sanity, compelling them to abandon the glades and travel north.",["al"]={"high elves tirisfal","why elves left tirisfal","madness beneath tirisfal"},["q"]="Why did the high elves abandon this region long ago?"},{["a"]="Shadowvale is a ruined village situated southwest of the forest's lake. It is occupied by the Tarnished alongside mindless undead afflicted by a necromantic crystal fragment dating back to clashes involving the Undercity.",["al"]={"shadowvale tirisfal","ruined village whispering forest"},["q"]="What is Shadowvale?"}},["kw"]={"bandarion keep","blightsculler","deathknell","faerie ring","shadowvale","tirisfal","whispering forest"},["n"]="Whispering Forest",["s"]="The Whispering Forest is a secluded, mountainous woodland nestled behind the steep cliffs west of Deathknell. Largely cut off from the rest of Tirisfal Glades, it harbors uncanny wildlife, a mysterious fairy circle, and deep-seated corruption sleeping far beneath the soil.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away behind Northface Rock and Bandarion Keep, the Whispering Forest feels entirely alienated from the surrounding plague-touched kingdom. While it contains afflicted deer and roaming predators, it also features a tranquil lake and a strange ring of giant mushrooms, glowing with an uncanny energy beneath a hovering cloud of mist. The ghostly Knight of Mourning wanders the fairy circle, bound there by oath, amid a natural magic that seems to defy the Scourge-ruined land.",["t"]="The Hidden Glen"},{["b"]="Despite its outward wonder, the forest is tainted by an ancient dread. Centuries ago, the high elves briefly attempted to settle in Tirisfal Glades before being driven away when the latent evil sleeping deep underground began driving them mad. Around the local lake, Vile Fin murlocs and the undead threshadon Blightsculler prowl the waters, while the ruined settlement of Shadowvale lies blighted by necromantic remnants. Even mad wanderers across Lordaeron mutter fearful warnings of the consuming darkness resting beneath Tirisfal's roots.",["t"]="The Shadow Beneath the Woods"}}}}}
t["subzone:whispering-shore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,263,14.468.0,17.299.0,38.111.0,59.136.0,38.171.0,54.183.0",["h"]="5ac93d",["n"]="Costa Murmurante",["s"]="Costa Murmurante. La Costa Murmurante es un sombrío tramo de costa en el oeste de Claros de Tirisfal, situado justo al norte de la Hacienda Solliden. En su día un refugio tranquilo y generoso para los pescadores de Lordaeron, sus frías aguas han sido invadidas desde entonces por una violenta tribu de múrlocs. Antes de que la Tercera Guerra arrasara el norte de Lordaeron, la Costa Murmurante era famosa entre los lugareños por ser un apreciado refugio de pesca, célebre por sus aguas tranquilas y sus abundantes capturas. Hoy en día, el gélido rocío del Mare Magnum rompe contra una costa vacía y despojada de su pacífico pasado. Las aguas se han vuelto frías y oscuras, carentes de su antigua generosidad, y cualquier viajero desafortunado que baje de las colinas se arriesga a sufrir una emboscada a manos de territoriales habitantes costeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken securing western Tirisfal Glades, the murloc infestation at Whispering Shore poses an unruly threat right along the perimeter of their holdings."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Whispering Shore lies along the western coast of Tirisfal Glades, directly north of the Solliden Farmstead.",["al"]={"whispering shore location","where is whispering shore","whispering shore map"},["q"]="Where is the Whispering Shore located?"},{["a"]="In the days of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, the shore was a beloved and tranquil spot for local fishermen drawn to its rich coastal waters.",["al"]={"whispering shore history","what was whispering shore used for","whispering shore past"},["q"]="What used to be at the Whispering Shore before the Scourge?"},{["a"]="A tribe of aggressive murlocs has taken over the coastline. They are led by a particularly vicious murloc chieftain named Muad, attacking anyone who strays near the water.",["al"]={"who lives on whispering shore","whispering shore enemies","whispering shore mobs"},["q"]="Who controls the Whispering Shore now?"},{["a"]="The coastline is no longer the peaceful haven it once was. Its waters are cold and dark, having lost much of their former bounty, and hostile murlocs aggressively guard the shoreline.",["al"]={"fishing at whispering shore","whispering shore fish"},["q"]="Can you still fish peacefully at the Whispering Shore?"}},["kw"]={"coast","fishing","muad","murloc","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","whispering shore"},["n"]="Whispering Shore",["s"]="The Whispering Shore is a somber stretch of coastline in western Tirisfal Glades, resting just north of the Solliden Farmstead. Once a tranquil and bountiful retreat for Lordaeron's fishermen, its cold waters have since been overrun by a violent tribe of murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War swept across northern Lordaeron, the Whispering Shore was renowned among locals as a favored fishing haven, celebrated for its calm waters and plentiful catches. Today, the chilling spray of the Great Sea crashes against an empty coast stripped of its peaceful past. The waters have grown cold and dark, devoid of their former bounty, and any unfortunate traveler wandering down from the hills risks being ambushed by territorial coastal dwellers.",["t"]="A Ruined Haven"},{["b"]="The beach is now firmly claimed by a band of hostile murlocs who ruthlessly attack anyone approaching the surf. Led by a fierce chieftain named Muad, these aquatic scavengers guard the shallows and tidal flats aggressively, posing a constant danger to nearby roads and the nearby Solliden Farmstead.",["t"]="The Murloc Menace"}}}}}
t["subzone:whitereach-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,351,27.506.0,24.134.0,39.105.0,32.131.0",["h"]="1adc1c",["n"]="Campamento del Tramo Blanco",["s"]="Campamento del Tramo Blanco. El Campamento del Tramo Blanco es un pequeño campamento de la Horda situado junto al polvoriento camino del cañón en Las Mil Agujas. Al funcionar como una parada menor cerca del Campamento E'thok, ofrece descanso y vigilancia sobre la dura ruta del desierto. Para los viajeros que se desplazan entre Feralas y los salares, se erige como un puesto de avanzada seguro de la Horda bajo los imponentes pilares de arenisca. Ubicado a lo largo del sendero trillado que serpentea por las profundidades de Las Mil Agujas, el Campamento del Tramo Blanco es uno de los diversos y modestos enclaves de la Horda labrados en el escarpado paisaje. Emplazado muy cerca del Campamento E'thok, el puesto ayuda a mantener una presencia constante en el fondo del cañón, vigilando el tránsito entre las mesetas azotadas por el viento. Aunque no está tan fortificado como El Gran Elevador o los principales asentamientos tribales, sirve como una parada indispensable para mensajeros, exploradores y aventureros que cruzan estos páramos en disputa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Whitereach Post represents a vital resting point and scouting presence for Horde travelers journeying through the perilous canyons of Thousand Needles.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren scouts help secure this roadside camp, ensuring that tribesfolk moving between Mulgore, Feralas, and the Shimmering Flats have a safe place to rest."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Whitereach Post is a minor Horde outpost located along the primary canyon path in Thousand Needles, situated not far from Camp E'thok.",["al"]={"whitereach","whitereach camp","where is whitereach post"},["q"]="What is Whitereach Post?"},{["a"]="It is controlled by the Horde, primarily maintained by tauren scouts keeping watch over the gorge trails.",["al"]={"is whitereach horde","whitereach faction"},["q"]="Which faction controls Whitereach Post?"},{["a"]="The post is manned by local Horde scouts and wanderers, including the tauren Kanati Greycloud, who watches over the canyon passage.",["al"]={"whitereach npcs","who lives at whitereach post"},["q"]="Who can be found stationed here?"}},["kw"]={"camp e'thok","horde outpost","kanati greycloud","tauren","thousand needles","whitereach post"},["n"]="Whitereach Post",["s"]="Whitereach Post is a small Horde encampment nestled along the dusty canyon path in Thousand Needles. Serving as a minor waystation near Camp E'thok, it offers respite and watchful eyes over the harsh desert highway. For travelers moving between Feralas and the salt flats, it stands as an outpost of Horde safety beneath the looming sandstone pillars.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched along the beaten path winding through the depths of Thousand Needles, Whitereach Post is one of several modest Horde footholds carved out of the rugged landscape. Stationed in close proximity to Camp E'thok, the post helps maintain a reliable presence along the canyon floor, monitoring travel between the windswept mesas. While not as fortified as the great lift or major tribal settlements, it serves as an indispensable stop for couriers, scouts, and adventurers traversing the contested wastes.",["t"]="A Waystation in the Canyons"}}}}}
t["subzone:wildbend-river"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,267,23.531.0,36.253.0,26.186.0,48.248.0",["h"]="cbf762",["n"]="Río Culebra",["s"]="Río Culebra. El Río Culebra es un cauce contaminado que serpentea por los bosques meridionales de Costa Oscura, cerca del Páramo de los Ancestros. Fluyendo directamente desde las corrompidas alturas de Frondavil, sus aguas arrastran veneno demoníaco hacia el mar, poniendo en peligro la naturaleza circundante. El Río Culebra atraviesa los confines meridionales de Costa Oscura, fluyendo hacia el oeste más allá del sagrado Páramo de los Ancestros antes de desembocar en el mar. En lugar de ofrecer un sustento limpio al bosque, hace descender la corrupción desde las montañas. El río es la continuación directa del Río del Veneno de Frondavil, cayendo entre las crestas rocosas y arrastrando fétidas escorrentías corruptas hacia el ecosistema de Costa Oscura. Los elfos de la noche vigilan sus orillas muy de cerca, atentos a la fauna deformada y a la insidiosa propagación de la plaga demoníaca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the ecological aftermath of the Third War keep a wary eye on the river, monitoring how deeply Felwood's corruption penetrates downstream flora and fauna.",["race:NightElf"]="The polluted waters cascading from Felwood threaten the ancient roots of Darkshore, making the riverbanks a frequent concern for night elf wardens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The river originates high in the mountains of Felwood, where it is known as the Bloodvenom River. Felwood was thoroughly saturated with demonic magic during the Third War, and that foul runoff spills down the cliffs into Darkshore as the Wildbend River.",["al"]={"why is water tainted","wildbend river poison","darkshore dirty water"},["q"]="Why is the Wildbend River corrupted?"},{["a"]="Cascading down from the eastern ridges that separate Felwood from Darkshore, the river winds through southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients before flowing into the Veiled Sea.",["al"]={"where is wildbend river","wildbend path","wildbend river location"},["q"]="Where does the river flow?"},{["a"]="The river passes close to the Grove of the Ancients, posing a constant environmental threat to the ancient protectors rooted there. The night elves work tirelessly to contain the blight and prevent the poisoned water from rotting the sacred groves.",["al"]={"grove of the ancients water","is grove of ancients corrupted"},["q"]="Does the river affect the Grove of the Ancients?"}},["kw"]={"bloodvenom river","darkshore","felwood","grove of the ancients","tainted water","wildbend river"},["n"]="Wildbend River",["s"]="Wildbend River is a tainted waterway winding through the southern forests of Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients. Flowing down directly from the corrupted heights of Felwood, its waters carry demonic poison toward the sea, endangering the surrounding wilderness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Wildbend River cuts through the southern reaches of Darkshore, flowing westward past the sacred Grove of the Ancients before emptying into the sea. Rather than offering clean nourishment to the woodland, it brings corruption down from the mountains. The river is the direct continuation of Felwood's Bloodvenom River, tumbling through the rocky ridges and dragging foul, corrupted runoff into Darkshore's ecosystem. The night elves monitor its banks closely, watching for twisted wildlife and the creeping spread of demonic blight.",["t"]="A Toxic Mountain Stream"}}}}}
t["subzone:wildmane-water-well"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,292,23.543.0,41.184.0,40.191.0,46.157.0",["h"]="7a9eb0",["n"]="Pozo Ferocrín",["s"]="Pozo Ferocrín. El Pozo Ferocrín es el más septentrional de los pozos de agua sagrados dispersos por Mulgore, situado justo al norte de los riscos de Cima del Trueno. Vital para las llanuras y sus manadas, se ha convertido en un punto conflictivo codiciado por oportunistas goblins que buscan asfixiar la savia vital de los tauren. Durante generaciones, los tauren nómadas han dependido de los sagrados pozos de agua excavados a lo largo de Las Llanuras Doradas de Mulgore para sustentar a su pueblo y a sus manadas errantes de kodos. El Pozo Ferocrín protege la extensión norte, justo más allá de la sombra de Cima del Trueno. Su importancia vital lo convierte en un objetivo irresistible para los enemigos de las tribus. Los goblins de Ventura y Cía. lo han contaminado con sus venenos en un intento de controlar el suministro de agua regional, y solo un ritual de purificación con un tótem creado por los tauren puede volver a purificar sus aguas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The goblins' attempts to corrupt Mulgore's fresh water threaten the delicate balance of the plains, demanding druidic vigilance to cleanse and heal the land.",["race:Tauren"]="The sacred wells of Mulgore are a gift from the Earth Mother. Defending the Wildmane Well from defilement and poison is a sacred duty for every young brave."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Wildmane Water Well is situated on the plains of Mulgore, directly north of the towering mesas of Thunder Bluff. It is the northernmost of the sacred wells that sustain the region.",["al"]={"wildmane well location","where is wildmane well","wildmane water well map"},["q"]="Where is the Wildmane Water Well located?"},{["a"]="Fresh water is life on the plains. The tauren hold the land's wells sacred as vital lifelines for their settlements, traveling hunters, and the great kodo herds roaming the plains of Mulgore.",["al"]={"why do tauren care about the well","wildmane well sacred"},["q"]="Why is the well important to the tauren?"},{["a"]="The goblins of the Venture Company have poisoned the well in an effort to control Mulgore's water supply, and the tauren must cleanse it with a sacred totem.",["al"]={"who attacked the well","wildmane well enemies","who poisoned wildmane well"},["q"]="Who has tried to sabotage or control the well?"}},["kw"]={"mulgore","sacred well","thunder bluff","venture company","water well","wildmane"},["n"]="Wildmane Water Well",["s"]="The Wildmane Water Well is the northernmost of the sacred water wells scattered across Mulgore, resting just north of the mesas of Thunder Bluff. Vital to the plains and their herds, it has become a contested flashpoint targeted by goblin opportunists seeking to choke the tauren's lifeblood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For generations, the nomadic tauren have relied on sacred water wells dug across the golden plains of Mulgore to sustain their people and their wandering kodo herds. The Wildmane Well guards the northern expanse just beyond the shadow of Thunder Bluff. Its vital importance makes it an irresistible target for enemies of the tribes. The goblins of the Venture Company have fouled it with their poisons in a bid to control the regional water supply, and only a cleansing ritual with a totem crafted by the tauren can make its waters pure again.",["t"]="A Lifeblood Under Siege"}}}}}
t["subzone:windfury-ridge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,245,16.644.0,36.267.0,53.250.0,32.131.0",["h"]="f97aa9",["n"]="Cresta Viento Furioso",["s"]="Cresta Viento Furioso. Cresta Viento Furioso es una escarpada zona de tierras altas que flanquea los pastos de Mulgore. Conocida por albergar a feroces arpías junto a lobos y pumas depredadores, supone un peligro constante para los viajeros, al tiempo que ofrece preciadas plumas a los artesanos tauren. Cresta Viento Furioso se alza abruptamente sobre las serenas llanuras de Mulgore, sirviendo como coto de caza para las arpías Viento Furioso. Estas feroces criaturas aladas anidan en lo alto de los riscos y se lanzan en picado sobre cualquier caminante incauto que bordee las colinas. El terreno rocoso está poblado además por lobos de las praderas al acecho y pumas de montaña salvajes, lo que convierte la cresta en una de las fronteras más traicioneras del corazón de las tierras tauren. A pesar del peligro, los valientes guerreros tauren cazan con frecuencia a las arpías; su plumaje vibrante e iridiscente es muy cotizado en toda Cima del Trueno para adornar ropajes ceremoniales en banquetes fastuosos y celebraciones de bodas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The steep inclines and cunning predators provide an excellent early testing ground for tracking, beast taming, and range management.",["race:Tauren"]="The ridge is both a recurring nuisance to young hunters and a source of vital ceremonial ornaments used to honor marriages and seasonal gatherings."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The ridge is teeming with predatory cougars and prairie wolves, but its most persistent menace is the flock of aggressive harpies nesting along the heights. They actively dive from the crags to capture or butcher intruders who wander too close to their nesting sites.",["al"]={"why is windfury ridge dangerous","hazards of windfury ridge","windfury ridge monsters"},["q"]="What makes Windfury Ridge dangerous?"},{["a"]="Beyond securing the borders from their predations, tauren hunt the Windfury harpies for their brilliant feathers. These colorful plumes are traditionally harvested and woven into ceremonial headdresses and decorations used during feasts and weddings.",["al"]={"why kill windfury harpies","harpy feathers mulgore","hunting harpies"},["q"]="Why do the tauren hunt the harpies on Windfury Ridge?"},{["a"]="Windfury Ridge lies along the elevated bluffs in the pastoral region of Mulgore, in the far north of Mulgore, beyond Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"windfury ridge location","where is windfury ridge","windfury ridge map"},["q"]="Where is Windfury Ridge located?"}},["kw"]={"cougars","feathers","harpies","mulgore","thunder bluff","windfury","windfury ridge"},["n"]="Windfury Ridge",["s"]="Windfury Ridge is a rugged highland area flanking the pastures of Mulgore. Notorious for harboring vicious harpies alongside predatory wolves and cougars, it poses a constant hazard to travelers while offering prized feathers to tauren artisans.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Windfury Ridge rises sharply above Mulgore's serene plains, serving as the hunting grounds of the Windfury harpies. These vicious winged creatures nest high along the crags, readily swooping down upon any unwary wanderers who skirt the hills. The rocky terrain is further populated by prowling prairie wolves and wild mountain cougars, making the ridge one of the more treacherous borders of the tauren heartland. Despite the danger, the harpies are frequently hunted by brave tauren warriors; their vibrant, iridescent plumage is highly sought after across Thunder Bluff to adorn ceremonial garments for lavish feasts and wedding celebrations.",["t"]="A Perilous Perch"}}}}}
t["subzone:windshear-crag"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,403,22.687.0,25.571.0,42.252.0,30.259.0,54.272.0,42.194.0,45.204.0",["h"]="97343b",["n"]="Risco Cortaviento",["s"]="Risco Cortaviento. Risco Cortaviento es un valle profundamente expoliado en el centro de Sierra Espolón, despojado de su madera ancestral por Ventura y Cía. Antaño un frondoso bosque, la región es ahora un páramo industrial dominado por el zumbido de trituradoras, escorrentías turbias y agresivas cuadrillas de leñadores. A la sombra de la maquinaria, los kóbolds locales escarban en busca de mineral mientras los pasos de montaña conectan este paisaje marcado por las cicatrices con Vallefresno. No hace mucho tiempo, Risco Cortaviento era un espeso bosque primario que flanqueaba las laderas de Sierra Espolón. Esa naturaleza tranquila desapareció cuando Ventura y Cía. llegó en busca de beneficios. Hoy en día, la cuenca está repleta de tocones cortados, humo acre y maquinaria ruidosa. Toda la empresa maderera está supervisada por Gerenzo Silbillave, un gnomo paria cuyo ingenio para la ingeniería produjo la Súper Leñadora 6000: un terror mecánico capaz de reducir troncos enormes a astillas en cuestión de instantes. Desde una plataforma elevada sobre el contaminado Lago del Peñasco, Gerenzo dirige una operación desenfrenada que deja la montaña al desnudo, granjeándose la hostilidad tanto de ingenieros rivales como de los habitantes locales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers heading toward Ashenvale encounter Braug Dimspirit near the Talondeep Path, where he tests their knowledge of Kalimdor's history.",["profession:Engineering"]="The industrial equipment throughout the crag showcases cutthroat goblin trade secrets and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's lethal Super Reaper designs."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The logging venture is commanded on-site by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a brilliant but contaminated leper gnome engineer. Operating under contract with the Venture Company, he watches over the crag from a timber platform raised directly over Cragpool Lake.",["al"]={"who leads venture co here","who is the boss of windshear","gerenzo wrenchwhistle lore"},["q"]="Who is running the logging operation here?"},{["a"]="The Super Reaper 6000 is an advanced mechanical logging prototype engineered by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle. Designed to clear timber at unprecedented speeds, it can grind ancient mountain trees into sawdust within moments, accelerating the company's clear-cutting.",["al"]={"super reaper 6000","what is the big shredder","venture co reaper"},["q"]="What is the Super Reaper 6000?"},{["a"]="Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union in Undermine wants Gerenzo dead, and the goblin Ziz Fizziks, who already helped steal the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints, puts out the order. The trade princes of Undermine disapprove of the Venture Company consorting with the gnome.",["al"]={"why kill gerenzo","ziz fizziks motives","tinkers union vendetta"},["q"]="Why is the Undermine Tinkers' Union targeting Gerenzo?"},{["a"]="The cave in the northeast corner is the Talondeep Path. It cuts through the subterranean roots of the mountains, providing a foot route between Windshear Crag and the dense forests of Ashenvale.",["al"]={"talondeep path destination","windshear cave exit","tunnel in windshear crag"},["q"]="Where does the cave in the northeast lead?"},{["a"]="The Windshear kobolds have overrun the local mine in the southeastern corner of the crag. They vigorously defend their subterranean claim, excavating deposits of Smoky Iron Ingots used by regional smiths.",["al"]={"windshear mine kobolds","why are kobolds here","smoky iron ingots"},["q"]="Who are the kobolds digging in the southeast?"}},["kw"]={"braug dimspirit","cragpool lake","gerenzo wrenchwhistle","super reaper 6000","talondeep path","venture company","windshear crag","windshear mine","ziz fizziks"},["n"]="Windshear Crag",["s"]="Windshear Crag is a heavily despoiled valley in the central Stonetalon Mountains, stripped of its ancient timber by the Venture Company. Once a lush forest, the region is now an industrial wasteland dominated by whirring shredders, murky runoff, and aggressive logging crews. In the shadows of the machinery, local kobolds burrow for ore while mountain passes connect the scarred landscape to Ashenvale.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Not long ago, Windshear Crag was a thick, old-growth woodland flanking the slopes of Stonetalon. That tranquil wilderness vanished when the Venture Company arrived in search of profit. Today, the basin is filled with severed stumps, acrid smog, and clanking machinery. The entire logging enterprise is overseen by Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a leper gnome whose engineering genius produced the Super Reaper 6000—a mechanical terror capable of reducing massive trunks to kindling in moments. From an elevated platform above the polluted Cragpool Lake, Gerenzo directs an unchecked operation that strips the mountain bare, earning the hostility of rival engineers and local inhabitants alike.",["t"]="Industrial Devastation"},{["b"]="Beyond the active timberyards, Windshear Crag holds other hazards and crossroads. To the southeast lies Windshear Mine, where territorial kobolds dig through the rock for Smoky Iron Ingots, fiercely attacking anyone who nears their haul. In the crag's northeast reaches, travelers can find the Talondeep Path, an underground cavern tunnel threading straight beneath the ridges into Ashenvale. Stationed near this shadowed portal stands the tauren elder Braug Dimspirit, who tests the historical wisdom and resolve of Horde wayfarers venturing through the contested peaks.",["t"]="Mines and Mountain Passes"}}}}}
t["subzone:winterhoof-water-well"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,315,21.547.0,24.439.1,43.111.0,39.188.0,38.178.0,44.226.0",["h"]="b89c08",["n"]="Pozo Pezuña Invernal",["s"]="Pozo Pezuña Invernal. El Pozo Pezuña Invernal es una fuente vital de agua dulce situada al borde de Las Llanuras Onduladas, en el sur de Mulgore. Crucial para la fauna local y las tribus tauren nómadas, el pozo se ha visto amenazado recientemente por la explotadora Ventura y Cía., que busca envenenar y controlar el suministro de agua de la región. En las áridas extensiones del centro de Kalimdor, el agua es vida, y los pozos subterráneos de Mulgore sustentan tanto a las manadas de las llanuras como a los campamentos de los tauren. El Pozo Pezuña Invernal, bautizado en honor a una de las respetadas tribus de las llanuras, se abastece de los profundos acuíferos que yacen bajo Las Llanuras Onduladas. Desgraciadamente, su importancia estratégica ha atraído la codicia de Ventura y Cía. En lugar de compartir la tierra o negociar, el despiadado cártel de goblins ha intentado envenenar el suministro de agua para ejercer presión sobre el territorio circundante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Cleansing the well requires elemental harmony, serving as a practical demonstration of using totems to heal wounded water spirits.",["race:Tauren"]="Defending and purifying the ancestral water wells is one of the first trials young braves face to safeguard the land from outside exploitation."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The well is located in southern Mulgore, right on the fringes of the Rolling Plains south of Bloodhoof Village.",["al"]={"winterhoof well location","where is winterhoof well","find winterhoof water well"},["q"]="Where is the Winterhoof Water Well located?"},{["a"]="The Venture Company poisoned the well. The unscrupulous goblin trading organization attempted to foul the water supply in a bid to control the local resources and weaken the native tauren.",["al"]={"who poisoned winterhoof well","why is the well poisoned","who ruined the water"},["q"]="Who poisoned the Winterhoof Water Well?"},{["a"]="The well is cleansed through a ritual utilizing an enchanted totem crafted by Mull Thunderhorn, which uses primal magic to purge the Venture Company's foul toxins from the water.",["al"]={"cleanse winterhoof well","fix the well","winterhoof cleansing"},["q"]="How can the poisoned well be cleansed?"},{["a"]="Beyond providing necessary hydration for tribes and roaming herds, water sources in Mulgore are viewed as gifts from the Earth Mother. Corrupting them is considered both a direct physical threat and a severe spiritual affront.",["al"]={"why do tauren care about wells","tauren well lore"},["q"]="Why are water wells so sacred to the tauren?"}},["kw"]={"cleansing","mulgore","mull thunderhorn","rolling plains","totem","venture company","water well","winterhoof"},["n"]="Winterhoof Water Well",["s"]="The Winterhoof Water Well is a vital fresh water source situated on the edge of the Rolling Plains in southern Mulgore. Crucial to the local wildlife and nomadic tauren tribes, the well has recently fallen under threat from the exploitative Venture Company, who seek to poison and control the region's water supply.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In the arid stretches of central Kalimdor, water is life, and Mulgore's subterranean wells sustain both the herds of the plains and the encampments of the tauren. The Winterhoof Water Well, named for one of the respected tribes of the plains, taps into the deep aquifers beneath the Rolling Plains. Unfortunately, its strategic importance has drawn the avarice of the Venture Company. Rather than sharing the land or negotiating, the ruthless goblin cartel has attempted to poison the water supply to exert leverage over the surrounding territory.",["t"]="A Threatened Lifeline"},{["b"]="To counter the industrial sabotage of the Venture Company, tauren elders and shamans have mobilized young braves across Mulgore. Mull Thunderhorn has crafted sacred totems designed to counter the industrial toxins and restore the spiritual and physical balance of the well. Cleansing the well is not merely an act of survival for the tauren, but a spiritual duty to ensure that the earth and its waters remain uncorrupted by foreign greed.",["t"]="Purification and Defense"}}}}}
t["subzone:xavian"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,267,16.643.0,19.565.1,31.293.0,31.277.0,43.264.0,51.247.0",["h"]="2aabf6",["n"]="Xavian",["s"]="Xavian. Xavian es un antiguo complejo de templos de elfos de la noche en ruinas en el noreste de Vallefresno, ahora invadido y reclamado por los sátiros. Al servir como la sede principal de la influencia de los sátiros en el bosque, la ruina está corrompida por la corrupción demoníaca y oscuros ritos dirigidos contra la arboleda. Escondido en las colinas del noreste de Vallefresno, al oeste de Canción del Bosque y al norte de Satyrnaar, Xavian se erige como el principal bastión del poder de los sátiros en la región. Antaño un templo élfico sagrado, sus arcos de piedra y terrazas han sido profanados por seguidores de la Legión Ardiente. Líderes entre los sátiros, incluidos Prince Raze y Geltharis, supervisan a los suyos desde estas ruinas. Llevan a cabo rituales profanadores por todo el lugar, utilizando incluso aceite Grito de Guerra robado para marchitar aún más el bosque sagrado. La zona recibe su nombre de Xavius, el consejero bien nacido que se convirtió en el primer sátiro durante la Guerra de los Ancestros tras fallarle a Sargeras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The satyrs here have stolen the Branch of Cenarius and use fel rites to corrupt the land; druids are called upon to reclaim the artifact and heal the grove's spiritual wounds.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the desecrated halls of an ancient temple defiled by the twisted descendants of the Highborne is a bitter offense to any night elf, demanding swift retribution."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The stronghold is named in honor of Lord Xavius, the highborne courtier of Queen Azshara who helped usher the Burning Legion into Azeroth during the War of the Ancients. After displeasing Sargeras, Xavius was remade into the very first satyr, a demonic curse that spread to others of his kind.",["al"]={"origin of xavian","who is xavian named after","xavius xavian"},["q"]="Why is this place named Xavian?"},{["a"]="The satyrs use Xavian as their primary command center in Ashenvale. They conduct dark rituals to spread demonic corruption throughout the ancient forest, utilizing defiled sacred relics like the stolen Branch of Cenarius as well as machinery oil pilfered from the Warsong orcs.",["al"]={"what are they doing in xavian","xavian satyr rituals"},["q"]="What are the satyrs doing here?"},{["a"]="Her name is Anilia. She was part of a dryad effort to recover the stolen Branch of Cenarius from the satyrs. She was mortally wounded during the skirmish and lies among the ruins, pleading for someone to reclaim the sacred branch before it is completely corrupted.",["al"]={"injured dryad xavian","who is anilia","dryad in xavian"},["q"]="Who is the dying dryad lying on the ground?"},{["a"]="While Satyrnaar and Night Run are notable satyr camps within Ashenvale, Xavian acts as the political and ritual heart of their forces in the forest. High-ranking satyr leaders such as Geltharis and Prince Raze make their base here among the ruins.",["al"]={"satyrnaar vs xavian","other satyr camps","why is xavian important"},["q"]="How does Xavian differ from Satyrnaar or Night Run?"}},["kw"]={"anilia","ashenvale","branch of cenarius","geltharis","raze","satyr","xavian","xavius"},["n"]="Xavian",["s"]="Xavian is an ancient ruined night elf temple complex in northeastern Ashenvale, now overrun and claimed by the satyrs. Serving as the primary seat of satyr influence in the forest, the ruin is foul with demonic corruption and dark rites directed against the woodland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the northeastern hills of Ashenvale, west of Forest Song and north of Satyrnaar, Xavian stands as the foremost bastion of satyr power in the region. Once a sacred elven temple, its stone arches and terraces have been desecrated by followers of the Burning Legion. Leaders among the satyrs, including Prince Raze and Geltharis, oversee their kin from these ruins. They perform defiling rituals across the grounds, even utilizing stolen Warsong oil to further blight the sacred woodland. The area takes its name from Xavius, the highborne councilor who became the first satyr during the War of the Ancients after failing Sargeras.",["t"]="A Seat of Shadow"},{["b"]="The corruption radiating from Xavian has not gone unchallenged, but confronting the satyrs comes at a grim price. Sentinels and woodland guardians keep a watchful eye on the stronghold, knowing its strategic malice eclipses nearby enclaves like Night Run. Recently, dryad defenders attempted to infiltrate the ruins to recover the sacred Branch of Cenarius, only to suffer grievous losses. Adventurers who breach the outer terraces can find the dying dryad Anilia, struck down while attempting to halt the defilers from using holy relics in their dark incantations.",["t"]="The Fallen Vanguard"}}}}}
t["subzone:yorgen-farmstead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,252,18.482.0,19.423.0,30.205.0,31.192.0,25.172.0,42.229.0",["h"]="ed045e",["n"]="La Hacienda Yorgen",["s"]="La Hacienda Yorgen. La Hacienda Yorgen es una granja abandonada ubicada en el sur de Bosque del Ocaso, caída en la ruina junto con el resto de la turbulenta región. Antaño propiedad del granjero Sven Yorgen, la finca ha sido tomada y ocupada por bandoleros de la Hermandad Defias. Situada en medio de los lúgubres bosques del sur de Bosque del Ocaso, La Hacienda Yorgen fue en su día un próspero hogar perteneciente a Sven Yorgen. Como muchos asentamientos aislados de la región, la granja no pudo resistir los crecientes peligros del territorio. Sven se vio obligado a abandonar sus tierras y se retiró al norte a un campamento improvisado a lo largo de La Ribera Lóbrega. En su ausencia, los terrenos desiertos fueron reclamados por forajidos que buscaban un punto de apoyo lejos de la mirada de las autoridades de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The hidden Defias assassins stalking the farmstead make the area treacherous, demonstrating how readily rogue operatives turn neglected wilderness holdings into camouflaged hideouts.",["faction:Alliance"]="The loss of Sven's farmstead to the Defias Brotherhood highlights how deeply the outlaw syndicates have penetrated Duskwood while the Night Watch struggles to maintain order in Darkshire."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farmstead was originally established and farmed by Sven Yorgen. After tragedy struck his home and driven away by rising dangers, Sven fled to a solitary camp located further north on the Darkened Bank.",["al"]={"who lived here","who owns yorgen farm","sven yorgen farm"},["q"]="Who owns the Yorgen Farmstead?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood has seized the deserted property. Cutpurses, bandits, and stealthed assassins prowl the overgrown yards and barnyards, making the farmstead extremely dangerous to visit.",["al"]={"who is at yorgen farmstead","what enemies are here","who lives here now"},["q"]="Who occupies the farmstead now?"},{["a"]="Sven abandoned the farm and can now be found residing in a modest camp along the Darkened Bank, situated to the north along the river separating Duskwood and Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","find sven yorgen"},["q"]="Where did Sven Yorgen go?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood has expanded its operations far beyond Westfall. Disorganized rural settlements and weakened regional defenses allow their agents to set up secret camps and strongholds out of reach of Stormwind's marshals.",["al"]={"defias in duskwood","why are bandits here","defias brotherhood farm"},["q"]="Why is the Defias Brotherhood in Duskwood?"}},["kw"]={"darkened bank","defias","defias brotherhood","duskwood","farm","sven yorgen","yorgen farmstead"},["n"]="Yorgen Farmstead",["s"]="The Yorgen Farmstead is a derelict farm nestled in southern Duskwood, fallen into ruin alongside the rest of the troubled region. Formerly owned by the farmer Sven Yorgen, the property has been seized and occupied by brigands of the Defias Brotherhood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated amidst the gloomy woodlands of southern Duskwood, the Yorgen Farmstead was once a functioning homestead belonging to Sven Yorgen. Like many isolated holdings in the region, the farm could not withstand the encroaching perils of the territory. Sven was forced to abandon his lands, retreating north to a makeshift camp along the Darkened Bank. In his absence, the abandoned grounds were claimed by outlaws looking for a foothold far from the gaze of Stormwind's authorities.",["t"]="A Ruined Homestead"},{["b"]="Rather than lying vacant, the farmstead has been repurposed as a staging ground by the Defias Brotherhood. Masked highwaymen and stealthy cutthroats lurk among the decaying fences and weathered outbuildings, using the dense tree cover to conceal their presence. Travelers approaching the farmstead must tread carefully, as Defias assassins patrol the perimeter and ambush anyone trespassing on their newly seized sanctuary.",["t"]="Defias Infiltration"}}}}}
t["subzone:zoram-gar-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,302,23.568.0,20.255.0,46.229.0,35.235.0,49.185.0,63.250.0",["h"]="13f191",["n"]="Avanzada de Zoram'gar",["s"]="Avanzada de Zoram'gar. La Avanzada de Zoram'gar es una cabeza de playa fortificada de la Horda situada en el extremo occidental de Vallefresno, a lo largo de La Ensenada de Zoram. Al servir como un campamento costero crucial, proporciona a la Horda acceso al Mar Velado y vigila las amenazas regionales, como los naga invasores y las siniestras profundidades cercanas. Situada en el extremo noroccidental de Vallefresno, donde el bosque primigenio se desploma hacia el mar, la Avanzada de Zoram'gar sirve como la aislada posición costera de la Horda en La Ensenada de Zoram. Cercado por el territorio de los elfos de la noche tierra adentro y por los peligros marítimos mar adentro, el campamento actúa como punto de partida para exploradores, cazadores y chamanes encargados de rastrear los peligros locales. La vida en la avanzada es una vigilia constante: los naga merodean con frecuencia por las aguas poco profundas, mientras que cultores al acecho y horrores primigenios palpitan desde el sistema de cavernas subterráneas conocido como Cavernas de Brazanegra, a poca distancia por la orilla.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="An entrenched Horde presence on the coast of Ashenvale, Zoram'gar represents a dangerous supply foothold close to night elf ancestral lands.",["faction:Horde"]="The outpost serves as your primary haven in northwest Ashenvale, offering shelter, rest, and wind rider transport amidst dangerous wilderness."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Horde established the camp to secure a foothold on the western shoreline of Ashenvale. It provides maritime monitoring along the Zoram Strand and offers a defensible station to counter the aggressive naga infesting the coast.",["al"]={"why is zoram'gar here","purpose of zoram gar","why did horde build zoram gar"},["q"]="Why did the Horde establish Zoram'gar Outpost?"},{["a"]="The immediate threat comes from the Wrathtail naga slithering across the Zoram Strand. Additionally, the twilight cultists and beastly horrors residing within the nearby temple ruins of Blackfathom Deeps pose a constant lurking danger.",["al"]={"threats to zoram gar","enemies at zoram gar"},["q"]="What threats does the outpost face?"},{["a"]="Zoram'gar Outpost connects aerial wind riders across central Kalimdor, linking travelers to Splintertree Post, Sun Rock Retreat, the Crossroads, and the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"flight paths zoram gar","where can i fly from zoram gar"},["q"]="Where does the outpost connect via flight master?"},{["a"]="Blackfathom Deeps lies just north of the outpost along the shoreline ruins. Horde forces stationed at Zoram'gar monitor the corruption seeping out of the flooded temple and dispatch adventurers inside to counter the cultists and their beast, Aku'mai.",["al"]={"blackfathom deeps near zoram","is bfd near zoram gar"},["q"]="What is the relation between the outpost and Blackfathom Deeps?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","horde","naga","outpost","zoram gar","zoram strand","zoram'gar"},["n"]="Zoram'gar Outpost",["s"]="Zoram'gar Outpost is a fortified Horde beachhead nestled on the western edge of Ashenvale along the Zoram Strand. Serving as a crucial coastal encampment, it provides the Horde with access to the Veiled Sea and keeps watch over regional threats like the encroaching naga and the sinister depths nearby.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated at the northwestern lip of Ashenvale where the primeval forest collapses into the sea, Zoram'gar Outpost serves as the Horde's isolated coastal footing on the Zoram Strand. Hemmed in by night elf territory inland and maritime hazards offshore, the encampment acts as a staging ground for scouts, hunters, and shaman tasked with tracking local dangers. Life at the outpost is an endless vigil: naga regularly prowl the shallows, while lurking cultists and primal horrors pulse from the subterranean cavern system known as Blackfathom Deeps just down the shore.",["t"]="A Bastion on the Strand"},{["b"]="Because of its peripheral location, Zoram'gar maintains flight connections with other critical Horde holdings like Splintertree Post, the Crossroads, and Thunder Bluff. While small in footprint, the outpost anchors Horde supply lines on the western coast.",["t"]="Strategic Importance"}}}}}
t["subzone:zoram-strand"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,345,27.453.0,21.453.0,39.239.0,36.269.0,43.202.0,49.251.0",["h"]="ea30ab",["n"]="La Ensanada de Zoram",["s"]="La Ensanada de Zoram. La Ensenada de Zoram es una costa azotada por el viento que bordea el extremo noroccidental de Vallefresno a lo largo del Mar Velado. En su día fue el emplazamiento de una antigua ciudad de los elfos de la noche engullida por el Gran Cataclismo; ahora, la costa está plagada de nagas Colafuria, naufragios y leviatanes varados. También alberga la entrada al complejo del templo sumergido de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Hace diez mil años, la grandiosa ciudad de los elfos de la noche de Zoram adornaba estas costas antes de que el Gran Cataclismo desgarrara Kalimdor y arrojara el asentamiento a las profundidades del océano. Hoy en día, la marea arrastra continuamente reliquias antiguas, restos de embarcaciones destrozadas y los cadáveres de enormes bestias marinas. Los nagas Colafuria han invadido las playas y las pozas de marea, custodiando con ferocidad las ruinas inundadas y los artefactos antiguos frente a cualquiera que ose acercarse.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Defending the approaches to Zoram'gar Outpost is vital to maintaining a northern naval and coastal presence in Ashenvale against the relentless Wrathtail brood.",["race:NightElf"]="The strand is a sobering reminder of the ancient world lost to the Sundering, where sacred relics and submerged temples to Elune now suffer beneath the tread of the naga."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Prior to the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, Zoram was a majestic night elven city. The cataclysm shattered the coast, plunging the city beneath the Veiled Sea and leaving only jagged ruins and washed-up statuettes along the shore.",["al"]={"zoram history","ancient zoram","what was zoram"},["q"]="What was Zoram before it was destroyed?"},{["a"]="The shoreline itself is largely overrun by the Wrathtail naga, who fiercely defend the shallows and ancient ruins. The Horde maintains a fortified foothold at Zoram'gar Outpost along the southern cliffs, while dangerous wildlife such as hydras and crabs prowl the sand.",["al"]={"who lives at zoram strand","zoram strand enemies","who controls zoram strand"},["q"]="Who controls the Zoram Strand today?"},{["a"]="The entrance to Blackfathom Deeps is located in the submerged caverns along the Zoram Strand. Travelers venture into the coastal caves along the water's edge to reach the descent into the sunken temple.",["al"]={"blackfathom deeps location","how to find bfd","bfd entrance zoram"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to Blackfathom Deeps?"},{["a"]="The tumultuous tides and dark currents of the Veiled Sea frequently wash massive marine creatures ashore. Researchers and naturalists from both factions often seek out these remains to investigate what drives ocean behemoths to perish along the rocks.",["al"]={"beached sea creature quest","dead whales zoram strand","beached creatures"},["q"]="Why are there so many beached sea creatures here?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","naga","ruuzel","veiled sea","wrathtail","zoram","zoram strand"},["n"]="Zoram Strand",["s"]="The Zoram Strand is a windswept coastline lining the northwestern edge of Ashenvale along the Veiled Sea. Once the site of an ancient night elven city swallowed by the Great Sundering, the shore is now plagued by Wrathtail naga, shipwrecks, and beached leviathans. It also holds the entrance to the submerged temple complex of Blackfathom Deeps.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ten thousand years ago, the grand night elven city of Zoram graced these shores before the Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart and cast the settlement into the ocean depths. Today, the tide continually washes up ancient relics, remnants of shattered vessels, and the carcasses of massive sea beasts. The Wrathtail naga have overrun the beaches and tidal pools, fiercely guarding the flooded ruins and ancient artifacts against anyone daring to approach.",["t"]="Ruins of the Sundered Coast"},{["b"]="Despite the naga menace, both mainland travelers and coastal wanderers find themselves drawn to the strand. To the south lies the fortified Horde encampment of Zoram'gar Outpost, whose warriors fight a continuous battle to secure the coast. Deep within the nearby caverns sits Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient temple of Elune that has fallen into dark hands, making the strand a gathering ground for scouts, scholars, and treasure seekers braving the surf.",["t"]="A Contested Shoreline"}}}}}
t["topic:skyborne"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="Los cielonatos, o shen'dorei («el pueblo oculto»), son altos elfos descendientes de antiguos elfos de la noche que se rebelaron contra el príncipe Tortheldrin en Eldre'Thalas. Para escapar de su flota vengativa, sellaron un pacto con espíritus del viento, quienes trasladaron su isla, la Isla de Zephras, al interior del Plano Elemental del Aire.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="a5c69e",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Milenios en el Plano Elemental del Aire han remodelado sutilmente su biología. Un fenómeno reciente conocido como la Bendición Tocada por el Cielo hace que una proporción creciente de niños (actualmente unos tres de cada diez) nazca con la piel azul. Los eruditos predicen que sus rasgos ancestrales de elfo de la noche pronto quedarán suplantados por completo.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="cc8652",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El Shal'nan, o «el Velado», fue el líder enmascarado que encabezó la resistencia contra la invocación demoníaca del príncipe Tortheldrin en Eldre'Thalas. Tras guiar a los supervivientes a un lugar seguro en Muro Celeste, abdicó para establecer un consejo democrático y sirvió a su pueblo hasta que desapareció misteriosamente hace siglos junto a sus benefactores elementales.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="8661cb",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La Isla de Zephras se sostiene en el aire dentro de Muro Celeste gracias a pilones mágicos sintonizados con el poder elemental. Cuando los espíritus del viento que los mantenían desaparecieron repentinamente hace siglos, los pilones de anclaje comenzaron a fallar. Ciertas partes de la masa de tierra se han quebrado hacia el vacío, dejando aislados a supervivientes y arrojando a elfos desplazados al bandidaje.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="ec7ba3",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Son las dos facciones culturales principales de los cielonatos. La Orden Eminente desciende de los magos altonato y busca reconstruir su decadente sociedad mediante un disciplinado dominio arcano. Los Formavientos tienen sus orígenes en los ciudadanos comunes entre los elfos de la noche y veneran las costumbres elementales y espirituales cultivadas durante su tiempo en Muro Celeste.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="d1711c",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Los Al'Aketh son una secta desesperada de cielonatos que adora a Al'Akir, el Señor del Viento. Aunque los benefactores elementales de sus antepasados temían y evitaban hablar de Al'Akir, el colapso de la Isla de Zephras llevó a refugiados desposeídos y sin hogar a acudir al señor elemental en busca de salvación y poder.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="131d49",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="8,417,24.687.0,20.628.0,17.716.1,21.300.0,36.317.0,21.348.0,34.318.0,44.342.0,21.290.0",["h"]="c74832",["n"]="Cielonatos",["s"]="Cielonatos. Los cielonatos, o shen'dorei, son una escisión de altos elfos descendientes de rebeldes que huyeron de Eldre'Thalas tras oponerse a los pactos demoníacos del príncipe Tortheldrin. Al forjar un trato desesperado con espíritus del viento, sus ancestros escaparon de Azeroth para morar sobre la flotante Isla de Zephras, en el interior de Muro Celeste. Hoy en día, con la repentina desaparición de sus benefactores elementales, su santuario flotante afronta fracturas internas y un colapso físico. Tras el Cataclismo, los Shen'dralar de Eldre'Thalas languidecieron sin el Pozo de la Eternidad. El príncipe Tortheldrin ideó una oscura salvación: invocar al demonio Immol'thar y drenar su poder. Nobles y ciudadanos horrorizados se resistieron, temiendo otra invasión de la Legión. En respuesta, Tortheldrin ejecutó una sangrienta purga de decenas de casas. De las sombras de los supervivientes surgió una resistencia encabezada por una figura enmascarada conocida solo como el Shal'nan («el Velado»). Cuando una incursión rebelde desesperada en el sagrario ritual de Tortheldrin degeneró en una catastrófica magia caótica, el Shal'nan reunió a los supervivientes y huyó hacia el oeste hasta el puerto de Eldre'narr, echándose a la mar perseguidos por la flota del Príncipe.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The High Order among the Skyborne preserves ancient Highborne spellcraft brought out of Eldre'Thalas, seeking to salvage their crumbling island through rigorous arcane mastery.",["class:Shaman"]="The Windshapers represent an elven lineage deeply intertwined with the wind spirits of Skywall, relying on elemental communion rather than the arcane traditions of their Highborne forebears.",["race:NightElf"]="The Skyborne share direct bloodlines with the ancient Shen'dralar and northern night elves, though millennia in Skywall have physically altered them into high elves with an increasing prevalence of elemental blue skin."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Skyborne, or shen'dorei ('the hidden people'), are high elves descended from ancient night elves who rebelled against Prince Tortheldrin in Eldre'Thalas. To escape his vengeful fleet, they struck a pact with wind spirits, who relocated their island, Zephras Isle, into the Elemental Plane of Air.",["al"]={"what are skyborne","who are shen'dorei","shendorei","skyborne lore"},["q"]="Who are the Skyborne?"},{["a"]="Millennia in the Elemental Plane of Air have subtly reshaped their biology. A recent phenomenon known as the Sky-Touched Blessing causes an increasing proportion of children—now roughly three out of ten—to be born with blue skin. Scholars predict their ancestral night elf traits will soon be entirely supplanted.",["al"]={"sky-touched blessing","why are they blue","blue elves","sky touched"},["q"]="Why do some Skyborne have blue skin?"},{["a"]="The Shal'nan, or 'the Veiled One', was the masked leader who spearheaded the resistance against Prince Tortheldrin's demon summoning in Eldre'Thalas. After leading the survivors to safety in Skywall, he abdicated to establish a democratic council, serving his people until mysteriously vanishing centuries ago alongside their elemental benefactors.",["al"]={"who is the veiled one","shalnan","the masked rebel","leader of skyborne"},["q"]="Who was the Shal'nan?"},{["a"]="Zephras Isle is held aloft within Skywall by magical pylons attuned to elemental power. When the wind spirits who maintained them abruptly disappeared centuries ago, the anchoring pylons began to fail. Portions of the landmass have broken off into the void, stranding survivors and driving displaced elves to banditry.",["al"]={"why is zephras isle crumbling","zephras falling","what happened to skywall island"},["q"]="What is happening to Zephras Isle?"},{["a"]="They are the two primary cultural factions of the Skyborne. The High Order descends from Highborne magisters and seeks to rebuild their crumbling society through disciplined arcane mastery. The Windshapers trace their roots to ordinary night elf citizens and revere the elemental and spiritual customs cultivated during their time in Skywall.",["al"]={"skyborne factions","high order vs windshapers","windshaper lore"},["q"]="What are the High Order and the Windshapers?"},{["a"]="The Al'Aketh are a desperate cult of Skyborne who worship Al'Akir the Windlord. While their ancestors' elemental benefactors feared and avoided speaking of Al'Akir, the collapse of Zephras Isle led homeless and disenfranchised refugees to turn to the elemental lord for salvation and power.",["al"]={"alaketh cult","cult of al'akir","skyborne cult"},["q"]="Who are the Al'Aketh?"}},["kw"]={"al'aketh","eldre'thalas","high order","shal'nan","shen'dorei","sky-touched","skyborne","skywall","windshapers","zephras isle"},["n"]="Skyborne",["s"]="The Skyborne, or shen'dorei, are an offshoot of high elves descended from rebels who fled Eldre'Thalas after opposing Prince Tortheldrin's demonic pacts. Striking a desperate bargain with wind spirits, their ancestors escaped Azeroth to dwell atop the floating Zephras Isle within Skywall. Today, with their elemental benefactors abruptly gone, their floating sanctuary faces internal fractures and physical collapse.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the Sundering, the Shen'dralar of Eldre'Thalas languished without the Well of Eternity. Prince Tortheldrin devised a dark salvation: summon the demon Immol'thar and siphon its power. Horrified nobles and citizens resisted, fearing another Legion invasion. In response, Tortheldrin executed a bloody purge of dozens of houses. From the surviving shadows rose a resistance spearheaded by a masked figure known only as the Shal'nan ('the Veiled One'). When a desperate rebel raid on Tortheldrin's ritual sanctum descended into catastrophic chaotic magic, the Shal'nan rallied the survivors and fled west to the port of Eldre'narr, taking to the seas pursued by the Prince's fleet.",["t"]="Flight from Eldre'Thalas"},{["b"]="Cornered on the open ocean, the exiles forged a pact with primordial wind spirits. These beings lifted Zephras Isle straight into the skies, anchoring it safely within Skywall—the Elemental Plane of Air. Relieved of absolute rule, the Shal'nan stepped down during the consecration of the Shrine of the Four Winds, placing governance in the hands of an elected council. Over millennia in this alien realm, the night elf exiles evolved into fair, slender high elves. In recent generations, an elemental influence known as the Sky-Touched Blessing has emerged, causing a growing number of children to be born with pale blue skin.",["t"]="Sanctuary in the Sky"},{["b"]="For centuries, life in Skywall flourished in isolation. The wind spirits strictly forbade mention of the Windlord, Al'Akir, brushing off questions with eerie unease. A few centuries ago, catastrophe struck: the elemental benefactors vanished without explanation, and the Shal'nan disappeared along with them. Deprived of their caretakers, the arcane pylons anchoring Zephras Isle began failing. Outlying landmasses broke away, refugees flooded what remained, and desperation fueled the rise of bandits and the Al'Aketh—a fanatical cult dedicated to Al'Akir. Today, society fractures between the High Order, who seek salvation in reclaiming ancestral arcane magic, and the Windshapers, who cling to elemental rites.",["t"]="A Shattering Calm"}}}}}
t["zone:arathi"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,328,18.594.0,19.625.0,25.593.1,33.371.0,19.278.0,42.251.0,45.213.0,38.274.0,38.271.1",["h"]="f6e831",["n"]="Tierras Altas de Arathi",["s"]="Tierras Altas de Arathi. Las Tierras Altas de Arathi son una meseta escarpada en el sureste de Lordaeron, célebre por ser la antigua cuna del Imperio de Arathor. Hoy en día, el reino de Stromgarde yace en ruinas, lo que deja a este territorio rocoso sumido en una guerra abierta en múltiples frentes entre los restos de Stromgarde, la Horda, los nobles criminales de la Hermandad y los ogros invasores. Hace milenios, el rey Thoradin unió a las fracturadas tribus humanas bajo el estandarte de los Arathi y construyó la majestuosa capital de Strom a lo largo de estas llanuras áridas y fáciles de defender. Fue aquí donde la humanidad forjó su legendario pacto con los altos elfos durante las Guerras Trol, dominando las artes arcanas para hacer retroceder a los Amani. Con el tiempo, los linajes nobles emigraron al norte hacia Lordaeron y al sur hacia Ventormenta, pero la guardia imperial se quedó atrás para fundar el reino marcial de Stromgarde. Durante eras, Stromgarde se alzó como un bastión de firmes guerreros consagrados a mantener a raya a los trols del bosque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Stromgarde produced the most celebrated frontline martial tradition on Azeroth, making its rugged battlegrounds a revered trial by arms.",["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall stands as sacred ground to the modern Horde—a monument to Orgrim Doomhammer's sacrifice that freed an enslaved people from internment.",["profession:Mining"]="The craggy ridges of Arathi are rich in iron and mithril, and Drywhisker Gorge is the only known source of lesser bloodstone ore.",["race:Human"]="Every human kingdom traces its roots to the Empire of Arathor; seeing the seat of human civilization broken and overrun by ogres and thieves is a profound cultural tragedy."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Following King Thoras Trollbane's death, Stromgarde succumbed to internal strife and overwhelming assaults. Boulderfist ogres seized the city's exterior districts while the opportunistic Syndicate seized the sanctum, leaving Prince Galen Trollbane and his dwindling garrison clinging to a single fortified corner while fighting desperate battles inside their own capital.",["al"]={"why is stromgarde ruined","who controls stromgarde","stromgarde status"},["q"]="What happened to Stromgarde Keep?"},{["a"]="Hammerfall is a fortified Horde outpost built within the remnants of a human internment camp where orcs were held after the Second War. It was named to honor former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell leading the campaign to liberate the captives held across Lordaeron's camps.",["al"]={"horde base arathi","history of hammerfall","why is it called hammerfall"},["q"]="What is Hammerfall?"},{["a"]="Alliance soldiers and Stromgarde defenders stage their operations out of Refuge Pointe, a naturally fortified canyon in the center of the highlands. From here, they launch sorties to reclaim Stromgarde Keep and fight back encroaching ogres and trolls.",["al"]={"alliance base arathi","refuge pointe","where are the stromgarde humans"},["q"]="Where does the Alliance operate in Arathi?"},{["a"]="The Circles of Binding—Inner, Outer, East, and West—are ancient magical seals maintained and guarded by rogue elementals. They serve to imprison an unknown, primordial entity buried deep beneath the highlands.",["al"]={"circles of binding","elementals in arathi","stone circles"},["q"]="What are the stone circles across the plains?"},{["a"]="Travelers from the north and west pass through the breach in Thoradin's Wall from the Hillsbrad Foothills. Travelers arriving from Khaz Modan in the south cross the massive dwarven bridge of the Thandol Span, which spans the chasm separating the highlands from the Wetlands.",["al"]={"getting to arathi","how to get to arathi highlands","arathi entrance"},["q"]="How do you reach the Arathi Highlands?"},{["a"]="The Syndicate consists of exiled Alteraci nobility seeking to carve out new domains by pillaging fallen realms. In Arathi, they have overrun large sections of Stromgarde Keep and outlying farms like Northfold Manor, secretly guided by the dark cultists of the Argus Wake.",["al"]={"why is syndicate in arathi","syndicate stromgarde","who leads the syndicate here"},["q"]="What is the Syndicate doing in Arathi?"}},["kw"]={"arathi","arathi highlands","arathor","boulderfist","galen trollbane","hammerfall","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","thoradin's wall"},["n"]="Arathi Highlands",["s"]="The Arathi Highlands are a rugged plateau in southeastern Lordaeron, renowned as the ancient birthplace of the Empire of Arathor. Today, the kingdom of Stromgarde lies in ruins, leaving the craggy realm engulfed in multi-front warfare between the remnants of Stromgarde, the Horde, criminal Syndicate nobles, and invading ogres.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Millennia ago, King Thoradin united the fractured human tribes under the banner of the Arathi, constructing the majestic capital of Strom across these dry, defensible plains. It was here that humanity forged its legendary compact with the high elves during the Troll Wars, mastering the arcane arts to push back the Amani. Over time, noble bloodlines migrated north into Lordaeron and south toward Stormwind, but the imperial guard stayed behind to form the martial realm of Stromgarde. For ages, Stromgarde stood as a bastion of stalwart warriors dedicated to keeping the forest trolls at bay.",["t"]="Cradle of Humanity"},{["b"]="Stromgarde proved vital in defending the Alliance during the Second War under King Thoras Trollbane, but the Third War and its aftermath shattered the nation. Although the kingdom spared itself the worst ravages of the Scourge plague, the mysterious death of King Thoras threw the realm into turmoil. Boulderfist ogres swept in from the hills, while the traitorous Alteraci nobles of the Syndicate seized sprawling districts of Stromgarde Keep. Today, Prince Galen Trollbane and his loyalist survivors cling to a tiny sliver of the city and their redoubt at Refuge Pointe, waging a bitter guerrilla war against hopeless odds.",["t"]="A Shattered Kingdom"},{["b"]="Arathi is a fiercely contested crossroads. In the northeast, the Horde converted an abandoned human internment camp into Hammerfall, named in honor of the legendary Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, using it as an anchor to secure their northern holdings and safeguard allies in Hillsbrad. Meanwhile, the Witherbark troll tribe seeks vengeance against their ancient human persecutors, and the Argus Wake pulls strings behind the Syndicate's occupation. At the center of the plateau lie ancient Circles of Binding, where bound elementals restrain an enigmatic, ancient power buried beneath the stone.",["t"]="The War for the Highlands"}}}}}
t["zone:azshara"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,468,16.604.0,33.497.0,30.492.0,42.223.0,30.253.0,24.285.0,22.248.0,43.213.0,49.212.0",["h"]="c3e886",["n"]="Azshara",["s"]="Azshara. Azshara es una costa escarpada y azotada por el viento en el noreste de Kalimdor, cubierta por un vibrante y perpetuo follaje otoñal. Antaño parte de la gloriosa capital de los elfos de la noche antes de que el Gran Cataclismo la arrojara al mar, sigue siendo un territorio salvaje y peligroso sembrado de ruinas antiguas, nagas taciturnos y practicantes de la magia aislados. Tanto la Horda como la Alianza mantienen precarios puestos de avanzada a lo largo de sus fronteras, cautelosos ante los fantasmas inquietos y los horrores oceánicos que acechan en su interior. Hace diez mil años, esta costa era el corazón palpitante de la civilización kaldorei, rodeando la capital real de Zin-Azshari. Cuando la reina Azshara y su corte de Altonato atrajeron a la Legión Ardiente a Azeroth, la consiguiente Guerra de los Ancestros culminó en el catastrófico colapso del Pozo de la Eternidad. El mar se precipitó tierra adentro con gran estruendo, devorando la mayor parte de la magnífica ciudad y dejando a su paso acantilados fracturados, traicioneros arrecifes de coral y agujas anegadas. Los supervivientes rebautizaron el paisaje en ruinas con el nombre de su monarca caída, marcándolo como un monumento maldito al orgullo y a la traición catastrófica.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The shattered stones of Eldarath still crackle with forgotten Highborne sorcery, and high above the cliffs, the reclusive Archmage Xylem tests those seeking mastery of arcane teleportation and spellcraft.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Azshara's perpetual autumn climate sustains rare and potent herbs, including Dreamfoil, Golden Sansam, Mountain Silversage, and Purple Lotus among the ruins.",["profession:Mining"]="The steep coastal cliffs and jagged ridges of Azshara are rich in precious mineral veins, containing abundant deposits of Mithril, Truesilver, and Thorium.",["race:NightElf"]="Every drowned pillar and wailing Highborne shade in Azshara serves as a grim, haunting testament to Queen Azshara's reckless arrogance and the cataclysmic ruin of the ancient kaldorei civilization."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Azshara is cloaked in a perpetual autumn. The vibrant orange, gold, and red canopy never sheds its leaves, giving the coastal woods a strikingly beautiful yet melancholy atmosphere that has persisted for thousands of years.",["al"]={"why is azshara autumn","why are trees red","azshara fall foliage"},["q"]="Why are all the trees red and orange here?"},{["a"]="This coastline once formed the outskirts of the kaldorei capital, Zin-Azshari. During the War of the Ancients, the Well of Eternity imploded during the Great Sundering, sundering the continent and sending vast portions of the city tumbling into the sea.",["al"]={"what happened to azshara","why is azshara broken","azshara history"},["q"]="How did Azshara become a ruin?"},{["a"]="No single faction holds dominion over the territory. The Alliance maintains a small watch at Talrendis Point near Ashenvale, while the Horde operates out of the encampment of Valormok. The surrounding land is dominated by dangerous Spitelash naga, violent satyrs, and untamed monsters.",["al"]={"who controls azshara","who runs azshara","is azshara alliance or horde"},["q"]="Who rules Azshara today?"},{["a"]="Archmage Xylem is an eccentric human sorcerer residing in a remote cliffside tower overlooking Azshara. Unaligned with regional politics, he aids visiting mages and rogues in unlocking unique martial and arcane potential through challenging trials.",["al"]={"xylem azshara","mage tower azshara","wizard in azshara"},["q"]="Who is Archmage Xylem?"},{["a"]="The great blue dragon Azuregos and his brood watch over the ancient ruins of Eldarath. He fiercely protects the powerful Highborne magical artifacts still buried in the rubble from being plundered by mortal hands.",["al"]={"azuregos in azshara","blue dragon azshara","dragon in eldarath"},["q"]="What is the blue dragon doing in the ruins?"},{["a"]="The kaldorei consider Azshara cursed because it bears the name and architectural legacy of their treacherous Queen Azshara, whose pact with the Burning Legion shattered their empire and brought ruin to the world.",["al"]={"is azshara cursed","why do night elves hate azshara","night elf curse azshara"},["q"]="Why do the night elves consider this land cursed?"}},["kw"]={"azshara","azuregos","bay of storms","coral sea","eldarath","highborne","spitelash","talrendis point","valormok","xylem"},["n"]="Azshara",["s"]="Azshara is a rugged, windswept coastline in northeastern Kalimdor cloaked in vibrant, perpetual autumn foliage. Once part of the glorious night elven capital before the Great Sundering shattered it into the sea, it remains a dangerous wilderness littered with ancient ruins, brooding naga, and isolated practitioners of magic. Both the Horde and the Alliance maintain precarious outposts along its borders, wary of the restless ghosts and ocean horrors lurking within.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ten thousand years ago, this coast was the beating heart of the kaldorei civilization, surrounding the royal capital of Zin-Azshari. When Queen Azshara and her Highborne court drew the Burning Legion into Azeroth, the resulting War of the Ancients culminated in the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity. The sea thundered inward, swallowing most of the magnificent city and leaving behind fractured cliffs, treacherous coral reefs, and waterlogged spires. The survivors renamed the ruined landscape after their fallen monarch, branding it as a cursed monument to pride and catastrophic betrayal.",["t"]="A Drowned Empire"},{["b"]="Azshara is famous for its stunning crimson, orange, and gold canopy, giving the impression of an eternal autumn unbroken by changing seasons. Beneath this tranquil canopy, however, lies an inhospitable expanse. Corrupted satyrs practice dark rituals in forested hollows, lingering Highborne apparitions haunt drowned foundations, and Spitelash naga prowl the shallow reefs of the Coral Sea. Ferocious beasts, giant hydras, and mountain giants roam unchecked across the highlands and ivory beaches.",["t"]="Autumn Splendor and Hidden Perils"},{["b"]="Because of its isolation and harsh terrain, Azshara draws recluse figures pursuing forgotten crafts or watching over dangerous powers. The enigmatic Archmage Xylem inhabits a secluded tower perched high above the cliffs, testing promising spellcasters and cunning rogues alike. Farther along the coast, the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes watches the waves from a barren isle, while the immense sea giant Lord Arkkoroc demands blood sacrifices from his temple overlooking the churning waters.",["t"]="A Realm of Exiles and Outcasts"}}}}}
t["zone:badlands"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,424,16.453.0,22.466.0,34.449.0,43.300.0,31.273.0,16.301.0,51.257.0,28.244.0,61.268.0",["h"]="4e198f",["n"]="Tierras Inhóspitas",["s"]="Tierras Inhóspitas. Tierras Inhóspitas es una extensión árida y castigada por el sol, repleta de tierra agrietada, tormentas de polvo y cañones rocosos, enclavada entre Loch Modan y La Garganta de Fuego. A pesar de encontrarse en las profundidades del Khaz Modan enano, sirve como una frontera inestable dominada por enanos Hierro Negro, troggs, ogros Rotapolvo y dracónidos negros anidando. También alberga las ruinas titánicas de Uldaman y el bastión de la Horda de Kargath, lo que la convierte en un punto de paso estratégico crucial. Situada al sur de las verdes colinas de Loch Modan, Tierras Inhóspitas se transforma rápidamente en una cuenca sofocante de llanuras yermas y barrancos escarpados. Sobrevivir aquí exige enfrentarse a coyotes despiadados, pumas, buitres y feroces tormentas de arena que oscurecen el horizonte. Dispersos por las mesetas se encuentran los toscos campamentos de los ogros Rotapolvo, mientras que el sombrío clan Hierro Negro fortifica la Fortaleza de Angor y choca con cualquiera que traspase su territorio.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Kargath serves as your sole military sanctuary deep in Khaz Modan, acting as the frontline against the Dark Horde occupying Blackrock Mountain.",["profession:Mining"]="The arid landscape is rich in iron, gold, truesilver, and mithril, including rare Indurium deposits found within Uldaman and the surrounding terrain.",["race:Dwarf"]="The Badlands holds the answers to your very ancestry within Uldaman, where the discovery of the titan-forged earthen reshaped dwarven understanding of history."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The outpost of Kargath was established by the Kargath Expeditionary Force on orders from Warchief Thrall. Stationed under Warlord Goretooth, the encampment provides the Horde a vital staging ground to strike against Rend Blackhand and his renegade Blackrock clan entrenched within Blackrock Mountain.",["al"]={"why kargath","horde in badlands","what is kargath"},["q"]="Why is the Horde stationed in the Badlands?"},{["a"]="Alliance travelers can walk directly south from Loch Modan through the Maker's Terrace pass. Horde travelers face a longer trek on foot through the southern hills of Loch Modan or through Searing Gorge via the western mountain pass before unlocking Kargath's flight master.",["al"]={"getting to badlands","how to reach badlands","badlands entrance"},["q"]="How do you get to the Badlands?"},{["a"]="Uldaman is a massive underground vault built by the ancient titans and their earthen servants. Though recently excavated by dwarven prospectors seeking the secrets of dwarven origins, the dig awoke buried earthen constructs and primitive Stonevault troggs, turning the ruin into a lethal battleground.",["al"]={"what's uldaman","uldaman dungeon lore","who made uldaman"},["q"]="What is Uldaman?"},{["a"]="Lethlor Ravine serves as an eastern breeding and nesting canyon for the black dragonflight. Guarded by drakes and whelps, the clutch maintains a dangerous presence near the mountains, preying upon wanderers and guarding the eastern reaches from trespassers.",["al"]={"dragons in badlands","lethlor ravine dragons","black dragonflight badlands"},["q"]="What are the black dragons doing in Lethlor Ravine?"},{["a"]="Angor Fortress is held by the hostile Dark Iron clan. Situated south of Uldaman, the fortress serves as a regional base where the Dark Irons conduct reconnaissance, contest the titan digsites, and battle neighboring ogres and surface explorers.",["al"]={"angor fortress","badlands fortress","dark irons badlands"},["q"]="Who controls Angor Fortress?"},{["a"]="No. The Badlands has no fortified Alliance settlements or flight masters. Ironforge prospectors and solitary hermits maintain scattered, fragile camps near the digsites, but Alliance adventurers must rely on bases in Loch Modan or Searing Gorge for extensive supplies.",["al"]={"alliance town badlands","alliance flight path badlands","friendly alliance badlands"},["q"]="Are there any friendly settlements for Alliance players here?"}},["kw"]={"angor fortress","badlands","dustbelcher","earthen","goretooth","kargath","lethlor","troggs","uldaman"},["n"]="Badlands",["s"]="The Badlands is an arid, sun-baked expanse of cracked earth, dust storms, and rocky canyons nestled between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge. Despite being deep within dwarven Khaz Modan, it serves as a volatile frontier dominated by Dark Iron dwarves, troggs, Dustbelcher ogres, and nesting black dragonkin. It also houses the titan ruins of Uldaman and the Horde stronghold of Kargath, making it a critical strategic waypoint.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Wedged south of Loch Modan's verdant hills, the Badlands quickly turns into a sweltering basin of barren flats and rugged ravines. Surviving here requires contending with merciless coyotes, cougars, vultures, and fierce sandstorms that obscure the horizon. Scattered across the plateaus are the crude encampments of the Dustbelcher ogres, while the brooding Dark Iron clan fortifies Angor Fortress and clashes with anyone trespassing on their territory.",["t"]="A Bleak Frontier"},{["b"]="In the northern bluffs lies Uldaman, an ancient subterranean complex carved out by the titan-forged earthen. Recently uncovered by Ironforge prospectors, the excavation unearthed monumental secrets regarding the ancient ancestry of the dwarven race. However, digging into the subterranean vaults awoke hordes of vicious Stonevault troggs and animated earthen guardians, slaughtering archaeological teams and turning the digsites outside into bloody skirmish grounds.",["t"]="The Secrets of Uldaman"},{["b"]="The Badlands is one of the Horde's most precarious footholds in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Established in the northwest, the fortress of Kargath gives Warchief Thrall's forces a base of operations to keep watch on the rogue Dark Horde in nearby Blackrock Mountain. Meanwhile, to the far east lies Lethlor Ravine, a treacherous chasm where black whelps and dangerous black dragonkin guard their brooding grounds under the shadow of the mountains.",["t"]="The Shadows of Kargath and Lethlor"}}}}}
t["zone:barrens"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,432,22.521.0,18.482.0,22.482.1,51.341.0,28.293.0,40.311.0,41.300.0,29.271.0,48.290.0",["h"]="7ed882",["n"]="Los Baldíos",["s"]="Los Baldíos. Los Baldíos son una vasta sabana abrasada por el sol que sirve como el palpitante corazón geográfico y logístico de la Horda en el centro de Kalimdor. Antaño un frondoso bosque antes del Gran Cataclismo, hoy son una llanura árida de polvo rojo, matorrales resistentes y fauna errante. Centrada en torno al enclave estratégico de El Cruce, esta tierra permanece sumida en una lucha constante contra las tribus de jabaespines, los asaltantes centauros y una corrupción insidiosa. Durante incontables generaciones, los tauren nómadas cazaron kodos y cebras a lo largo de estas llanuras mientras libraban una guerra cíclica y defensiva contra los merodeadores centauros Kolkar. Cuando Thrall guio a los orcos a Kalimdor durante la Tercera Guerra, ayudó a Cairne Pezuña de Sangre a repeler a los centauros y a cruzar la sabana hasta Mulgore. En la actualidad, Los Baldíos conectan Durotar, Mulgore y Vallefresno. Puestos avanzados como El Cruce y Campamento Taurajo aseguran el comercio a lo largo del Camino del Oro, mientras que los asentamientos orcos desafían el clima árido para forjar un hogar duradero.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The twisted waters flowing from the Wailing Caverns represent a profound tragedy, where Naralex's noble attempt to restore the Barrens succumbed to the nightmare.",["class:Shaman"]="The arid plains test your connection to the elements, from the dry earth spirits of the plains to the enchanted, altered waters that bubble up in isolated oases.",["faction:Horde"]="The Barrens is the logistical backbone of your realm; securing the Crossroads and defending supply convoys across the Gold Road ensures the survival of Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",["race:Tauren"]="Before the orcs landed on Kalimdor, your nomadic ancestors wandered these savannas for generations, hunting sacred game and fighting for survival against the ruthless Kolkar centaur."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The sudden pools—such as the Forgotten Pools and Lushwater Oasis—are fed by underground springs flowing out of the Wailing Caverns. The night elf druid Naralex tapped into the Emerald Dream to channel spring waters and regreen the arid land, but the venture went awry, saturating the northern Barrens with potent, volatile natural magic.",["al"]={"barrens oases","why is there water in barrens","wailing caverns water"},["q"]="Why are there lush oases in the middle of a desert?"},{["a"]="The Crossroads is garrisoned by the Horde, primarily orc and tauren warriors serving Warchief Thrall. Because it sits at the intersection of the primary trade routes linking Durotar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale, it serves as the Horde's chief strategic military and transit hub in central Kalimdor.",["al"]={"who runs crossroads","crossroads horde","crossroads guards"},["q"]="Who controls the Crossroads?"},{["a"]="The quilboar consider the Barrens their ancestral birthright, believing the colossal brambles sprouted from the blood of their demigod, Agamaggan, during the War of the Ancients. They view both the arriving Horde and the native tauren as trespassers stealing their sacred foraging grounds and hunting territory.",["al"]={"quilboar lore","why quilboar aggressive","razormane motive"},["q"]="Why are the quilboar attacking everyone?"},{["a"]="The Alliance maintains a presence along the edges of the savanna. Northwatch Hold is garrisoned by human troops from Theramore keeping watch over Horde movements, while the dwarves of Bael Modan and Bael'dun Keep are deeply invested in excavating ancient titan artifacts buried in the southern hills.",["al"]={"northwatch hold alliance","bael modan dwarves","alliance in barrens"},["q"]="Why are Alliance soldiers in the Barrens?"},{["a"]="No. Ratchet is an independent goblin port run by Gazlowe. It maintains strict neutrality, acting as a gateway for maritime trade, smugglers, and adventurers of both the Horde and the Alliance, provided everyone respects goblin commerce and keeps weapons sheathed in town.",["al"]={"is ratchet horde","ratchet faction","gazlowe ratchet"},["q"]="Is Ratchet part of the Horde?"},{["a"]="Insectoid creatures called silithid have emerged from earthen hives in the southern Barrens, particularly around the Field of Giants. Their sudden appearance and rapid colony growth pose an escalating threat to travelers and local outposts, prompting the Horde to investigate their origins.",["al"]={"barrens bugs","field of giants bugs","silithid south barrens"},["q"]="What is going on with the silithid in the south?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","gold road","kolkar","naralex","quilboar","ratchet","taurajo","wailing caverns"},["n"]="The Barrens",["s"]="The Barrens is an expansive, sun-baked savanna that serves as the beating geographical and logistical heart of the Horde in central Kalimdor. Once a verdant forest prior to the Great Sundering, it is now an arid plain of red dust, hardy scrub, and wandering wildlife. Centered around the strategic hub of the Crossroads, the land remains locked in constant struggle against quilboar tribes, centaur raiders, and creeping corruption.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For countless generations, nomadic tauren hunted kodo and zhevra across these plains while waging a defensive, cyclical war against marauding Kolkar centaur. When Thrall led the orcs to Kalimdor during the Third War, he aided Cairne Bloodhoof in repelling the centaur and traversing the savanna into Mulgore. Today, the Barrens connects Durotar, Mulgore, and Ashenvale. Outposts like the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo secure trade along the Gold Road, while orcish homesteads brave the arid climate to forge a lasting home.",["t"]="Heart of the New Horde"},{["b"]="Despite Horde dominance, control over the savanna is hotly contested. Porcupine-like Razormane quilboar aggressively raid farms and supply lines from their thorn-choked redoubts, backed by the looming dens of Razorfen Kraul to the south. Along the eastern coast, Theramore forces garrison Northwatch Hold, while dwarven prospectors dig into the titan complex of Bael Modan. Meanwhile, the goblins of Ratchet enforce an uneasy mercantile neutrality, welcoming any traveler with coin.",["t"]="A Land Under Siege"},{["b"]="Several oases punctuate the northern plains, their waters unnaturally surging with life-giving vigor. This surge originates from the Wailing Caverns, where the night elf druid Naralex attempted to tap into the Emerald Dream to restore the Barrens to its ancient, forested glory. Instead, a nightmare twisted Naralex's vision. Corrupted water now seeps across the Forgotten Pools and Stagnant Oasis, spawning bizarre deviate flora, unnatural beasts, and the rogue Druids of the Fang.",["t"]="The Emerald Corruption"}}}}}
t["zone:burningsteppes"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,384,20.652.0,24.569.0,29.528.0,46.377.0,42.301.0,28.286.0,51.257.0,43.243.0,33.265.0",["h"]="78dcc4",["n"]="Las Estepas Ardientes",["s"]="Las Estepas Ardientes. Las Estepas Ardientes son un páramo volcánico y calcinado que flanquea la base sur de la Montaña Roca Negra. Formado por la catastrófica invocación de Ragnaros hace siglos, este traicionero territorio alberga el principal paso terrestre entre Ventormenta y Khaz Modan. En la actualidad, está plagado de orcos Roca Negra rebeldes, ogros Pirontraña, enanos Hierro Negro y crías del Vuelo Negro. Hace mucho tiempo, estas colinas no eran más que la extensión norte de las Montañas Crestagrana. Durante la Guerra de los Tres Martillos, el clan Hierro Negro exiliado estableció aquí su reino y erigió su capital, Thaurissan. Al verse al borde de la derrota absoluta a manos de los clanes Barbabronce y Martillo Salvaje, el desesperado Thane hechicero Thaurissan intentó conjurar fuerzas elementales. En su lugar, resquebrajó la tierra e invocó a Ragnaros el Señor del Fuego en Azeroth. La violenta explosión pulverizó las montañas circundantes, abrió ríos de lava e hizo brotar el colosal volcán conocido como la Montaña Roca Negra, dejando las estepas carbonizadas y yermas para siempre.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Burning Steppes are a somber, dangerous frontier where Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar fell; Marshal Maxwell at Morgan's Vigil continually seeks brave champions to counter the threats encroaching toward Redridge.",["faction:Horde"]="Thrall's New Horde watches Flame Crest with deep concern, determined to curb the dangerous, unrepentant Blackrock clan whose warmongering stains the honor of orckind.",["profession:Mining"]="The volcanic landscape is rich in rare minerals, making it one of the select open-air regions on Azeroth to harvest valuable Dark Iron deposits alongside veins of rich thorium.",["race:Dwarf"]="Every stone in the steppes bears witness to the Dark Iron clan's folly during the War of the Three Hammers, culminating in the shattering of their capital and the summoning of Ragnaros."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Centuries ago, the Dark Iron Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan attempted to summon an elemental minion to rescue his clan from defeat in the War of the Three Hammers. His spell mistakenly breached the Elemental Plane and summoned Ragnaros the Firelord, ripping open the earth, creating the massive Blackrock volcano, and reducing the northern Redridge Mountains to a charred wasteland.",["al"]={"why is it burning","what happened to burning steppes","why is blackrock mountain a volcano"},["q"]="Why is the ground charred and covered in lava?"},{["a"]="No. The orcs in the Burning Steppes are remnants of the Blackrock clan who refuse to join Thrall's New Horde. They do not honor the armistice with the Alliance and remain dedicated to the savage, warmongering traditions of the First and Second Wars, serving Blackrock Spire and the black dragonflight.",["al"]={"are these thralls orcs","are blackrock orcs horde","why are orcs hostile here"},["q"]="Do the orcs here belong to Thrall's Horde?"},{["a"]="Anduin Lothar was slain by Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer at the foot of Blackrock Mountain in the Burning Steppes near the end of the Second War. Lothar's demise spurred his second-in-command, Turalyon, and the Alliance forces into a furious counterattack that shattered the Horde's lines.",["al"]={"where was lothar killed","lothar death location","orgrim doomhammer and lothar duel"},["q"]="Where did Anduin Lothar die?"},{["a"]="Alliance soldiers and travelers base themselves at Morgan's Vigil, an elevated outpost in the southeastern foothills of the zone. Marshal Maxwell commands the station, watching over the northern pass and monitoring enemy troop movements around the mountain.",["al"]={"alliance base burning steppes","where is alliance flight path","morgans vigil location"},["q"]="Where can the Alliance find shelter in the steppes?"},{["a"]="Horde adventurers report to Flame Crest, an elevated camp located along the northeastern ridge. From here, emissaries watch the rival Blackrock clan and maintain flight connections back to the Badlands, the Swamp of Sorrows, and Searing Gorge.",["al"]={"horde base burning steppes","flame crest","where is horde town"},["q"]="Where does the Horde stage operations here?"},{["a"]="The Ruins of Thaurissan are the remnants of the grand city built by the Dark Iron clan after their exile from Ironforge. When Thane Thaurissan summoned Ragnaros, the raw elemental blast destroyed his capital and enslaved his surviving people to the Firelord's will.",["al"]={"thaurissan ruins","what is the destroyed dwarf city","ruins in middle of map"},["q"]="What are the Ruins of Thaurissan?"}},["kw"]={"anduin lothar","blackrock clan","blackrock mountain","blackrock spire","burning steppes","doomhammer","flame crest","morgan's vigil","ragnaros","thaurissan"},["n"]="Burning Steppes",["s"]="The Burning Steppes are a scorched, volcanic wasteland flanking the southern base of Blackrock Mountain. Formed by the catastrophic summoning of Ragnaros centuries ago, this treacherous territory holds the primary overland passage between Stormwind and Khaz Modan. Today, it crawls with rogue Blackrock orcs, Firegut ogres, Dark Iron dwarves, and broodlings of the black dragonflight.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long ago, these foothills were simply the northern reaches of the Redridge Mountains. During the War of the Three Hammers, the exiled Dark Iron clan established their kingdom here, raising their capital city of Thaurissan. Facing total defeat at the hands of the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans, the desperate Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan attempted to conjure elemental forces. Instead, he shattered the earth and summoned Ragnaros the Firelord into Azeroth. The violent explosion pulverized the surrounding mountains, tore open rivers of lava, and birthed the colossal volcano known as Blackrock Mountain, leaving the steppes forever charred and barren.",["t"]="A Cataclysmic Origin"},{["b"]="During the Second War, the Old Horde claimed Blackrock Spire as its foremost seat of power. At the climax of the conflict, the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron pushed deep into the Burning Steppes to lay siege to the mountain. It was at the foot of Blackrock Mountain that Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer clashed with Lord Anduin Lothar, striking down the human champion. Rather than breaking the Alliance's resolve, Lothar's death galvanized the Allied armies to rout the orcs, sealing the victory of the Second War and leaving behind an enduring valley of ash and rusted steel.",["t"]="Echoes of the Second War"},{["b"]="Though Thrall established a New Horde in distant Kalimdor, the Blackrock clan remaining in the steppes maintains the bloodthirsty cruelty of the Old Horde. Operating from Blackrock Stronghold, these orcs openly ally with the black dragonflight and local Firegut ogres rather than honor any truce. Meanwhile, Dark Iron dwarves and elemental servitors lurk among the fiery ruins, all while black drakes and wyrmkin prey upon unwary travelers attempting to use the thoroughfare to cross between Stormwind and the northern kingdoms.",["t"]="A Den of Monsters and Dragons"}}}}}
t["zone:darkshore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,443,25.491.0,22.499.0,37.549.0,26.293.0,51.298.0,44.329.1,28.273.0,51.244.0,36.208.0",["h"]="747a95",["n"]="Costa Oscura",["s"]="Costa Oscura. Costa Oscura es una fría franja costera envuelta en niebla que bordea el noroeste de Kalimdor, salpicada de antiguas ruinas kaldorei y fauna perturbada. Con el pueblo portuario de Auberdine de la Alianza como eje central, sirve como la principal puerta de entrada continental para los viajeros que llegan desde Teldrassil y los Reinos del Este. Más allá del camino patrullado, los cultos demoníacos, los invasores naga y una corrupción que repta desde las tierras altas amenazan el delicado equilibrio de la región. Extendiéndose bajo las sombras occidentales del Monte Hyjal y Frondavil, Costa Oscura se caracteriza por sus pinares, niebla marina y playas rocosas azotadas por olas frías. Hace milenios, esta costa albergó las prósperas ciudades gemelas kaldorei de Ameth'Aran y Bashal'Aran. Destrozadas durante el Gran Cataclismo, sus pilares esqueléticos y arcos de mármol yacen ahora medio sumergidos en el oleaje o cubiertos de raíces, atormentados por inquietos espíritus Altonato e invadidos por múrlocs carroñeros y voraces naga.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Darkshore serves as the front line for Cenarion Circle initiates answering summons from Moonglade to diagnose tainted waterways and brew cleansers for sick forest creatures.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine represents the Alliance's primary trade nexus in northern Kalimdor, maintaining the direct maritime link connecting Stormwind and Ironforge to the night elf capital of Darnassus.",["faction:Horde"]="A remote, heavily patrolled Alliance bastion, Darkshore sits directly north of Horde encampments in Ashenvale, offering a treacherous coastline prowled by hostile sentinels and dangerous cults.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil, Darkshore is their first step onto mainland Kalimdor, confronting the painful ruins of their ancient civilization and the spreading corruption of the wild."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Alliance players can take a boat directly to Auberdine from either Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil or from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Horde travelers journeying north must walk through Ashenvale, following the main road northeast from Zoram'gar Outpost up across the border.",["al"]={"getting to darkshore","how to reach auberdine","darkshore boat"},["q"]="How do I get to Darkshore?"},{["a"]="Rivers running out of the tainted heights of Felwood, such as the Cliffspring River, wash demonic pollution straight down into Darkshore's water table. Drinking from these foul streams has driven the native furbolg tribes feral and infected the local deer and predators with disease and aggression.",["al"]={"why are animals sick","furbolg corruption","darkshore taint"},["q"]="What is wrong with the local wildlife and furbolgs?"},{["a"]="They were prosperous twin Kaldorei cities destroyed ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering. Their ruler, Athrikus Narassin, claimed he would rescue his people from the cataclysm, but he instead bound their souls into gems to preserve them as eternal power sources for himself, leaving the ruins full of weeping ghosts.",["al"]={"ameth'aran history","bashal'aran lore","ruins in darkshore"},["q"]="What happened to Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran?"},{["a"]="Located in southern Darkshore, the Master's Glaive is a massive petrified skull impaled by an enormous stone weapon. It is an ancient relic associated with the primordial Old Gods and their servitors, and it currently attracts dangerous cultists from the Twilight's Hammer.",["al"]={"what is the masters glaive","giant skull darkshore","masters glaive monster"},["q"]="What is the Master's Glaive?"},{["a"]="That is Onu, a wise and venerable Ancient of Lore. Resting in his tranquil grove south of Auberdine, he ponders the disturbing encroachment of the Twilight's Hammer cult and assists travelers in investigating disturbances throughout the forest.",["al"]={"ancient of lore darkshore","who is onu","tree person darkshore"},["q"]="Who is the giant tree in the Grove of the Ancients?"},{["a"]="The tower is occupied by the Dark Strand, a vicious cult practicing dark sorcery and summoning demonic entities. Their cabal actively ambushes unwary travelers along the northern reaches of the coastal woods.",["al"]={"tower of althalaxx","darkshore tower cultists","althalaxx cult"},["q"]="Who lives in the Tower of Althalaxx?"}},["kw"]={"ameth'aran","auberdine","bashal'aran","blackwood den","cliffspring falls","darkshore","master's glaive","onu","tower of althalaxx"},["n"]="Darkshore",["s"]="Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei ruins and troubled wildlife. Anchored by the Alliance harbor town of Auberdine, it serves as the primary continental gateway for travelers arriving from Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms. Beyond the patrolled road, demonic cults, encroaching naga, and a creeping corruption from the highlands threaten the region's delicate balance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching beneath the western shadows of Mount Hyjal and Felwood, Darkshore is characterized by pine groves, sea fog, and rocky beaches beaten by cold waves. Millennia ago, this coast was home to the flourishing Kaldorei twin cities of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. Shattered during the Great Sundering, their skeletal pillars and marble arches now lie half-drowned in the surf or overgrown with roots, haunted by restless Highborne spirits and overrun by scavenger murlocs and invasive naga.",["t"]="A Land of Mist and Memory"},{["b"]="Following the Third War and the planting of Teldrassil, the night elves established Auberdine as a bustling maritime haven amidst the wilderness. Featuring wooden piers that welcome regular vessels from Rut'theran Village and Menethil Harbor in the distant Wetlands, Auberdine is the lifeline linking night elf territory to the rest of the Alliance. Sentinels diligently patrol the trade highway south toward Ashenvale, though their small garrison struggles to police the deep wilds beyond the path.",["t"]="The Haven of Auberdine"},{["b"]="Despite its shelter against the eastern mountains, Darkshore suffers from a slow, malignant rot. Corrupted run-off trickling down from Felwood poisons sources like Cliffspring Falls, fouling the water table and driving the local bears, stags, and furbolgs of Blackwood Den into violent madness. Worse still, sinister organizations have established footholds in the shadows: the Dark Strand and Twilight's Hammer cultists perform foul rituals at the Tower of Althalaxx and convene around the terrifying, ancient monument known as the Master's Glaive.",["t"]="Poisoned Waters and Whispering Depths"}}}}}
t["zone:darnassus"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="La suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos gobierna Darnassus y a los kaldorei desde el gran Templo de la Luna. El archidruida Fandral Corzocelada lidera a los druidas del Círculo Cenarion desde el Enclave Cenarion, actuando como la autoridad druídica de facto mientras Malfurión Tempestira continúa perdido en El Sueño Esmeralda.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="59ff2b",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Darnassus fue fundada poco después de la Tercera Guerra. Cuando los elfos de la noche sacrificaron su inmortalidad para derrotar a Archimonde en el Monte Hyjal, Fandral Corzocelada impulsó el crecimiento del nuevo Árbol del Mundo, Teldrassil, para recuperar su antiguo estado. Darnassus fue esculpida en sus ramas como su nuevo refugio.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="2e9df5",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Malfurión Tempestira está desaparecido, con su espíritu atrapado dentro del Sueño Esmeralda. En su ausencia, el archidruida Fandral Corzocelada gobierna a los druidas de Teldrassil, mientras que Tyrande Susurravientos busca continuamente una manera de despertar y recuperar a su amado compañero.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="a9aca7",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La ciudad está dividida en bancales especializados. El Bancal del Artesano alberga disciplinas de recolección y sastrería junto con una posada, mientras que el Bancal de los Mercaderes cuenta con puestos comerciales y la Casa de Subastas. Los instructores de herrería y marciales residen en el Bancal del Guerrero, y el banco de la ciudad se encuentra en la isla central de Los Jardines del Templo.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="9f1364",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Tras la devastación de la Tercera Guerra, los elfos de la noche se enfrentaron a la creciente presión de la Horda, en particular a las expediciones de tala orcas en Vallefresno. Al reconocer la necesidad de aliados frente a estas incursiones y otras amenazas emergentes por todo Kalimdor, Darnassus estableció lazos diplomáticos y se unió a la Gran Alianza.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="41cbdf",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="9,450,28.496.0,25.528.0,16.558.0,49.254.0,20.298.0,37.290.0,39.243.0,52.343.0,42.314.0",["h"]="b1ca99",["n"]="Darnassus",["s"]="Darnassus. Darnassus es la serena capital al aire libre de los elfos de la noche, erigida entre las ramas del recién plantado Árbol del Mundo, Teldrassil. Gobernada por la suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos junto a los druidas del Enclave Cenarion, sirve como un apacible santuario para un pueblo ancestral que se adapta a la mortalidad. Extendida por amplios bancales que rodean un lago cristalino, se alza como el corazón de la sociedad de los elfos de la noche y su puente hacia la Alianza. A diferencia de la densa mampostería de Ventormenta o los túneles de piedra tallada de Forjaz, Darnassus es amplia, tranquila y está íntimamente abierta a la naturaleza salvaje. En el dosel superior de Teldrassil, frente a la costa norte de Kalimdor, las elegantes estructuras de madera y los sinuosos senderos de la capital rodean un apacible lago central. Elegantes puentes conectan bancales dedicados a mercaderes, artesanos, centinelas y druidas, creando una atmósfera que equilibra el gobierno civil con una profunda reverencia por la naturaleza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Enclave serves as the nexus of druidic training in Teldrassil, overseen by the demanding and uncompromising Archdruid Fandral Staghelm.",["class:Priest"]="The grand Temple of the Moon is the holy center of the Sisters of Elune, presided over by High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind herself.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darnassus acts as the westernmost stronghold of the Alliance, providing critical naval and strategic shelter on the continent of Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="As the heart of your sovereign civilization, Darnassus is your sanctuary as you navigate the unprecedented trials of mortal existence."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Because Teldrassil is an island isolated off Kalimdor's northwest coast, travelers must reach Rut'theran Village at the foot of the tree by boat or flight. From the village docks, a glowing magical portal takes travelers directly up into the city boughs.",["al"]={"how to get to darnassus","travel to darnassus","darnassus entrance"},["q"]="How do you travel to Darnassus from the mainland?"},{["a"]="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind rules Darnassus and the kaldorei from the grand Temple of the Moon. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave, acting as the de facto druidic authority while Malfurion Stormrage remains lost in the Emerald Dream.",["al"]={"darnassus leader","who is in charge","ruler of darnassus"},["q"]="Who rules Darnassus?"},{["a"]="Darnassus was founded shortly after the Third War. When the night elves sacrificed their immortality to defeat Archimonde at Mount Hyjal, Fandral Staghelm pushed to grow the new World Tree, Teldrassil, to reclaim their former state. Darnassus was carved into the boughs as their new refuge.",["al"]={"why is darnassus new","when was darnassus built","darnassus history"},["q"]="Why was the city founded so recently?"},{["a"]="Malfurion Stormrage is missing, his spirit trapped within the Emerald Dream. In his absence, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm governs the druids of Teldrassil, while Tyrande Whisperwind continually seeks a way to awaken and recover her beloved mate.",["al"]={"where is malfurion","is malfurion in darnassus","malfurion location"},["q"]="Where is Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage?"},{["a"]="The city is divided into specialized terraces. The Craftsmen's Terrace hosts gathering and tailoring disciplines along with an inn, while the Tradesmen's Terrace houses trade stalls and the Auction House. Blacksmithing and martial trainers reside on the Warrior's Terrace, and the city bank rests upon the central island of the Temple Gardens.",["al"]={"darnassus professions","auction house darnassus","darnassus bank"},["q"]="Where are the profession trainers and shops located?"},{["a"]="After the devastation of the Third War, the night elves faced mounting pressure from the Horde, particularly orcish logging expeditions into Ashenvale. Recognizing the need for allies against these incursions and other rising threats across Kalimdor, Darnassus opened diplomatic ties and joined the Grand Alliance.",["al"]={"why are night elves alliance","night elf alliance ties","alliance darnassus"},["q"]="Why did the night elves join the Alliance?"}},["kw"]={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","fandral","night elf capital","rut'theran","staghelm","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande","whisperwind"},["n"]="Darnassus",["s"]="Darnassus is the serene, open-air capital city of the night elves, built amidst the branches of the newly planted World Tree, Teldrassil. Governed by High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind alongside the druids of the Cenarion Enclave, it serves as a tranquil sanctuary for an ancient people adapting to mortality. Sheltered across vast terraces surrounding a crystalline lake, it stands as the heart of night elf society and their bridge to the Alliance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Unlike the dense masonry of Stormwind or the carved stone tunnels of Ironforge, Darnassus is broad, quiet, and intimately open to the wilderness. Formed upon the upper canopy of Teldrassil off northern Kalimdor's coast, the capital's graceful wooden structures and winding pathways encircle a tranquil central lake. Elegant bridges connect terraces dedicated to tradesmen, craftsmen, sentinels, and druids, creating an atmosphere that balances civic governance with profound reverence for nature.",["t"]="A Crown High in the Branches"},{["b"]="Darnassus is remarkably young for a civilization thousands of years old. Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil at Mount Hyjal, the kaldorei suddenly faced the perils of aging and sickness. Seeking a renewal of their lost vitality, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and his followers planted Teldrassil in defiance of missing Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage's warnings. Darnassus was founded among its immense boughs as an asylum and monument to their survival, though shadows of malaise already whisper among its roots.",["t"]="Refuge of a Mortal People"},{["b"]="Though peaceful on its surface, Darnassus balances on a delicate political divide. From the towering colonnades of the Temple of the Moon, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind guides the spiritual life and military defense of her people through the vigilant Sentinels. Across the waterways in the Cenarion Enclave, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm commands the druids in Malfurion's continuing absence. While both leaders present a united front to their newfound Alliance partners, friction between the priestesses and the druidic circle lingers throughout the city.",["t"]="A Divided Hearth"}}}}}
t["zone:deadmines"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,480,25.717.0,26.666.0,27.519.1,47.241.0,42.224.0,22.296.0,37.235.0,65.255.0,63.314.0,57.189.0",["h"]="72134b",["n"]="Las Minas de la Muerte",["s"]="Las Minas de la Muerte. En las profundidades del polvoriento pueblo agrícola de Arroyo de la Luna se encuentran Las Minas de la Muerte, un enorme complejo subterráneo que antaño suministraba un tercio de las reservas de oro de Ventormenta. Abandonados durante la Primera Guerra y considerados embrujados durante mucho tiempo, estos laberínticos túneles han sido tomados en secreto por la Hermandad Defias como su base de operaciones definitiva. Aquí, Edwin VanCleef y sus ingenieros goblins reclutados a la fuerza trabajan lejos de los ojos del reino para construir una máquina de venganza contra la corona. Antes de la Primera Guerra, Las Minas de la Muerte eran celebradas como el mayor centro productor de oro de las tierras humanas, financiando la prosperidad de Ventormenta. Cuando la Horda orca arrasó el reino y redujo a cenizas la capital, las minas fueron apresuradamente abandonadas a la oscuridad. Durante aquellos años turbulentos, figuras legendarias recorrieron estas profundidades: Sir Anduin Lothar fue encarcelado por ogros subterráneos durante veinte meses mientras recuperaba el sagrado Libro de la Divinidad, y la rebelde hija del Jefe de Guerra Puño Negro, Griselda, huyó a los pasadizos inferiores junto al ogro Turok antes de que ambos encontraran su final. Consideradas malditas y pobladas únicamente por no-muertos errantes y alimañas subterráneas al acecho, las profundidades permanecieron intactas durante décadas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="These desecrated shafts are a test of valor and faith, echoing the historic trials of Sir Anduin Lothar and the lost miners whose restless dead still wander the outer tunnels.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Deadmines represent the gravest internal threat to the kingdom of Stormwind; bringing down VanCleef is the defining victory that restores hope to the besieged farmers of Westfall.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Goblin Foundry and Sneed's mechanical workshop offer an inside look at cutting-edge steam shredders, remote-controlled golems, and specialized ordnance.",["profession:Mining"]="Once supplying a third of the capital's wealth, the rocky tunnels remain rich in veins of copper, tin, and precious silver."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance is hidden inside a derelict barn in the ruined town of Moonbrook, located in southwestern Westfall. Winding tunnels pass through an outer complex of Defias diggers and undead miners before reaching the locked instance threshold.",["al"]={"deadmines entrance","how to get to deadmines","where is deadmines"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Deadmines located?"},{["a"]="Adventurers frequently refer to the dungeon as 'VC' after its master, Edwin VanCleef. This shorthand is used to avoid confusing the Deadmines with Dire Maul, an ancient elven complex in Feralas that shares the initials 'DM'.",["al"]={"why vc","vc meaning","why call it vc"},["q"]="Why does everyone call the Deadmines 'VC'?"},{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant guildmaster of the Stonemasons who oversaw the majestic reconstruction of Stormwind City after the First War. When the House of Nobles refused to honor their debts, VanCleef formed the Defias Brotherhood to exact restitution through rebellion and open brigandage.",["al"]={"vancleef backstory","who is the final boss","defias leader"},["q"]="Who is Edwin VanCleef?"},{["a"]="The Defias have contracted goblin engineers to assemble a massive ironclad juggernaught. Armed with heavy ordnance and sturdy timber, the warship is designed to sail out of the cove's sea gate and raid the trade that feeds the capital.",["al"]={"what are they building","deadmines ship","juggernaught"},["q"]="What is being built in Ironclad Cove?"},{["a"]="Foreman Thistlenettle and his crew were sent to legally reopen the mines for the kingdom. When the Defias stormed the works, a devastating tunnel collapse trapped the miners in the dark, where they starved and eventually rose as mindless, restless undead.",["al"]={"thistlenettle fate","why are there undead miners","collecting memories lore"},["q"]="What happened to the Miners' League workers outside the instance?"},{["a"]="Cookie serves as the bizarre ship's cook aboard VanCleef's dreadnaught. While defeating VanCleef cuts off the head of the rebellion, slaying Cookie cleans out the remaining crew lingering in the ship's galley, utterly breaking the crew's presence in Ironclad Cove before adventurers escape out the coastal passage.",["al"]={"cookie the murloc","why is cookie a boss","cookie deadmines"},["q"]="What does defeating Cookie the murloc mean for the Defias ship?"},{["a"]="Following the natural tunnel out behind the dreadnaught brings adventurers to an exit along the coastal bluffs of the Dagger Hills, looking out toward the ocean and the Westfall Lighthouse.",["al"]={"deadmines exit","where does the exit go"},["q"]="Where does the exit tunnel lead when leaving the dungeon?"}},["kw"]={"cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","moonbrook","mr. smite","vancleef","westfall"},["n"]="The Deadmines",["s"]="Deep beneath the dusty farm town of Moonbrook lies the Deadmines, an enormous subterranean complex that once supplied a third of Stormwind's gold reserves. Abandoned during the First War and long considered haunted, these labyrinthine tunnels have secretly been overtaken by the Defias Brotherhood as their ultimate staging ground. Here, Edwin VanCleef and his conscripted goblin engineers labor away from the eyes of the realm to build an engine of vengeance against the kingdom.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the First War, the Deadmines were celebrated as the greatest gold-producing center in human lands, financing the prosperity of Stormwind. When the Orcish Horde swept through the kingdom and razed the capital, the mines were hastily abandoned to the dark. During those turbulent years, legendary figures walked these depths: Sir Anduin Lothar was imprisoned by subterranean ogres for twenty months while recovering the sacred Tome of Divinity, and Warchief Blackhand's rebellious daughter Griselda fled into the lower passages alongside the ogre Turok before both met their ends. Believed to be cursed and populated only by shambling undead and lurking subterranean vermin, the depths lay untouched for decades.",["t"]="A Legacy of Gold and Ruin"},{["b"]="When the Stonemasons' Guild was cast out of Stormwind without payment for rebuilding the city, Edwin VanCleef reorganized the disenfranchised artisans into the Defias Brotherhood. Seeking a secure headquarters safe from Gryan Stoutmantle's People's Militia, the thieves established their central redoubt within the abandoned tunnels. They drove out the legitimate Miners' League—leaving Foreman Thistlenettle's doomed workers to perish and rise as undead ghouls—and converted the shafts into an industrial war camp. Guarded by lumbering ogres, seasoned brigands, and mechanical constructs, the lower mines echo once again with picks, fires, and illicit industry.",["t"]="Sanctum of the Brotherhood"},{["b"]="Beyond the sweltering Goblin Foundry and the timber-strewn Mast Room lies Ironclad Cove, a vast subterranean grotto hollowed out beneath the Dagger Hills. In this hidden harbor, VanCleef has employed goblin shipbuilders and tinkerers to construct a colossal ironclad dreadnaught. Commanded by Captain Greenskin and First Mate Mr. Smite, this warship is engineered to sail through an underwater sea gate leading out toward the ocean, where the Defias Brotherhood means to prey on the sea trade that keeps Stormwind rich.",["t"]="The Secret of Ironclad Cove"}}}}}
t["zone:dunmorogh"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="Tanto los enanos como los gnomos inician aquí sus viajes, en el Valle de Crestanevada, una cuenca resguardada en el suroeste de Dun Morogh, antes de aventurarse a través del Desfiladero de Crestanevada hacia Kharanos y el resto de la zona.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="73a334",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Durante la Tercera Guerra, una raza subterránea conocida como troggs invadió Gnomeregan en tropel. En un intento por purgar a los invasores, el Manitas Mayor Gelbin Mekkatorque liberó gas radiactivo en los niveles inferiores. El plan fracasó de forma catastrófica, matando a miles y convirtiendo a muchos gnomos en gnomos parias desquiciados debido a la radiación, lo que obligó a los supervivientes sanos a huir a Forjaz.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="637710",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Dun Morogh está amurallado por altas crestas montañosas. Para viajar a pie hacia el este, rumbo a Loch Modan, toma los caminos que conducen al Paso de la Puerta Norte o al Paso de la Puerta Sur en las montañas del noreste. También puedes viajar directamente a Ciudad de Ventormenta a través del Tren subterráneo que hay dentro de Forjaz.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="b4489a",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El único maestro de vuelo de la Alianza operativo en la zona se encuentra dentro de la Gran Fundición, en Forjaz, y conecta a los viajeros con emplazamientos de Khaz Modan, Ventormenta y los puestos avanzados del norte de la Alianza.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="65db36",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Los Peloescarcha son una tribu de trolls de hielo que gobernó Dun Morogh mucho antes de que los enanos emergieran de Uldaman. Aunque fueron derrotados y arrojados a los riscos hace generaciones, siguen siendo acérrimos enemigos de Forjaz y asaltan con frecuencia granjas y caminos enanos desde refugios como el Poblado Peloescarcha.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="33317b",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Kharanos es el asentamiento enano principal del centro de Dun Morogh. Alberga la Destilería Cebatruenos, instructores y suministros, y sirve como centro de operaciones principal para los jóvenes aventureros y montañeros que lidian con los problemas locales de trolls y fauna salvaje.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e67911",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="10,374,21.621.0,16.623.0,21.550.0,31.194.0,28.349.0,36.270.0,41.202.0,29.283.0,17.249.0",["h"]="9d3861",["n"]="Dun Morogh",["s"]="Dun Morogh. Dun Morogh es una meseta montañosa azotada por la nieve y situada en el corazón de Khaz Modan. Sirve como punto de partida ancestral y hogar compartido para los enanos de Forjaz y los gnomos desplazados de Gnomeregan. Aunque está protegido por imponentes picos y pasos fortificados, este reino nevado se enfrenta a crecientes amenazas internas procedentes de los troggs, los trolls Peloescarcha y los gnomos parias irradiados. Dun Morogh ocupa los picos más altos de los Reinos del Este, una extensión alpina rodeada de cumbres escarpadas que la protegen de La Garganta de Fuego al sur y de Los Humedales al norte. Estas montañas nevadas alimentan los ríos que fluyen a través de Khaz Modan y proporcionan vetas prácticamente ilimitadas de cobre y hierro. El acceso está sumamente restringido a túneles de montaña como el Paso de la Puerta Norte y el Paso de la Puerta Sur, vigilados de cerca por los montañeros enanos. En el corazón de la región se asienta Forjaz, una antigua maravilla subterránea y capital del reino del Rey Magni Barbabronce, comunicada directamente con Ventormenta mediante la maravilla del Tren subterráneo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Cooking"]="Local hunters and innkeepers in Kharanos and Brewnall Village make hearty use of boar meat, bear ribs, and dwarven stout to ward off the biting mountain frost.",["profession:Mining"]="The mountain crags of Dun Morogh are rich with surface deposits of Copper Veins, particularly around the quarry at Gol'Bolar and along the snowy rock faces.",["race:Dwarf"]="This is your ancestral homeland. From the hearthfires of Anvilmar to the blazing core of the Great Forge in Ironforge, defending these peaks from trolls and troggs is your duty to King Magni.",["race:Gnome"]="Your lost home, Gnomeregan, lies irradiated in the western valley. Dun Morogh serves as your base in exile alongside your dwarven cousins while you fight back against troggs and rogue leper gnomes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Both dwarves and gnomes begin their journeys here in Coldridge Valley, a sheltered basin in southwestern Dun Morogh, before venturing out through Coldridge Pass into Kharanos and the wider zone.",["al"]={"dun morogh starting race","who starts here","dwarf start zone","gnome start zone"},["q"]="What races start in Dun Morogh?"},{["a"]="During the Third War, a subterranean race called troggs swarmed Gnomeregan. In an attempt to purge the invaders, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque released radioactive gas into the lower levels. The plan failed catastrophically, killing thousands and irradiating many gnomes into crazed leper gnomes, forcing the healthy survivors to flee to Ironforge.",["al"]={"why is gnomeregan ruined","what happened to the gnomes","why are leper gnomes here"},["q"]="What happened to Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="Dun Morogh is walled in by high mountain ridges. To travel eastward into Loch Modan on foot, take the roads leading to North Gate Pass or South Gate Pass in the northeastern mountains. You can also travel directly to Stormwind City via the Deeprun Tram inside Ironforge.",["al"]={"exit dun morogh","dun morogh to loch modan","leave dun morogh"},["q"]="How do you leave Dun Morogh on foot?"},{["a"]="The only functional Alliance flight master in the zone is located inside the Great Forge of Ironforge, connecting travelers to locations across Khaz Modan, Stormwind, and the northern Alliance outposts.",["al"]={"dun morogh flight master","dun morogh flight path","where to fly dun morogh"},["q"]="Where is the flight master in Dun Morogh?"},{["a"]="The Frostmane are a tribe of ice trolls who ruled Dun Morogh long before the dwarves emerged from Uldaman. Though defeated and driven into the crags generations ago, they remain bitter enemies of Ironforge, routinely raiding dwarven farms and roads from retreats like Frostmane Hold.",["al"]={"why are there trolls in dun morogh","dun morogh trolls","frostmane tribe"},["q"]="Who are the Frostmane trolls?"},{["a"]="Kharanos is the primary dwarven settlement in central Dun Morogh. It houses the Thunderbrew Distillery, trainers, and supplies, serving as the central operational hub for young adventurers and Mountaineers tackling local troll and wildlife problems.",["al"]={"town in dun morogh","kharanos hub","what is the main town"},["q"]="What is Kharanos?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","brewnall village","coldridge valley","deeprun tram","dun morogh","frostmane","gnomeregan","gol'bolar","ironforge","kharanos","magni bronzebeard","troggs"},["n"]="Dun Morogh",["s"]="Dun Morogh is a snow-swept mountain highland situated at the heart of Khaz Modan. It serves as the ancestral starting ground and shared homeland for the dwarves of Ironforge and the displaced gnomes of Gnomeregan. Though guarded by towering peaks and fortified passes, the snowy realm faces rising internal threats from troggs, Frostmane trolls, and irradiated leper gnomes.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dun Morogh occupies the highest peaks in the Eastern Kingdoms, an alpine expanse ringed by jagged summits that shield it from Searing Gorge to the south and the Wetlands to the north. These snowy mountains feed the rivers flowing across Khaz Modan and provide near-limitless veins of copper and iron. Access is heavily restricted to mountain tunnels like North Gate Pass and South Gate Pass, watched closely by dwarven Mountaineers. At the heart of the region sits Ironforge, an ancient subterranean wonder and the capital of King Magni Bronzebeard's realm, linked straight to Stormwind by the marvel of the Deeprun Tram.",["t"]="A Mountain Stronghold"},{["b"]="Centuries ago, the dwarves drove the native Frostmane ice trolls into the crags, carving out room for themselves alongside their brilliant gnome allies. The two races flourished in neighboring mountain halls until the recent catastrophe in Gnomeregan during the Third War. A horrific trogg invasion and a catastrophic radioactive venting ruined the technological wonder, turning its defenders into mindless leper gnomes and driving High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his surviving folk into exile. Now, the gnomes dwell as guests inside Ironforge, while leper gnomes and surviving troggs spill out into Chill Breeze Valley.",["t"]="A Refuge Divided"},{["b"]="Life in the drifts is far from quiet. The Frostmane tribe has grown emboldened, establishing heavily armed encampments from Shimmer Ridge down to Coldridge Valley. Meanwhile, primitive troggs have clawed their way out of ancient subterranean fissures into Gol'Bolar Quarry, threatening the region's mining operations. Between prowling wendigos, wild boars, infiltrating Dark Iron dwarven agents, and toxic fallout spreading from the ruins of Gnomeregan, the dwarven Mountaineers are stretched thin maintaining order from Kharanos to the border gates.",["t"]="Trouble in the Drifts"}}}}}
t["zone:dustwallow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,455,19.504.0,29.597.0,25.524.2,42.305.0,53.235.0,58.268.2,52.241.0,52.222.0,41.193.2",["h"]="65f2a1",["n"]="Marjal Revolcafango",["s"]="Marjal Revolcafango. Marjal Revolcafango es un vasto y sofocante pantano en el centro de Kalimdor, atrapado entre las áridas llanuras de Los Baldíos y el Mare Magnum. Alimentadas por perpetuos manantiales subterráneos, sus traicioneras ciénagas albergan peligrosos depredadores, escaramuzas encubiertas entre facciones y la acechante presencia del Vuelo Negro. Sirve de hogar a la isla-fortaleza de la Alianza de Theramore en el este y a los ogros Quebrantarrocas del Poblado Murohelecho, aliados de la Horda, al noroeste. Antes del Gran Cataclismo, Marjal Revolcafango era una meseta herbosa repleta de manadas de animales. El cataclismo destrozó el valle, haciendo que el nivel freático subiera y ahogara la tierra en interminables charcas estancadas, bajíos cubiertos de musgo y lodo asfixiante. Los manantiales subterráneos garantizan que la ciénaga permanezca perpetuamente húmeda y sumergida, cubierta por una densa niebla e infestada de crocoliscos, raptores y arañas. Los bajíos escarpados y las ciénagas movedizas hacen que viajar sea peligroso para cualquier aventurero que se aleje de las calzadas en ruinas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,2,0,0,2},["sec"]={0,0,2}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Mages are drawn across the fens to Tabetha's Farm in the Quagmire, seeking out the recluse's unique expertise regarding arcane conduits and ancient power sources.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dustwallow Marsh hosts Theramore Isle, the heart of the Alliance's presence on Kalimdor. Adventurers arriving via Menethil Harbor guard its causeways while untangling a web of deserters and missing envoys.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde emissaries come to support the beleaguered Stonemaul ogres at Brackenwall Village, repelling dragon incursions from the Wyrmbog and keeping a wary eye on human movements from the coast."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Alliance's presence is centered at Theramore Isle, a fortified city-state situated on a rocky island off the eastern coast. Founded by Lady Jaina Proudmoore following the Third War, it connects to Kalimdor by a narrow roadway and maintains vital ship routes to Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["al"]={"alliance base dustwallow","where is theramore","human town dustwallow"},["q"]="What is the main Alliance settlement here?"},{["a"]="Horde travelers make camp at Brackenwall Village in the northwestern reaches of the marsh. The settlement was founded by the Stonemaul clan of ogres, who joined the Horde under Rexxar and opened their gates to orcish and tauren allies.",["al"]={"horde base dustwallow","where is brackenwall","ogre village"},["q"]="Where can Horde adventurers find refuge in the swamp?"},{["a"]="The southern region, known as the Wyrmbog and Dragonmurk, is the brood grounds and domain of Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing. Her black dragonspawn violently drove out the Stonemaul ogres and turned the rocky outcroppings and deep caves into nests for whelps and drakes.",["al"]={"wyrmbog dragons","why black dragons here","dragonmurk"},["q"]="Why are there so many black dragons in the southern marsh?"},{["a"]="The Stonemaul ogres originally dwelt peacefully in Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh. However, the black dragonflight launched a devastating assault, slaughtering many and forcing the survivors to flee northwest to Brackenwall Village.",["al"]={"stonemaul ruins","what happened to stonemaul village","old ogre town"},["q"]="What happened to the Stonemaul ogres' original home?"},{["a"]="The cottage belongs to Tabetha, an eccentric and powerful hermit mage living quietly in the depths of the marsh. Arcane practitioners often seek her out for instruction or assistance with cleansing volatile magical relics.",["al"]={"tabetha's farm","tabetha dustwallow","who is the witch in the swamp"},["q"]="Who lives in the lonely cottage out in the Quagmire?"},{["a"]="Alcaz Island is a heavily guarded isle off the northeast coast of the marsh, held by the Strashaz naga and patrolled by dangerous elite defenders, with hydras lurking in the surrounding waters.",["al"]={"alcaz island","island off coast dustwallow","what is on alcaz"},["q"]="What is Alcaz Island and who controls it?"}},["kw"]={"alcaz","brackenwall","dustwallow","jaina","marsh","onyxia","quagmire","stonemaul","tabetha","theramore","wyrmbog"},["n"]="Dustwallow Marsh",["s"]="Dustwallow Marsh is a vast, sweltering swampland in central Kalimdor, trapped between the arid plains of the Barrens and the Great Sea. Fed by perpetual subterranean springs, its treacherous fens harbor dangerous predators, covert faction skirmishes, and the lurking presence of the black dragonflight. It serves as home to the Alliance fortress-island of Theramore in the east and the Horde-allied Stonemaul ogres of Brackenwall Village to the northwest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Great Sundering, Dustwallow was a high, grassy plain teeming with herd animals. The cataclysm shattered the valley, causing the water table to rise and drown the earth in endless stagnant pools, mossy shallows, and choking mud. Underground springs ensure the marsh remains perpetually humid and submerged, blanketed in thick fog and infested with crocolisks, raptors, and spiders. Jagged shallows and wandering bogs make travel perilous for any adventurer stepping off the crumbling causeways.",["t"]="A Drowned Landscape"},{["b"]="Dustwallow was largely wild until the aftermath of the Third War, when Lady Jaina Proudmoore led human refugees across the sea to establish the citadel of Theramore Isle on its eastern coast. Soon after, Kul Tiran forces under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore waged war against Thrall's fledgling Horde, culminating in bloody battles across the wetlands and the Admiral's defeat. Today, an official armistice exists between Theramore and Orgrimmar, yet tension smolders beneath the surface. Theramore struggles with desertions and sabotage, while spies wage quiet, deadly conflicts across the fens.",["t"]="Old Hatreds and Uneasy Truces"},{["b"]="The south of the marsh rises into a jagged, rocky quagmire known as the Dragonmurk and the Wyrmbog. Originally settled by the Stonemaul ogres under the Mok'Nathal champion Rexxar, the area became a graveyard when the black dragonflight violently drove the clan from Stonemaul Village. The displaced ogres fled north to Brackenwall Village under Overlord Mok'Morokk, swearing vengeance. Within these jagged crags lurks Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing, directing her brood and weaving sinister machinations far beyond the swamp.",["t"]="The Shadow of the Wyrmbog"}}}}}
t["zone:elwynn"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="Las fuerzas armadas de Ventormenta apenas dan abasto. El reino amplió cuantiosos despliegues militares hacia el sur, en la Vega de Tuercespina, contrayendo profundas deudas y mermando la mano de obra local. Como resultado, puestos avanzados como el Cuartel Arroyoeste y Villadorada dependen de guarniciones muy reducidas y reclutas voluntarios para repeler a bandidos, gnolls y múrlocs.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e68732",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Ante la escasez de guardias, kóbolds oportunistas irrumpieron en la Mina Abisal, la Cantera de Jaspe y la Mina del Eco en busca de oro y minerales preciosos. Expulsaron a los prospectores y mineros humanos, defendiendo con agresividad sus concesiones subterráneas con velas, picos rudimentarios y herramientas improvisadas.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="9f68a6",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Son miembros de la Hermandad Defias, liderados por Edwin VanCleef. En su origen, muchos eran artesanos de la Hermandad de los Albañiles que reconstruyeron Ciudad de Ventormenta tras la Primera Guerra. Cuando la nobleza se negó a pagarles los salarios prometidos, estallaron revueltas que llevaron a su destierro y a su caída en el bandidaje organizado.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="2d27bc",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Al cruzar el puente sobre el río Nazferiti se entra en el Bosque del Ocaso, conocido históricamente como Brightwood. Ese territorio, antaño pacífico, ha caído en una oscuridad antinatural y ahora está infestado de no-muertos, arañas monstruosas y bestias voraces.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e7e497",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Los Pedregosa y los Maclure son familias campesinas vecinas del sur de Elwynn que mantienen un rencor encarnizado y de larga data entre sí. A pesar de sus incesantes riñas y acusaciones, dos de sus parientes más jóvenes, Maybell Maclure y Tommy Joe Pedregosa, se han enamorado en secreto, complicando la rivalidad aún más.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="22d611",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La Torre de Azora es una aguja arcana situada junto al camino entre Villadorada y el Aserradero de la Vega del Este. Alberga a magos solitarios, entre ellos Theocritus, que observan las líneas ley de la región y llevan a cabo investigaciones mágicas al margen de la supervisión directa del Sagrario del Mago de Ventormenta.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="185114",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="13,409,28.423.0,18.493.0,22.639.1,54.341.0,43.303.0,38.313.0,31.240.0,54.342.0,27.282.0",["h"]="baf765",["n"]="Bosque de Elwynn",["s"]="Bosque de Elwynn. El Bosque de Elwynn es el corazón verde del Reino de Ventormenta, y abastece a la capital de madera, oro, pescado y cosechas esenciales. Al abrigo de majestuosos árboles de madera dura, sirve como campo de pruebas para los nuevos reclutas humanos que parten de la Abadía de Villanorte. Sin embargo, bajo su idílica cubierta de ramas, los bosques se encuentran seriamente asediados por alimañas invasoras, fauna desplazada y un bandidaje generalizado. Extendiéndose hacia el sur desde las puertas de Ventormenta hasta el río Nazferiti, Elwynn es una región fértil bendecida con abundantes lluvias y densos bosques de madera dura. Comunidades como Villadorada y el Aserradero de la Vega del Este proporcionan grano, ganado, madera y cobre en bruto cruciales para sostener la gran capital. La región también es famosa por la cría de robustos caballos de Evendale, predilectos de viajeros y caballeros de todo el reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The pervasive shadow of the Defias Brotherhood makes Elwynn an intriguing crossroads of thievery, smuggled goods, and underground rebel signals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting Elwynn is vital to the survival of the Alliance's primary human kingdom; if the lumber, ore, and grain routes collapse, Stormwind City cannot sustain itself.",["profession:Mining"]="Echo Ridge, Fargodeep, and Jasperlode are laden with copper veins, making the forest an essential early proving ground for miners despite the kobold infestations.",["race:Human"]="This is the ancestral heart of the kingdom. Human adventurers begin here, training at Northshire Abbey before venturing out to defend their homeland from bandits, beasts, and political ruin."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stormwind's armed forces are severely overstretched. The kingdom expanded heavy military deployments southward into Stranglethorn Vale, running up deep debts and draining local manpower. As a result, outposts like Westbrook Garrison and Goldshire rely on small skeleton crews and volunteer recruits to fight off bandits, gnolls, and murlocs.",["al"]={"where are the guards","why no stormwind army","why is elwynn undefended"},["q"]="Why is the Stormwind Guard barely policing the forest?"},{["a"]="With guards in short supply, opportunistic kobolds swarmed into Fargodeep Mine, Jasperlode Mine, and Echo Ridge Mine in search of precious gold and minerals. They drove out the human prospectors and miners, aggressively defending their subterranean claims with candles, crude picks, and scavenged tools.",["al"]={"why are kobolds in the mines","elwynn kobolds","fargodeep infested"},["q"]="Why are there kobolds inside all the mines?"},{["a"]="They are members of the Defias Brotherhood, led by Edwin VanCleef. Many were originally artisans of the Stonemasons Guild who rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War. When the nobility refused to pay them their promised wages, riots broke out, leading to their banishment and descent into organized brigandage.",["al"]={"red masks","red bandana bandits","who are the defias in elwynn"},["q"]="Who are the bandits wearing red masks?"},{["a"]="Crossing the bridge over the Nazferiti River takes you into Duskwood, historically known as Brightwood. That once-peaceful territory has fallen into unnatural darkness and is now infested with undead, monstrous spiders, and ravenous beasts.",["al"]={"what is across the river","where does duskwood bridge go","bridge across the nazferiti"},["q"]="Where does the road south lead?"},{["a"]="The Stonefields and the Maclures are neighboring farming families in southern Elwynn who have maintained a bitter, longstanding grudge against each other. Despite their endless bickering and accusations, two of their younger kin—Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield—have secretly fallen in love, complicating the rivalry even further.",["al"]={"maclure vs stonefield","elwynn farm rivalry","stonefield maclure feud"},["q"]="What is the feud between the Maclures and Stonefields?"},{["a"]="The Tower of Azora is an arcane spire located along the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp. It houses secluded mages, including Theocritus, who observe the region's leylines and conduct magical research outside the direct oversight of Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum.",["al"]={"tower on the road to eastvale","wizard tower elwynn","who lives in the tower of azora"},["q"]="What is the Tower of Azora?"}},["kw"]={"defias","eastvale","elwynn","elwynn forest","fargodeep","goldshire","hogger","jasperlode","nazferiti","northshire","northshire abbey","vancleef"},["n"]="Elwynn Forest",["s"]="Elwynn Forest is the verdant heartland of the Kingdom of Stormwind, providing the capital with essential timber, gold, fish, and crops. Sheltered beneath stately hardwoods, it serves as the proving ground for new human recruits stepping forth from Northshire Abbey. Yet beneath its idyllic pastoral canopy, the woods are sorely beleaguered by encroaching vermin, displaced wildlife, and widespread brigandage.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching south from the gates of Stormwind down to the Nazferiti River, Elwynn is a fertile region blessed with abundant rainfall and dense hardwood forests. Communities like Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp provide crucial grain, livestock, lumber, and raw copper to sustain the grand capital. The region is also celebrated for breeding sturdy Evendale horses, favored by travelers and knights across the kingdom.",["t"]="The Breadbasket of the Realm"},{["b"]="Despite its outward serenity, the woods are on the brink of disorder. The Stormwind Army is stretched thin by distant obligations, leaving local marshals and deputies reliant on untested recruits. Kobolds have overrun the vital Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines, Riverpaw gnolls prowl the southwestern borders, and savage murlocs have claimed the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. In the wake of rising corruption across the river in Duskwood, wolves have fled north across the border.",["t"]="A Precarious Peace"},{["b"]="Far more organized than mere scavengers, the Defias Brotherhood has deeply infiltrated the forest. Originating from Edwin VanCleef's disenfranchised Stonemasons Guild following bitter pay disputes with the House of Nobles, these masked outlaws have seized holdings across Elwynn, including the Northshire Vineyards, the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Jerod's Landing, and Mirror Lake Orchard. Rumors persist that their coordinated agents are subtly orchestrating the neighboring gnolls and kobolds to further destabilize the realm. Guards Rolf and Malakai, sent to investigate murlocs near Stone Cairn Lake, were killed and left along its banks.",["t"]="The Red Bandana Threat"}}}}}
t["zone:felwood"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,424,19.653.0,21.569.0,22.458.1,25.279.0,51.281.0,22.263.0,36.267.0,60.250.0,49.238.0",["h"]="aa4dde",["n"]="Frondavil",["s"]="Frondavil. Frondavil es un bosque asolado situado entre Vallefresno y el Monte Hyjal, profundamente envenenado por magia demoníaca durante la Tercera Guerra. Antaño un exuberante paraíso de praderas y arboledas cuidadas por los elfos de la noche, ahora está infestado de sátiros demoníacos, bestias babeantes y ancestros retorcidos. Los druidas del Círculo Cenarion, junto con avanzadas de la Alianza y la Horda, trabajan desesperadamente para purificar la tierra y purgar al Consejo de la Sombra de sus profundidades. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, este valle era un remanso de paz con aves cantarinas, arroyos transparentes y arboledas tranquilas custodiadas por antiguos protectores. Todo terminó cuando el señor del terror Tichondrius y la Legión Ardiente desplegaron la Calavera de Gul'dan para envenenar el norte de Kalimdor antes de su asalto al Monte Hyjal. Las viles hechicerías de la calavera convirtieron el suelo del bosque en una ciénaga ennegrecida. Aunque Illidan Tempestira acabó matando a Tichondrius y consumió la esencia del artefacto, la tierra permaneció sumida en la corrupción vil. Poderosos antárboles y ancestros se pudrieron desde dentro, los ríos se convirtieron en bilis hirviente y las bestias del bosque cayeron en una locura caníbal.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Felwood is a profound tragedy for the Cenarion Circle, where druids dedicate their lives to cleansing blighted plants and calming maddened nature spirits.",["class:Warlock"]="The dark tunnels of Jaedenar and the lingering demonic forces make Felwood a focal point for hunting rival cultists of the Shadow Council.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The fel-soaked earth yields rare and volatile flora, serving as one of the few places in Azeroth to gather Gromsblood and Arthas' Tears.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of these ancient woods is a source of immense grief and shame for the kaldorei, who failed to protect them from the Legion's touch."},["faq"]={{["a"]="During the Third War, the dreadlord Tichondrius used the demonic artifact known as the Skull of Gul'dan to corrupt the forest. This was intended to weaken the night elves' defenses during the Burning Legion's march toward Mount Hyjal, blighting the wildlife, water, and ancients.",["al"]={"how did felwood get corrupted","what happened to felwood","why are the trees dead"},["q"]="Why is Felwood corrupted?"},{["a"]="Yes. Druids of the Cenarion Circle provide adventurers with salves brewed from collected fel taints and mineral residues. Applying these salves to plants like songflowers, whiplash tubers, and night dragons purges their corruption and yields potent restorative fruit and blessings.",["al"]={"how to cleanse plants","cenarion plant salve","corrupted songflower"},["q"]="Can the corrupted plants in the forest be cleansed?"},{["a"]="Jaedenar is held by the Shadow Council, a clandestine sect of mortal warlocks and demon worshippers. From deep within the subterranean caverns of Shadow Hold, the dreadlord Lord Banehollow oversees their dark rituals and commands the satyrs inhabiting the region.",["al"]={"what is jaedenar","who is in shadow hold","jaedenar boss"},["q"]="Who controls Jaedenar?"},{["a"]="Most are hostile. Tribes such as the Deadwood have completely succumbed to demonic corruption and fel madness. However, the Timbermaw tribe holding the northern tunnel network remains uncorrupted, though they are deeply distrustful of outsiders until proven friendly.",["al"]={"felwood furbolgs","timbermaw furbolgs","deadwood village"},["q"]="Are the furbolgs in Felwood hostile?"},{["a"]="The road leads north directly into Timbermaw Hold, a fortified cavern complex. The uncorrupted Timbermaw furbolgs control the tunnels connecting Felwood to Moonglade and Winterspring. Travelers must either earn their trust or fight their way through.",["al"]={"timbermaw tunnel","road to winterspring","pass to moonglade"},["q"]="How do you get to Moonglade or Winterspring through Felwood?"},{["a"]="The once-noble ancients and treants were warped and poisoned by demonic magic. Bound in eternal agony, their shattered minds harbor deep resentment toward the night elves, whom they perceive as having abandoned them to the Burning Legion.",["al"]={"mad treants","corrupted ancients","why ancients hostile"},["q"]="Why do the corrupted ancients attack night elves?"}},["kw"]={"banehollow","bloodvenom","deadwood","emerald sanctuary","felwood","jaedenar","songflower","talonbranch","tichondrius","timbermaw"},["n"]="Felwood",["s"]="Felwood is a blighted forest nestled between Ashenvale and Mount Hyjal, deeply poisoned by demonic magic during the Third War. Once a lush paradise of meadows and groves tended by the night elves, it now crawls with demonic satyrs, slavering beasts, and twisted ancients. Cenarion Circle druids, alongside outposts of the Alliance and Horde, desperately work to cleanse the land and purge the Shadow Council from its depths.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this valley was a peaceful haven of singing birds, clear streams, and tranquil groves guarded by ancient protectors. That ended when the dreadlord Tichondrius and the Burning Legion deployed the Skull of Gul'dan to poison northern Kalimdor ahead of their assault on Mount Hyjal. The skull's vile sorceries twisted the forest floor into a blackened mire. Though Illidan Stormrage eventually slew Tichondrius and consumed the artifact's essence, the land remained steeped in fel corruption. Mighty treants and ancients rotted from within, rivers turned to boiling bile, and the forest's beasts were driven into cannibalistic madness.",["t"]="A Paradise Befouled"},{["b"]="Healing Felwood has proven agonizingly slow. At the Emerald Sanctuary along the southern border, the Cenarion Circle wages an uphill battle against the blighted corruption. Druids equip wanderers with Cenarion beacons and cleansing salves, laboring to heal poisoned plants like songflowers and night dragon bulbs. Both factions maintain footholds in the tainted wilds—the night elves at Talonbranch Glade in the north and the Horde at Bloodvenom Post. These outposts serve as fragile bulwarks amid a deadly wilderness where nature has turned against all mortal flesh.",["t"]="The War for Cleansing"},{["b"]="The lingering fel taint is actively nurtured by dark cultists. Within the subterranean labyrinth of Jaedenar and Shadow Hold, remnants of the Shadow Council conduct foul rituals under the direction of Lord Banehollow. Allied with deceitful satyrs who desecrate ancient moonwells, these warlocks harvest the forest's agony and summon forth demonic reinforcements. Any lasting hope of redeeming Felwood requires tearing this insidious council out by its roots.",["t"]="The Shadow in Jaedenar"}}}}}
t["zone:feralas"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,414,32.516.0,25.502.0,26.486.0,18.309.0,62.340.0,61.302.0,24.275.0,44.273.0,30.249.0",["h"]="4b33bc",["n"]="Feralas",["s"]="Feralas. Feralas es una vasta selva tropical envuelta en niebla situada entre Desolace, Las Mil Agujas y el Mar Adusto. Protegida por imponentes murallas montañosas, preserva un ecosistema ancestral salpicado de ruinas kaldorei cubiertas de vegetación y bestias primigenias. En la actualidad, esta naturaleza virgen es territorio en disputa, atrapada entre antiguos vestigios de los Altonato, los invasores ogros Gordunni y los puestos de avanzada rivales establecidos por la Alianza y la Horda. Mientras que las vecinas Desolace y Las Mil Agujas se han secado hasta convertirse en yermos áridos y cañones desecados, Feralas permanece intensamente verde. Las cordilleras montañosas aíslan el dosel arbóreo, manteniendo un microclima cálido de densas nieblas, árboles milenarios y cascadas imponentes. Antes del Gran Cataclismo, gran parte de Kalimdor lucía así. Con el paso de los milenios, la densa jungla devoró los monumentos de la civilización kaldorei que una vez dominó aquí, ocultando templos y pabellones olvidados bajo el musgo asfixiante y espesos helechos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The Dream Bough and its connection to the Emerald Dream make Feralas sacred ground, demanding vigilance against encroaching corruption and defilers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operations are anchored out of Feathermoon Stronghold under Shandris Feathermoon, tasking operatives with policing coastal naga and defending elven legacy.",["faction:Horde"]="Camp Mojache serves as a vital frontier bastion, requiring reliable warriors to push back aggressive Gordunni incursions, rogue Grimtotem, and Woodpaw gnolls.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, shaded floor of the canopy yields prized temperate and tropical flora, including Sungrass, Purple Lotus, and Khadgar's Whisker.",["race:NightElf"]="Feralas holds profound cultural weight as a cradle of ancient Kaldorei civilization, yet the sight of sacred ruins like Eldre'Thalas defiled by ogres stirs deep sorrow and anger."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dire Maul is the present-day name for Eldre'Thalas, a glorious elven city that survived the Sundering. Over the millennia, it fell into decline and was overrun by the brutal Gordunni clan. The complex is now partitioned into contested wings harboring ogres, treacherous spirits, and ancient Highborne secrets.",["al"]={"eldre'thalas","ogre city","ancient ruins center"},["q"]="What is Dire Maul?"},{["a"]="Alliance explorers coming from Desolace can pass south through the Twin Colossals, though the beasts there are perilous. Alternatively, travelers can slip into the ocean along the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace and swim south along the Forgotten Coast directly to Sardor Isle, entirely bypassing the dangerous overland road and Camp Mojache.",["al"]={"getting to feathermoon","alliance entrance to feralas","how to get to feralas alliance"},["q"]="How do Alliance travelers safely reach Feathermoon Stronghold?"},{["a"]="The Gordunni ogres are violently expanding out of Dire Maul, raiding supply caravans and attacking travelers across the jungle. Their destructive war parties actively threaten Camp Mojache, prompting Horde leaders like Belgrom Rockmaul to call for swift, aggressive strikes against the clan's outposts.",["al"]={"why kill gordunni","horde ogre war","camp mojache ogres"},["q"]="Why is the Horde fighting the Gordunni ogres so aggressively?"},{["a"]="The Dream Bough is one of the four Great Trees of Azeroth, housing a mystical natural portal that connects physical reality to the Emerald Dream. Like its counterparts in Ashenvale, Duskwood, and the Hinterlands, it is watched by the green dragonflight and ancient guardians.",["al"]={"green dragon portal","great tree feralas","emerald dream tree"},["q"]="What is the Dream Bough?"},{["a"]="A renegade sect of Grimtotem tauren maintains a compound in the wilderness, operating outside the authority of Thunder Bluff. Their presence is hostile toward both the Alliance and the Horde; they have trapped local faerie dragons and are actively targeted by Horde scouts.",["al"]={"grimtotem feralas","grimtotem compound","hostile tauren"},["q"]="Why are Grimtotem tauren present in Feralas?"},{["a"]="Yes. South of the main road lies The Writhing Deep, a swarming subterranean hive of silithid insectoids. Their emergence in the lush rainforest is an unsettling sign that the hive mind is expanding far beyond the desert borders of southern Kalimdor.",["al"]={"writhing deep","bugs in feralas","silithid hive"},["q"]="Are there Silithid in Feralas?"}},["kw"]={"camp mojache","dire maul","dream bough","eldre'thalas","feathermoon","feralas","gordunni","shandris","thalanaar"},["n"]="Feralas",["s"]="Feralas is a vast, mist-shrouded rainforest nestled between Desolace, Thousand Needles, and the Veiled Sea. Sheltered by soaring mountain walls, it preserves an ancient ecosystem dotted with overgrown Kaldorei ruins and primordial beasts. Today, the wilderness is contested territory, caught between ancient Highborne remnants, invasive Gordunni ogres, and rival outposts established by the Alliance and the Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While neighboring Desolace and Thousand Needles have dried into barren badlands and desiccated canyons, Feralas remains intensely verdant. Mountain ranges seal off the canopy, sustaining a warm microclimate of deep mists, ancient trees, and towering waterfalls. Before the Great Sundering, much of Kalimdor looked like this. Over millennia, the deep jungle swallowed the monuments of the Kaldorei civilization that once ruled here, hiding forgotten temples and pavilions beneath strangling moss and thick fern brush.",["t"]="A Forest Untouched by the Wastes"},{["b"]="Dominating central Feralas is the ruined metropolis of Eldre'Thalas, now called Dire Maul. Built at the peak of the Kaldorei empire, its vast stone courtyards have fallen into ruin, desecrated by the savage Gordunni ogre clan. These ogres spread across the valley, pillaging sacred sites, defiling pristine groves, and driving indigenous wildlife into territorial frenzy. Deep within Dire Maul's sealed chambers, whispers persist of Highborne remnants and trapped powers dating back ten thousand years.",["t"]="The Ruins of Eldre'Thalas"},{["b"]="Both the Alliance and the Horde have mounted major expeditions into the jungle, though traversing it remains dangerous. From Feathermoon Stronghold on Sardor Isle, General Shandris Feathermoon directs Sentinels against both ogre expansion and encroaching naga. To the east lies Camp Mojache, a central Horde garrison struggling against aggressive Woodpaw gnolls, hostile Grimtotem tauren, and the relentless ogre clans. Neither faction commands true control over the untamable interior.",["t"]="The Struggle for Footholds"}}}}}
t["zone:gnomeregan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,464,26.669.0,36.818.0,27.701.1,17.647.1,29.409.0,35.313.0,67.382.0,22.335.0,25.321.0,53.396.1,48.315.0,42.319.0",["h"]="4946bb",["n"]="Gnomeregan",["s"]="Gnomeregan. Esculpida en las estribaciones nevadas de Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan fue antaño la capital subterránea y la mayor maravilla tecnológica de la raza gnoma. Hoy yace en ruinas y en cuarentena, envenenada por la lluvia radiactiva tras una desesperada defensa contra una invasión subterránea de troggs. Sus supervivientes viven ahora como refugiados en la cercana Forjaz, mientras las salas irradiadas siguen infestadas de troggs mutados, gnomos parias desquiciados y centinelas mecánicos rebeldes. Mucho antes de su trágica caída, Gnomeregan se erigía como un testimonio de las cumbres del ingenio, la ambición y la industria gnomos. Construido con la ayuda de los cercanos enanos de Forjaz, el extenso complejo mecánico funcionaba gracias a gigantescos motores trituradores, engranajes giratorios y una intrincada red de ventilación que requería a quince técnicos trabajando día y noche solo para mantener el aire fresco. Era un próspero centro de invención, artesanía competitiva y política centrado en la Cámara de los Manitas, y servía como la orgullosa capital desde la que los gnomos aportaron valiosas máquinas de asedio, artefactos voladores y armamento a la Alianza de Lordaeron durante la Segunda Guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,1,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The gnomes stood shoulder-to-shoulder with the Alliance in the Second War, and liberating their lost capital from Thermaplugg is vital to restoring their strength within the faction.",["profession:Engineering"]="The ruined city remains an unmatched graveyard of advanced masterworks, schematics, and experimental contraptions, offering invaluable blueprints amidst the lethal mechanical chaos.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your kinship with the gnomes traces back to when your ancestors helped lay Gnomeregan's foundations, and your excavations at Uldaman inadvertently unleashed the trogg hordes that caused its ruin.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomeregan is the heart of your people's deepest tragedy and enduring shame; venturing within is a harrowing pilgrimage to avenge eighty percent of your fallen race and dethrone the traitor Thermaplugg."},["faq"]={{["a"]="When troggs invaded from beneath the earth, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque attempted to exterminate them by opening the pressure valves on the city's radioactive waste tanks on the advice of Sicco Thermaplugg. The plan was meant to flood only the lower sectors, but the deadly toxic radiation seeped throughout the entire city, slaughtering eighty percent of the gnomish population and mutating the survivors.",["al"]={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan green","radiation in gnomeregan"},["q"]="Why is Gnomeregan irradiated?"},{["a"]="The troggs were ancient creatures stirred from deep subterranean slumber by dwarven archaeological excavations at the titan complex of Uldaman. Drawn to the vibrations and heat of Gnomeregan's heavy machinery, they dug extensive tunnel networks directly into the lower levels and engineering quarters of the city.",["al"]={"why are there troggs in gnomeregan","trogg origin","trogg invasion"},["q"]="Where did all the troggs come from?"},{["a"]="The trogg invasion occurred at the height of the Third War, while the Kingdom of Lordaeron was falling to the Scourge. Believing the survival of the wider Alliance took precedence, High Tinker Mekkatorque chose not to divert human, dwarven, or elven forces away from the northern battlefronts, attempting to handle the invasion internally with gnomish technology and soldiers alone.",["al"]={"why didn't alliance help gnomeregan","did alliance abandon gnomes"},["q"]="Why didn't the gnomes ask the Alliance for help against the troggs?"},{["a"]="Leper gnomes are gnomes who survived the radioactive venting of Gnomeregan but suffered severe physical and mental corruption from prolonged exposure. Their skin has turned a sickly pale green, their bodies are blistered and diseased, and their minds have decayed into raving, homicidal mania under the thrall of Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",["al"]={"why are the gnomes green and crazy","irradiated gnomes","leper gnome lore"},["q"]="What are leper gnomes?"},{["a"]="Sicco Thermaplugg was High Tinker Mekkatorque's closest confidant and chief advisor. Driven mad by jealousy and a lust for power, he intentionally engineered the radioactive purge to ruin Mekkatorque and seize the throne. Irradiated along with the city, he now rules as a deranged leper despot from within Tinkers' Court.",["al"]={"thermaplugg","who is the final boss","mekgineer thermaplugg"},["q"]="Who is Sicco Thermaplugg?"},{["a"]="Defeating Thermaplugg cuts off the leadership directing the leper gnomes and rogue defenses, securing critical technical data and striking a major blow for gnomish morale. However, it does not immediately cleanse the city. Lethal radiation and thick trogg infestations continue to choke the lower corridors, requiring Mekkatorque to prepare deeper excavations before a full reclamation can occur.",["al"]={"do we retake gnomeregan","what happens when thermaplugg dies","is gnomeregan saved"},["q"]="What changes after Mekgineer Thermaplugg is defeated?"},{["a"]="The hostile Dark Iron clan dispatched emissaries into Gnomeregan, represented by the Dark Iron Ambassador. Ever eager to sabotage both Ironforge and the Alliance, the Dark Irons seek an opportunistic alliance with Thermaplugg, hoping to exploit gnomish technology and weaponized machinery for their own war efforts.",["al"]={"dark iron ambassador","why are dark irons in gnomeregan","dwarves in gnomeregan"},["q"]="Why are the Dark Iron dwarves inside Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="Following the radioactive catastrophe, the surviving untainted gnomes fled through the mountains to Ironforge. Their dwarven cousins granted them sanctuary inside Tinkertown, an engineering enclave within the mountain fortress where Gelbin Mekkatorque governs his exiled people while planning their eventual homecoming.",["al"]={"where are gnomes living","gnome home city","refugees in ironforge"},["q"]="Where are the surviving gnomes living now?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","grubbis","leper gnome","mekkatorque","radiation","thermaplugg","tinkers court","trogg","viscous fallout"},["n"]="Gnomeregan",["s"]="Carved into the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan was once the subterranean capital and greatest technological wonder of the gnomish race. Today it lies ruined and quarantined, poisoned by radioactive fallout following a desperate defense against an underground trogg invasion. Its surviving people now dwell as refugees in nearby Ironforge, while the irradiated halls remain overrun by mutated troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and rogue mechanical sentries.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long before its tragic fall, Gnomeregan stood as a testament to the heights of gnomish brilliance, ambition, and industry. Constructed with the assistance of the nearby dwarves of Ironforge, the sprawling mechanical complex was powered by giant grinding engines, whirring gears, and an intricate ventilation network that required fifteen technicians working around the clock just to maintain fresh air. It was a thriving center of invention, competitive craft, and politics centered on Tinkers' Court, serving as the proud capital from which gnomes contributed invaluable siege engines, flying machines, and armaments to the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War.",["t"]="A Marvel of Iron and Steam"},{["b"]="Around the time the Scourge tore through Lordaeron during the Third War, a subterranean nightmare stirred beneath Dun Morogh. Unwitting dwarven excavations at the ancient titan vault of Uldaman awakened hordes of primitive troggs, which burrowed into the lower foundations of Gnomeregan. Reluctant to abandon the Alliance in its hour of need by asking for help, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his forces fought an agonizing five-year war of attrition against the invaders. When defenses collapsed, Mekkatorque yielded to the counsel of his chief advisor, Mekgineer Sicco Thermaplugg, and authorized venting the city's radioactive waste tanks into the lower levels to eradicate the troggs. Instead, the toxic gas spread uncontrollable catastrophe, wiping out nearly eighty percent of the gnomish population in days.",["t"]="The Trogg Invasion and the Poisoning"},{["b"]="The disaster was no mechanical accident. Sicco Thermaplugg, consumed by jealousy over Mekkatorque's election as High Tinker, intentionally allowed the invasion to escalate and planned the toxic catastrophe, plotting to sweep in, slay the troggs, and seize leadership of the survivors. Instead, the disaster spun beyond his control. The radiation failed to kill the troggs, driving them into a violent frenzy, while Thermaplugg himself was trapped within the contaminated lower tiers. Twisted by radioactive sickness into an insane leper gnome, Thermaplugg crowned himself the techno-overlord of Gnomeregan, commanding mindless leper survivors and erratic machineries from his throne in Tinkers' Court.",["t"]="The Mad Mekgineer's Treason"},{["b"]="High Tinker Mekkatorque currently coordinates the reclamation of Gnomeregan from Tinkertown in Ironforge, dispatching Alliance adventurers into the toxic depths to break Thermaplugg's rule. Slaying the Mekgineer at the heart of Tinkers' Court dismantles his command over the rogue defenses and leper cohorts, delivering long-sought vengeance for his monumental betrayal. Yet a permanent reconquest remains elusive: the deeper tunnels remain choked with irradiated sludge, mutated beasts, and troggs, leaving Mekkatorque to assemble gyrodrillmatic excavationators and formulate broader military plans to one day reclaim his people's ancestral home.",["t"]="A Fragile Victory"}}}}}
t["zone:hallofthanes"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,344,28.365.0,19.340.0,25.399.1,36.188.0,43.182.0,42.174.0,49.153.0,43.116.0,47.227.1",["h"]="b1c245",["n"]="El Salón de los Feudales",["s"]="El Salón de los Feudales. En las profundidades de la bulliciosa ciudad de Forjaz se encuentra el Salón de los Feudales, un antiguo complejo subterráneo impregnado de historia enana. Destinada a los aventureros noveles de la Alianza, esta apartada mazmorra alberga reliquias del pasado del reino de la montaña que se encuentran amenazadas. Lograr acceder requiere desenterrar rutas olvidadas a través de la propia montaña. Mientras Forjaz vibra con el repiqueteo de los martillos en la Gran Fundición, salas olvidadas se adentran mucho más abajo en la piedra. El Salón de los Feudales representa uno de estos venerables confines subterráneos. Ligado durante mucho tiempo a linajes enanos ancestrales y reliquias de cantería, ahora requiere que intrépidos campeones de la Alianza se aventuren en sus sombrías bóvedas para asegurar las profundidades.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The stability of Ironforge directly bolsters the Alliance, making the cleansing of these deep caverns vital to securing the High Seat.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, entering the Hall of Thanes is a journey into the ancestral bedrock of Dun Morogh, purging defilers from sacred halls that bear legendary clan names.",["race:Gnome"]="As close allies living within Ironforge, gnomes share an urgent interest in neutralizing mechanical constructs like Plunder that threaten their shared refuge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Hall of Thanes is located beneath the dwarven capital of Ironforge. It is tucked away in the mountain's deeper, restricted subterranean sectors rather than the main city thoroughfares.",["al"]={"hall of thanes location","where is hall of thanes","ironforge dungeon location"},["q"]="Where is the Hall of Thanes located?"},{["a"]="Entry requires unlocking the dungeon through an attunement questline. Adventurers must begin by pursuing the quest 'Underground Map' to chart a path into the mountain's lower vaults.",["al"]={"how to get into hall of thanes","hall of thanes attunement","underground map quest"},["q"]="How do I gain access to the Hall of Thanes?"},{["a"]="The expedition challenges four major threats: Faldrim Anvilmar, the volcanic behemoth Magmatus, an enchanted golem named Plunder, and the final adversary, Durgen Dirgehammer.",["al"]={"boss list","who are the bosses","hall of thanes bosses"},["q"]="What bosses are inside the Hall of Thanes?"},{["a"]="The dungeon is tailored for Alliance adventurers between levels 13 and 18, serving as an early subterranean challenge alongside Ironforge's deep network.",["al"]={"what level is hall of thanes","hall of thanes level range"},["q"]="What level range is recommended for this dungeon?"},{["a"]="No. The Hall of Thanes is an Alliance-exclusive dungeon situated directly beneath the Alliance capital of Ironforge.",["al"]={"can horde do hall of thanes","is hall of thanes alliance only"},["q"]="Can Horde players enter the Hall of Thanes?"},{["a"]="Overcoming Durgen Dirgehammer breaks the grip of rogue dwarven forces and their summoned constructs deep within Ironforge's foundations. Striking him down restores safety to the ancient ancestral vaults beneath the Great Forge.",["al"]={"why kill dirgehammer","final boss story","durgen dirgehammer lore"},["q"]="What does defeating Durgen Dirgehammer achieve?"}},["kw"]={"attunement","dungeon","durgen dirgehammer","faldrim anvilmar","hall of thanes","ironforge","magmatus","plunder","underground map"},["n"]="Hall of Thanes",["s"]="Deep beneath the bustling city of Ironforge lies the Hall of Thanes, an ancient subterranean complex steeped in dwarven history. Intended for early Alliance adventurers, this secluded dungeon holds relics of the mountain kingdom's past that have fallen into peril. Gaining entry requires unearthing forgotten routes through the mountain itself.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Ironforge hums with the ringing of hammers in the Great Forge, forgotten halls delve far deeper beneath the stone. The Hall of Thanes represents one of these venerable subterranean reaches. Long tied to ancestral dwarven bloodlines and relics of stonecraft, it now requires intrepid Alliance champions to venture into its shadowed vaults to secure the depths.",["t"]="Secrets Beneath the Mountain"},{["b"]="Accessing the Hall of Thanes is no casual feat. The corridors leading to these ancient vaults have been sealed away or hidden from everyday travelers in Ironforge. Adventurers must decipher forgotten charting, beginning with recovering an Underground Map, before they can navigate the deeper tunnels and breach the threshold of the dungeon.",["t"]="Uncovering the Path"},{["b"]="Within the heart of the complex lies a formidable assembly of threats, from enchanted guardians like Plunder and the fiery brute Magmatus to rogue figures of ancient dwarven lineage such as Faldrim Anvilmar. Presiding over the inner sanctuary is Durgen Dirgehammer, whose defeat finally quells the growing unrest simmering beneath the city floor and secures the sacred dwarven halls from subversion.",["t"]="The Threat of Dirgehammer"}}}}}
t["zone:hillsbrad"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,398,25.489.0,37.558.0,28.528.0,56.305.0,33.287.0,23.316.0,54.333.0,23.275.0,51.299.0",["h"]="bb43e6",["n"]="Laderas de Trabalomas",["s"]="Laderas de Trabalomas. Laderas de Trabalomas es una región verde y fértil que representa el último bastión pastoral del reino caído de Lordaeron. A pesar de haber escapado en gran medida a la peste de la Plaga, la tierra está desgarrada por una brutal guerra abierta entre los humanos de Costasur y los Renegados atrincherados en Molino Tarren. Sirve como una violenta encrucijada donde los ejércitos de la Alianza y la Horda chocan sin piedad. Mientras el norte de Lordaeron se pudre bajo la peste de la Plaga, Trabalomas permanece sorprendentemente verde. Sus onduladas praderas, pinares y granjas en activo ofrecen a los viajeros un insólito atisbo de cómo lucía el reino antes de la Tercera Guerra. Sin embargo, esa apariencia tranquila es engañosa. Los pacíficos campos y caminos rurales son recorridos constantemente por patrullas armadas, mercenarios renegados y bestias carroñeras. Lo que debería ser el granero de Lordaeron se ha convertido en su frontera más disputada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Hidden high in the mountains above the foothills lies Ravenholdt Manor, the secretive gathering place and training ground for Azeroth's most elite guild of thieves and assassins.",["race:Dwarf"]="The soldiers of Dun Garok represent Ironforge's resolute military commitment to defending their human allies and containing the undead threat north of the Wetlands.",["race:Human"]="Southshore is one of your people's final refuges in Lordaeron; walking these pastures is a painful reminder of the great kingdom that was lost to betrayal and undeath.",["race:Orc"]="This soil holds monumental weight for your people: the ruined ramparts of Durnholde Keep are where Warchief Thrall broke his chains and reawakened the spirit of the Horde.",["race:Undead"]="Tarren Mill anchors the southern frontier of the Forsaken realm, where Apothecary Lydon works tirelessly to develop the New Plague to secure your people's future."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Scourge marched primarily along the central corridors toward the capital and the northern kingdoms, leaving Hillsbrad largely bypassed by the plague cauldrons that ruined the north. As a result, the soil remains fertile and the vegetation healthy, making it the most pristine remnant of old Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why is hillsbrad green","did hillsbrad get plagued","why no plague in hillsbrad"},["q"]="Why isn't Hillsbrad blighted like the rest of Lordaeron?"},{["a"]="Neither faction holds full control. The Alliance maintains Southshore and nearby farms like the Hillsbrad Fields, while the Forsaken hold Tarren Mill to the north. Dwarven forces hold the fortress of Dun Garok in the east, and the criminal Syndicate occupies the ruins of Durnholde Keep.",["al"]={"who owns hillsbrad","hillsbrad faction control","is hillsbrad alliance or horde"},["q"]="Who controls Hillsbrad right now?"},{["a"]="Durnholde was once the headquarters of the Alliance internment camp system after the Second War, governed by Aedelas Blackmoore, who raised Thrall there as a gladiator slave. Thrall escaped, rallied the orcs, and laid waste to the keep. In the aftermath of Lordaeron's fall, the ruins were occupied by the Syndicate.",["al"]={"durnholde lore","what happened at durnholde","who runs durnholde"},["q"]="What is Durnholde Keep?"},{["a"]="Tarren Mill represents the southern frontier of Sylvanas Windrunner's domain, while Southshore is the Alliance's primary staging ground and port into Lordaeron. The Forsaken view Southshore as an existential threat to their southern flank, while the humans view the undead as horrific usurpers who must be driven from their homeland.",["al"]={"why the southshore war","southshore vs tarren mill lore","hillsbrad conflict reason"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken and humans fight so fiercely here?"},{["a"]="Purgation Isle is an isolated, rugged island off the southern coast of Hillsbrad. Unlike the mainland hills, the island is infested with powerful undead ghouls, skeletons, and vengeful spirits, making it an extremely dangerous offshore haven for dark magic and restless dead.",["al"]={"purgation isle lore","island off southshore","why undead on purgation isle"},["q"]="What is Purgation Isle?"},{["a"]="They belong to the Syndicate, an organized network of former nobility and foot soldiers from the fallen human kingdom of Alterac. Cast out for their kingdom's betrayal during the Second War, they now operate as ruthless bandits seeking to reclaim their lands through blackmail, theft, and slaughter.",["al"]={"hillsbrad bandits","who is the syndicate","syndicate in hillsbrad"},["q"]="Who are the bandits occupying the camps and towers?"}},["kw"]={"azurelode","dun garok","durnholde","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","purgation isle","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},["n"]="Hillsbrad Foothills",["s"]="Hillsbrad Foothills is a green, fertile region that represents the last pastoral bastion of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. Despite having largely escaped the Scourge's plague, the land is torn apart by brutal open war between the humans of Southshore and the Forsaken entrenched at Tarren Mill. It serves as a violent crossroads where the armies of the Alliance and the Horde clash without mercy.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While northern Lordaeron rots under the blight of the Scourge, Hillsbrad remains strikingly green. Its rolling pastures, pine groves, and working farmsteads offer travelers a rare glimpse of what the kingdom looked like before the Third War. Yet that tranquil appearance is deceptive. The peaceful fields and rural roads are constantly swept by armed patrols, rogue mercenaries, and scavenger beasts. What should be Lordaeron's breadbasket has instead become its most contested borderland.",["t"]="A Garden Beside the Ruins"},{["b"]="The political heart of Hillsbrad is defined by two entrenched strongholds. In the south along the coast lies Southshore, an Alliance haven populated by human refugees and soldiers fiercely loyal to the Alliance. To the north sits Tarren Mill, once a quiet human farming hamlet that was wiped out by the Scourge and later fortified as the Forsaken's southernmost garrison. The open ground between the two settlements is known throughout Azeroth as a relentless kill zone, where Alliance and Horde champions wage perpetual skirmishes for control of the region.",["t"]="The War of Southshore and Tarren Mill"},{["b"]="Hillsbrad's history of violence runs deep. During the Second War, its coast and hills witnessed the first massive clashes between the Grand Alliance and the Old Horde. Later, the fortress of Durnholde Keep served as the internment camp where Thrall was raised before leading the orcish rebellion. Today, Durnholde lies in ruins, seized by the Syndicate—displaced human nobles turned bandit cutthroats. Coastal murlocs, hostile gnolls, and the shadowed dead on Purgation Isle ensure that no corner of the hills is truly secure.",["t"]="Old Scars and Hidden Threats"}}}}}
t["zone:ironforge"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="El Rey Magni Barbabronce gobierna Forjaz y el reino de Khaz Modan desde el Trono. Un hábil guerrero y maestro herrero, ha guiado a su pueblo a través de la Segunda y la Tercera Guerra, manteniéndose como un pilar profundamente leal de la Alianza.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="8ff9bf",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Cuando la cercana capital gnómica de Gnomeregan cayó ante una repentina invasión trogg y un desastroso accidente radiactivo, los gnomos supervivientes huyeron hacia Dun Morogh. El Rey Magni les dio la bienvenida en Forjaz, otorgándoles un barrio entero de la ciudad que ahora se conoce como Ciudad Manitas.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="812ba5",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La Gran Fundición es el ardiente corazón industrial de la ciudad, alimentado por cascadas subterráneas de magma derretido. Rodea al Gran Yunque, donde los maestros armeros enanos forjan armas y armaduras legendarias. El propio Rey Magni forjó la célebre hoja sagrada Crematoria sobre este yunque.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="be1e36",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Forjaz está conectada directamente con la Ciudad de Ventormenta mediante el Tren subterráneo, una extraordinaria vía férrea subterránea construida por la ingeniería gnómica que atraviesa el lecho de roca montañosa de los Reinos del Este.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="f12be7",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Forjaz nunca ha caído ante un invasor externo. El clan Foso Sangrante de Kilrogg Mortojo la asedió durante meses durante la Segunda Guerra, y los Hierro Negro combatieron hasta el interior de la ciudad durante la Guerra de los Tres Martillos, pero las puertas y los defensores resistieron.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="c1bd84",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Tras la Guerra de los Tres Martillos, el derrotado clan Martillo Salvaje se trasladó al norte, hacia Los Humedales y las Tierras del Interior, mientras que el hostil clan Hierro Negro se asentó en las regiones de Crestagrana y Roca Negra bajo el yugo del Señor del Fuego.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="f7a0c0",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="9,441,24.622.0,28.636.0,21.574.0,18.482.0,20.241.0,42.268.0,24.269.0,50.210.0,43.250.0,35.236.0",["h"]="4a2ad0",["n"]="Forjaz",["s"]="Forjaz. Tallada en el corazón de la montaña de Forjaz, en la nevada Dun Morogh, Forjaz es la capital ancestral de los enanos Barbabronce y un inexpugnable bastión de la Alianza. Con el calor ardiente de la Gran Fundición en su centro, esta extensa ciudad subterránea sirve como un bullicioso núcleo de comercio, industria y antiguos saberes enanos. Bajo el firme mandato del Rey Magni Barbabronce, ahora también cobija a los gnomos desplazados de la cercana Gnomeregan. Forjaz fue fundada hace dos mil quinientos años, cuando la primera generación de enanos despertó en Uldaman y viajó hacia el oeste, hacia los escarpados picos de Dun Morogh. Al excavar en la montaña más alta, erigieron un inmenso santuario dedicado a su progenitor titán Khaz'goroth junto a la colosal Gran Fundición. Desde entonces, la ciudad se ha expandido en anillos concéntricos alrededor de ese ardiente hogar. A diferencia de las capitales de la superficie, Forjaz está enteramente protegida bajo techos de piedra, caldeada por rugientes hornos y ríos subterráneos de magma ardiente. Sus puertas fortificadas y sus cavernosas profundidades han demostrado ser casi inexpugnables a lo largo de siglos de guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Connected seamlessly to Stormwind via the Deeprun Tram, Ironforge stands as the Alliance's northern anchor and one of its most reliable military fortresses.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The Great Forge is revered across Azeroth as the premier center of metalworking, housing the Great Anvil where master smiths and King Magni himself shape metal into legend.",["race:Dwarf"]="Ironforge is the ancestral home of your kin, standing as a proud testament to your resilience, your mastery of stone, and the sacred lineage tracing back to the titans.",["race:Gnome"]="Since the disaster that consumed Gnomeregan, Tinker Town has served as your temporary home and command center as High Tinker Mekkatorque plots the liberation of your city."},["faq"]={{["a"]="King Magni Bronzebeard rules Ironforge and the kingdom of Khaz Modan from the High Seat. A skilled warrior and master blacksmith, he has governed his people through the Second and Third Wars and remains a deeply loyal pillar of the Alliance.",["al"]={"ironforge king","ruler of ironforge","who is the dwarf king"},["q"]="Who rules Ironforge?"},{["a"]="When the nearby gnomish capital of Gnomeregan fell to a sudden trogg invasion and a disastrous radiation accident, the surviving gnomes fled into Dun Morogh. King Magni welcomed them into Ironforge, granting them an entire quarter of the city now known as Tinker Town.",["al"]={"gnomes in ironforge","why are gnomes here","tinker town gnomes"},["q"]="Why are there so many gnomes in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The Great Forge is the fiery industrial heart of the city, fed by underground waterfalls of molten magma. It surrounds the Great Anvil, where dwarven weaponsmiths craft legendary arms and armor. King Magni himself forged the famed holy blade Ashbringer upon this anvil.",["al"]={"great forge","ironforge anvil","center of ironforge"},["q"]="What is the Great Forge?"},{["a"]="Ironforge is connected directly to Stormwind City by the Deeprun Tram, an extraordinary subterranean railway built by gnomish engineering that cuts straight through the mountain bedrock of the Eastern Kingdoms.",["al"]={"ironforge to stormwind","deeprun tram","train to stormwind"},["q"]="How do you travel between Ironforge and Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Ironforge has never fallen to an outside invader. Kilrogg Deadeye's Bleeding Hollow clan laid siege to it for months during the Second War, and the Dark Irons fought into the city during the War of the Three Hammers, but the gates and defenders held.",["al"]={"has ironforge been conquered","did ironforge fall","ironforge siege"},["q"]="Has Ironforge ever fallen to an enemy army?"},{["a"]="After the War of the Three Hammers, the defeated Wildhammer clan relocated north into the Wetlands and the Hinterlands, while the hostile Dark Iron clan settled within the Redridge and Blackrock regions under the thrall of the Firelord.",["al"]={"where are wildhammers","where are dark irons","three hammer clans"},["q"]="Where did the other dwarf clans go?"}},["kw"]={"bronzebeard","deeprun tram","dun morogh","great forge","high seat","ironforge","khaz modan","magni bronzebeard","tinker town"},["n"]="Ironforge",["s"]="Carved into the heart of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, Ironforge is the ancestral capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves and an unassailable bastion of the Alliance. Centered on the molten heat of the Great Forge, this sprawling underground city serves as a bustling hub of commerce, industry, and ancient dwarven lore. Under the steadfast rule of King Magni Bronzebeard, it now also shelters the displaced gnomes of nearby Gnomeregan.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ironforge was founded twenty-five hundred years ago when the first generation of dwarves awakened in Uldaman and journeyed west into Dun Morogh's jagged peaks. Delving into the tallest mountain, they built a massive shrine to their titan progenitor Khaz'goroth alongside the colossal Great Forge. Ever since, the city has expanded in concentric rings around that fiery hearth. Unlike surface capitals, Ironforge is entirely enclosed beneath stone ceilings, warmed by roaring hearths and subterranean rivers of molten magma. Its fortified gates and cavernous depths have proven near-impregnable throughout centuries of war.",["t"]="A City of Stone and Fire"},{["b"]="For generations, three dwarven clans coexisted within Ironforge: the Bronzebeards, the Wildhammers, and the Dark Irons. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died in 230 BDP, a bitter civil war erupted for dominion over the mountain. The Bronzebeard clan prevailed and expelled their rivals. Later, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan led a vengeful Dark Iron siege that penetrated to the heart of Ironforge before being repulsed by Bronzebeard forces. Thaurissan accidentally summoned Ragnaros the Firelord to the south, shattering the Redridge Mountains and dooming his own host. The Bronzebeards have held undisputed control of Ironforge ever since.",["t"]="The War of the Three Hammers"},{["b"]="During the Second War, the Bleeding Hollow orc clan overran much of Khaz Modan, but Ironforge held firm behind its sealed gates until the Alliance of Lordaeron lifted the siege. Bound by this debt of honor, King Magni Bronzebeard pledged Ironforge's eternal loyalty to the Alliance, standing firm even when kingdoms like Gilneas and Quel'Thalas abandoned it. In the Third War, Magni channeled his grief over the loss of his brother Muradin in Northrend to forge the famed blade Ashbringer at the Great Anvil. Today, Ironforge remains one of the Alliance's fiercest bulwarks.",["t"]="Honor to the Alliance"},{["b"]="Following the tragic fall of Gnomeregan to trogg invaders and irradiation, King Magni opened Ironforge's gates to thousands of gnome refugees. Under High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, the exiles established Tinker Town, carving out a buzzing technological haven within the stone city. Coupled with the subterranean Deeprun Tram connecting Ironforge directly to Stormwind City, the dwarven stronghold has transformed into a lively crossroads of dwarven steelcraft and gnomish ingenuity.",["t"]="A Haven for Exiles"}}}}}
t["zone:lochmodan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,325,16.560.0,31.544.0,20.406.1,52.229.0,35.216.0,52.188.0,30.188.0,44.207.0,64.202.0",["h"]="927e32",["n"]="Loch Modan",["s"]="Loch Modan. Loch Modan es un valle montañoso templado al este de Dun Morogh, famoso por su enorme lago alpino contenido por la monumental Presa de las Tres Cabezas. Centrada alrededor del pueblo enano de Thelsamar, la región lidia con crecientes infestaciones de troggs, kóboldes en las minas y agresivos ogros en las tierras altas del noreste. Situado en el este de Khaz Modan, Loch Modan presenta un marcado y agradable contraste con los campos nevados y helados de Dun Morogh. Cumbres montañosas escarpadas encierran un valle templado de pinos y abedules en cuyo centro se extiende el lago. Esta enorme masa de agua dulce está contenida por la Presa de las Tres Cabezas, un triunfo arquitectónico que se alza imponente a lo largo del borde norte. El apacible asentamiento de Thelsamar actúa como núcleo cívico del territorio, albergando a montaraces itinerantes, cazadores y mineros que aprovechan las productivas vetas de cobre y estaño dispersas por las colinas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The Farstrider Lodge along the southeastern ridges offers a renowned gathering place for trackers hunting the valley's bears, crocolisks, and mountain buzzards.",["faction:Alliance"]="Guarding the line between Dun Morogh and the northern routes toward the Wetlands, Loch Modan is a vital bulwark for Ironforge's territorial defense.",["profession:Mining"]="The hills, quarries, and trogg-infested caves of Loch Modan are rich in accessible veins of copper, tin, and silver.",["race:Dwarf"]="Loch Modan represents both the unmatched engineering genius of dwarven masonry and the dangerous ancient history your people repeatedly uncover beneath the stone."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Stonewrought Dam, a massive wonder of dwarven stonework and engineering, holds back the entire Loch. Dwarven engineers maintain it meticulously, as its failure would wash out the lower marshlands of the Wetlands to the north.",["al"]={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why does loch modan have a dam"},["q"]="What holds the lake back from flooding the Wetlands?"},{["a"]="Dwarven exploratory expeditions and miners accidentally breached underground chambers deep in the mountains, unleashing hordes of savage troggs that quickly swarmed to the surface and carved out camps in the valleys.",["al"]={"why are there troggs here","trogg invasion loch modan","trogg origin"},["q"]="Where did all the troggs come from?"},{["a"]="Thelsamar, nestled on the western bluffs, serves as the main Alliance town and travel hub, featuring the Stoutlager Inn, tradesfolk, and gryphon masters connecting to Ironforge and beyond.",["al"]={"loch modan town","hub in loch modan","thelsamar"},["q"]="What is the primary Alliance settlement in the zone?"},{["a"]="The stronghold in the northeast mountains is held by brute ogres who descended into the valley, establishing a fortified micro-dungeon outpost that terrorizes nearby hunters and travelers.",["al"]={"ogre camp loch modan","ogres northeast loch modan","mogrosh"},["q"]="Who rules Mo'grosh Stronghold?"},{["a"]="Prospector Ironband's archaeological dig was overrun by troggs spilling out from the subterranean chambers, forcing the excavation team to abandon their progress and fight to secure their remaining supplies.",["al"]={"ironbands dig","why was ironbands site abandoned","prospector ironband problem"},["q"]="What happened to Ironband's Excavation Site?"},{["a"]="Yes. Footpaths lead south through the mountains into the arid wasteland of the Badlands, while the Stonewrought Pass through the Valley of Kings leads southwest into the volcanic crags of Searing Gorge.",["al"]={"loch modan to badlands","loch modan south exit","path to badlands"},["q"]="Can you travel from Loch Modan to the Badlands or Searing Gorge?"}},["kw"]={"farstrider lodge","ironband","mo'grosh stronghold","stonesplinter","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","troggs","valley of kings"},["n"]="Loch Modan",["s"]="Loch Modan is a temperate mountain valley east of Dun Morogh, renowned for its massive alpine lake held in place by the monumental Stonewrought Dam. Centered around the dwarven town of Thelsamar, the region struggles under encroaching trogg infestations, kobolds in the mines, and aggressive ogres in the northeast highlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated in eastern Khaz Modan, Loch Modan presents a stark, pleasant contrast to the frozen snowfields of Dun Morogh. Rugged mountain peaks enclose a temperate valley of pine and birch, cradling the Loch itself. This massive body of fresh water is held in place by the Stonewrought Dam, an architectural triumph that towers along the northern rim. The peaceful settlement of Thelsamar serves as the civic heart of the territory, housing traveling mountaineers, hunters, and miners who ply the productive veins of copper and tin scattered throughout the hills.",["t"]="A Highland Jewel"},{["b"]="Loch Modan's tranquil scenery conceals recurrent violence. Broken catapults and ballistae resting on the lake bed remain from the Second War, when the orcish Horde occupied the valley before the dwarves drove them out. More recently, dwarven archaeological excavations accidentally unearthed subterranean swarms of savage troggs. Led by savage chieftains, trogg tribes have overrun the southern canyons of Stonesplinter Valley and the Valley of Kings, threatening trade routes and forcing the Ironforge Mountaineers to wage a desperate defense.",["t"]="Unearthed Terrors and Invasions"},{["b"]="Troggs and the hulking ogres of Mo'grosh Stronghold are not the only dangers encroaching on the valley. Deeper investigations into local sabotages reveal that the treacherous Dark Iron dwarves are operating in Loch Modan. Having made incursions from the burning passes to the south, Dark Iron infiltrators target dwarven blastpowder reserves and harbor sinister designs against the Stonewrought Dam itself.",["t"]="Plots in the Shadows"}}}}}
t["zone:orgrimmar"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="El Jefe de Guerra Thrall gobierna la ciudad desde su trono en el Fuerte Grommash. Dirige la nueva Horda centrándose en el honor, la supervivencia y el legado chamánico, con el estrecho apoyo del cacique Lanza Negra Vol'jin y el veterano comandante Varok Colmillosauro.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="b6a431",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Thrall bautizó la ciudad en honor a Orgrim Martillo Maldito, el legendario antiguo Jefe de Guerra que rompió el dominio del Consejo de la Sombra sobre la Antigua Horda y cedió su armadura de guerra y el Martillo Maldito a Thrall antes de caer en batalla.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="3623a7",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Aunque fue fundada por orcos, la ciudad es un refugio para la tribu de Trols de Lanza Negra (que ocupan el Valle de los Espíritus) y acoge a embajadores tauren de visita en el Valle de la Sabiduría. Un contingente de emisarios de los Renegados también ha establecido su presencia tras su reciente ingreso en la Horda.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="9d1b09",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El Circo de las Sombras es una fisura cavernosa y sombría escondida bajo los riscos del cañón junto a la Calle Mayor. Alberga los gremios de pícaros y brujos de la ciudad, manteniendo sus negocios ilícitos y sus peligrosas invocaciones demoníacas apartados de los distritos civiles.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="8afc82",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Directamente bajo el Circo de las Sombras se encuentra Sima Ígnea, una traicionera red de fisuras volcánicas subterráneas infestada de troggs, elementales abrasadores y brujos traicioneros que conspiran para socavar el gobierno de Thrall desde las profundidades.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="f44402",["i"]=5,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Los zepelines de ingeniería goblin atracan en lo alto de las torres situadas fuera de la puerta principal, ofreciendo vuelos regulares a través del Mare Magnum hacia los Claros de Tirisfal, cerca de Entrañas, y al sur hacia el Campamento Grom'Gol, en la Vega de Tuercespina.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="5a5ae5",["i"]=6,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="9,300,26.525.0,20.512.0,23.464.1,20.231.0,32.212.0,36.284.0,28.241.0,35.230.0,53.203.0",["h"]="dc5229",["n"]="Orgrimmar",["s"]="Orgrimmar. Orgrimmar es la fortaleza capital de los orcos y el corazón palpitante de la nueva Horda de Thrall. Esculpida directamente en los imponentes cañones de roca roja del norte de Durotar, la ciudad fortificada se alza como un monumento a la perseverancia orca y un santuario inquebrantable para trols, tauren y aliados Renegados por igual. Tras la Tercera Guerra, el Jefe de Guerra Thrall guio a los orcos a las áridas costas de Kalimdor para forjar un hogar libre de la corrupción demoníaca y de la servidumbre humana. Tras bautizar la inhóspita región como Durotar en honor a su padre, Thrall fundó Orgrimmar en memoria de su difunto mentor, Orgrim Martillo Maldito. Levantar la ciudad exigió sangre y sudor; con la ayuda de los tauren, los Trols de Lanza Negra, los ingenieros goblins y el Campeón Rexxar, la Horda repelió el asedio de centauros, arpías y feroces lagartos del trueno para asegurar la fortaleza del cañón.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Thrall has restored shamanism to the core of Horde leadership; practitioners gather within the tranquil Valley of Wisdom to study the elements and commune with ancestral spirits.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks find an uneasy refuge here: banished to the secluded Cleft of Shadow, they operate under Thrall's watchful eye while honing their dark arts away from open judgment.",["faction:Horde"]="As the supreme military and cultural seat of the New Horde, Orgrimmar provides all Horde champions with essential weaponmasters, class mentors, trade hubs, and direct audience with Warchief Thrall.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs, Orgrimmar represents hard-won freedom from demonic lethargy and internment, serving as their proud ancestral fortress on the soil of Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="Having lost the Darkspear Isles, the Darkspear trolls found enduring sanctuary alongside the orcs, claiming the Valley of Spirits as a secure spiritual home."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Warchief Thrall rules the city from his seat in Grommash Hold. He leads the New Horde with a focus on honor, survival, and shamanistic heritage, supported closely by Darkspear chieftain Vol'jin and veteran commander Varok Saurfang.",["al"]={"orgrimmar leader","who is in charge of orgrimmar","current warchief"},["q"]="Who rules Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="Thrall named the city in honor of Orgrim Doomhammer, the legendary former Warchief who broke the shadow council's hold on the Old Horde and passed his warplate and the Doomhammer to Thrall before dying in battle.",["al"]={"orgrimmar name origin","who is orgrimmar named after"},["q"]="Why is the city named Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="While founded by orcs, the city is a haven for the Darkspear troll tribe—who occupy the Valley of Spirits—and hosts visiting tauren ambassadors in the Valley of Wisdom. An emissary contingent of Forsaken has also established a presence following their recent entry into the Horde.",["al"]={"races in orgrimmar","who lives here","trolls in orgrimmar"},["q"]="Who lives in Orgrimmar besides orcs?"},{["a"]="The Cleft of Shadow is a dim, cavernous fissure tucked beneath the canyon bluffs off The Drag. It houses the city's rogue and warlock guilds, keeping their illicit trade and dangerous demonic invocations secluded from the civilian districts.",["al"]={"cleft of shadow","underground orgrimmar","orgrimmar warlock area"},["q"]="What is the Cleft of Shadow?"},{["a"]="Directly below the Cleft of Shadow lies Ragefire Chasm, a treacherous network of subterranean volcanic fissures infested with troggs, searing elementals, and treacherous warlocks seeking to undermine Thrall's rule from the depths.",["al"]={"dangers in orgrimmar","ragefire chasm threat","orgrimmar cultists"},["q"]="What threats exist inside the city?"},{["a"]="Goblin-engineered zeppelins dock atop towers outside the main gate, providing regular flights across the Great Sea to Tirisfal Glades near Undercity and south to Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",["al"]={"orgrimmar zeppelins","getting to tirisfal from orgrimmar","travel from orgrimmar"},["q"]="How do you travel to other continents from Orgrimmar?"}},["kw"]={"cleft of shadow","drag","durotar","grommash hold","orgrim doomhammer","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","thrall","valley of spirits","valley of strength","valley of wisdom","warchief"},["n"]="Orgrimmar",["s"]="Orgrimmar is the fortress capital of the orcs and the beating heart of Thrall's New Horde. Carved directly into the towering red-rock canyons of northern Durotar, the fortified city stands as a monument to orcish perseverance and an unyielding sanctuary for trolls, tauren, and Forsaken allies alike.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the Third War, Warchief Thrall led the orcs to the arid coasts of Kalimdor to build a homeland free from demonic corruption and human bondage. Naming the harsh region Durotar after his father, Thrall established Orgrimmar in memory of his fallen mentor, Orgrim Doomhammer. Raising the city required blood and sweat; aided by the tauren, the Darkspear trolls, goblin engineers, and the Champion Rexxar, the Horde drove back encroaching centaur, harpies, and ferocious thunder lizards to secure the canyon stronghold.",["t"]="A Home Chiseled from Stone"},{["b"]="Orgrimmar is naturally fortified by rugged mountains that shield it from both foreign invaders and the violent razor-winds sweeping through Durotar. The settlement is partitioned into distinct natural hollows. The Valley of Strength serves as the bustling civic gatehouse, leading deeper into the trade bazaar of The Drag. Tauren druids and shaman congregate in the serene pools of the Valley of Wisdom, while Darkspear shadow hunters and witch doctors dwell among the stilted pavilions of the Valley of Spirits.",["t"]="Valleys of the Horde"},{["b"]="Beneath the martial pride of the Valley of Honor and the heights of Grommash Hold lies a dimmer reality. In the subterranean cavern known as the Cleft of Shadow, warlocks and rogues practice arts Thrall strictly watches yet grudgingly tolerates. Deeper still plunges Ragefire Chasm, a fiery labyrinth of volcanic tunnels beneath the canyon floor where dark cultists and subterranean beasts fester, threatening the fortress from directly within its own foundations.",["t"]="Shadows in the Red Rock"}}}}}
t["zone:ragefire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,396,18.413.0,17.420.0,19.540.1,40.172.0,31.184.0,40.169.0,64.237.1,46.216.0,50.177.1",["h"]="89f129",["n"]="Sima Ígnea",["s"]="Sima Ígnea. Sima Ígnea es una red de serpenteantes túneles volcánicos situada directamente bajo la capital orca de Orgrimmar. Con entrada a través de las oscuras cavidades del Circo de las Sombras, la sima está infestada de salvajes troggs y una secta demoníaca de fanáticos conocida como la Hoja Abrasadora. De no ser controlados, los oscuros poderes y los enjambres subterráneos que proliferan en las profundidades amenazan los cimientos mismos de la joven nación de la Horda. Bajo el polvo y las rocas rojas de Orgrimmar se oculta un abrasador laberinto de corredores volcánicos y fosas de lava. Mientras los constructores orcos forjaban su nuevo hogar en la superficie, agresivos troggs Furia Ígnea comenzaron a brotar desde las profundidades del subsuelo. Magatha Tótem Siniestro intentó abrir vías diplomáticas con los brutos en nombre de Cima del Trueno, pero su enviado Maur Tótem Siniestro fue masacrado, lo que demostró que los troggs solo cederán ante la fuerza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The dark rites and demonic tomes used by Jergosh the Invoker and Bazzalan offer warlock initiates a firsthand look at the dark magic of the Searing Blade.",["faction:Horde"]="Cleansing the chasm under Orgrimmar is an essential trial for young champions to prove their strength and protect the Horde's vulnerable capital.",["race:Tauren"]="Maur Grimtotem's tragic death at the hands of the Ragefire troggs makes hunting the subterranean beasts a matter of honor and retribution for Thunder Bluff."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance portal is located inside Orgrimmar within the subterranean district known as the Cleft of Shadow. It sits near the tent of the warlock trainer Neeru Fireblade.",["al"]={"rfc location","where is rfc","ragefire entrance"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="The Ragefire troggs tunneled upward from subterranean recesses beneath Durotar. Their sudden presence beneath the capital is regarded as a severe danger that diplomacy failed to quell.",["al"]={"ragefire troggs origin","why are there troggs here","orgrimmar troggs"},["q"]="Why are troggs under Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="The Searing Blade within the chasm is directed by the warlock Jergosh the Invoker and the satyr Bazzalan, both supported by the summoned felguard Taragaman the Hungerer.",["al"]={"rfc bosses","searing blade leaders","who rules ragefire"},["q"]="Who leads the cultists inside the chasm?"},{["a"]="Slaying Bazzalan and Jergosh breaks the active leadership of the Searing Blade cultists lurking under Orgrimmar. Their deaths demonstrate the Horde's resilience and allow Thrall to thwart a demon-worshiping cell right beneath his throne.",["al"]={"bazzalan lore meaning","why kill bazzalan","hidden enemies outcome"},["q"]="What does killing Bazzalan and Jergosh accomplish for the story?"},{["a"]="Physically, any adventurer can walk through the portal, but reaching the Cleft of Shadow deep inside Orgrimmar as an Alliance member requires evading high-level Horde guards and hostile defenders throughout the city.",["al"]={"can alliance do rfc","alliance in ragefire"},["q"]="Can Alliance adventurers enter Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="Thrall tolerates the practitioners of dark magic who gather in the Cleft of Shadow, preferring to keep them close and under his watchful eye rather than drive them out of sight.",["al"]={"thrall neeru fireblade","why let neeru live"},["q"]="Why doesn't Thrall simply execute Neeru Fireblade?"}},["kw"]={"bazzalan","chasm","cleft of shadow","jergosh","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire","rfc","searing blade","taragaman"},["n"]="Ragefire Chasm",["s"]="Ragefire Chasm is a network of winding volcanic tunnels situated directly beneath the orcish capital of Orgrimmar. Entered through the dark hollows of the Cleft of Shadow, the chasm is overrun by savage troggs and a demonic sect of cultists known as the Searing Blade. Left unchecked, the dark powers and subterranean swarms festering below threaten the very foundation of the young Horde nation.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Beneath the dust and red rocks of Orgrimmar lies a blistering maze of volcanic corridors and lava pits. While orcish builders forged their new home above, aggressive Ragefire troggs began erupting from deep below the surface. Magatha Grimtotem sought to open diplomatic channels with the brutes on behalf of Thunder Bluff, but her envoy Maur Grimtotem was slaughtered, proving the troggs will yield only to force.",["t"]="Subterranean Peril"},{["b"]="Far more dangerous than simple troggs is the presence of the Searing Blade, a fanatical cell loyal to the Shadow Council. Operating from the dark caverns alongside the magma streams, this demonic cult plots the utter ruin of the fledgling Horde. They are led by the warlock Jergosh the Invoker, a cunning satyr named Bazzalan, and the vicious felguard Taragaman the Hungerer, who presides over an altar in the lava lake.",["t"]="The Searing Blade"},{["b"]="Neeru Fireblade, an ostensible warlock trainer dwelling beside the chasm's entrance in the Cleft of Shadow, secretly serves as the local leader of the Burning Blade. Neeru sends Horde adventurers into the depths under the guise of loyalty tests, hoping to cull weak cultists and eliminate Thrall's supporters. However, Thrall is fully aware of Neeru's deception. The Warchief uses these forays to eliminate dangerous cult leaders like Jergosh and Bazzalan while letting Neeru remain in place to monitor the Shadow Council's broader schemes.",["t"]="The Warchief's Game"}}}}}
t["zone:razorfenkraul"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,417,21.573.0,20.556.1,23.229.0,34.186.0,25.174.0,48.203.0,48.207.0,59.348.0",["h"]="129962",["n"]="Horado Rajacieno",["s"]="Horado Rajacieno. Escondido en el extremo sur de Los Baldíos, Horado Rajacieno es el corazón ancestral de los jabaespines de Kalimdor. Estas feroces tribus veneran el denso laberinto de zarzas gigantes como el sagrado lugar de descanso de su progenitor, el semidiós caído Agamaggan. En la actualidad, el Horado se ha vuelto agresivamente hostil bajo la tiranía de la matriarca jabaespín Charlga Filonavaja, cuyos oscuros tratos amenazan a toda la región. Hace diez mil años, durante la apocalíptica Guerra de los Ancestros, el colosal dios salvaje Agamaggan se lanzó a la lucha contra la Legión Ardiente. El gran jabalí acabó muriendo en combate, pero su sacrificio preservó la vida en Azeroth. Cuenta la leyenda que allí donde su sangre se filtró en la tierra brotaron enormes enredaderas cubiertas de espinas, formando densos laberintos defensivos por las llanuras del sur. Los jabaespines, que veneraban a Agamaggan como su antepasado divino, reclamaron estas colosales espesuras como sus tierras sagradas y convirtieron la mayor de ellas en Rajacieno.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Quilboar geomancy twists the earth and elements around the blood of Agamaggan, providing a stark look at primal shamanistic powers wielded with savage intent.",["faction:Horde"]="Neutralizing the aggression within the Kraul is essential to protecting supply wagons and fledgling settlements across the southern expanses of the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="The quilboar have long contested Mulgore's borders, and their desecration of the earth through dark alliances makes the cleansing of the Kraul a vital matter of tribal defense.",["race:Undead"]="Apothecaries from the Undercity take an acute interest in the bizarre reagents, bat guano, and rumors of Scourge incursions found within the briars."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Razorfen Kraul is an ancient subterranean network of massive thorny vines in the southern Barrens. It serves as the spiritual heartland and stronghold of the quilboar race, who consider the tangled labyrinth their ancestral home.",["al"]={"what is rfk","explain razorfen kraul","razorfen overview"},["q"]="What is Razorfen Kraul?"},{["a"]="The enormous brambles sprouted from the earth ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, springing forth directly from the blood spilled by the fallen boar demigod Agamaggan.",["al"]={"why are there giant thorns","where did the brambles come from","agamaggan thorns"},["q"]="How were the giant thorns created?"},{["a"]="The Kraul is ruled by Charlga Razorflank, a ruthless quilboar crone and shaman who commands the Razorfen tribe and orchestrates attacks on neighboring villages and travelers.",["al"]={"who is the boss of rfk","charlga razorflank","crone of the kraul"},["q"]="Who rules Razorfen Kraul?"},{["a"]="Beyond constant quilboar raids on nascent settlements in the Barrens, Horde scouts have spotted undead skulking around the thickets, raising terrifying concerns that Charlga is aligning with the Scourge.",["al"]={"why does the horde care","horde rfk interest","barrens threat"},["q"]="Why is the Horde concerned about Razorfen Kraul?"},{["a"]="The aggressive expansion of Charlga's tribe threatens outposts near Feralas and the Thousand Needles, prompting Alliance commanders and scouts at Thalanaar to seek the crone's demise to stabilize the border.",["al"]={"alliance quests rfk","why alliance go here","thalanaar quest"},["q"]="Why are Alliance forces interested in the Kraul?"},{["a"]="Defeating Earthcaller Halmgar, a rare and influential geomancer deep within the thickets, strikes a blow against the quilboar's earth-shaping priesthood. Stripping the Kraul of such powerful elemental summoners disrupts Charlga Razorflank's defensive fortifications and hinders the quilboar's ability to manipulate the sacred brambles of Agamaggan.",["al"]={"what happens after earthcaller halmgar dies","earthcaller halmgar lore","halmgar defeated"},["q"]="What does defeating Earthcaller Halmgar mean for the story?"}},["kw"]={"agamaggan","barrens","charlga","halmgar","kraul","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen","razorflank","scourge"},["n"]="Razorfen Kraul",["s"]="Tucked away in the far south of the Barrens, Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland of Kalimdor's quilboar. These ferocious tribes revere the dense labyrinth of giant brambles as the sacred resting place of their progenitor, the fallen demigod Agamaggan. Today, the Kraul has grown aggressively hostile under the tyranny of the quilboar matriarch Charlga Razorflank, whose dark dealings threaten the entire region.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ten thousand years ago during the apocalyptic War of the Ancients, the colossal wild god Agamaggan threw himself into the fight against the Burning Legion. The great boar was eventually slain in battle, yet his sacrifice preserved life on Azeroth. Legends tell that wherever his blood seeped into the earth, massive thorn-covered vines erupted, forming thick, defensive labyrinths across the southern plains. The quilboar, venerating Agamaggan as their divine ancestor, claimed these colossal thickets as their holy lands, establishing the greatest of them as the Razorfen.",["t"]="Blood of the Boar God"},{["b"]="Razorfen Kraul is ruled with an iron tusk by the elder crone Charlga Razorflank. Under her despotic guidance, the shamanistic quilboar have abandoned their traditional territorial skirmishes to wage aggressive, coordinated war upon rival tribes, regional trade routes, and young Horde settlements. Far worse, troubling whispers and scout reports tell of undead fiends prowling near the brambles. It is feared that Charlga has begun negotiating with emissaries of the dreaded Scourge, seeking to harness forbidden necromancy to bolster her tribe's savagery.",["t"]="The Crone's Ambition"}}}}}
t["zone:riverglades"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,442,22.570.0,25.482.0,20.493.0,24.255.0,28.330.0,27.236.0,46.172.0,34.289.0,28.141.0",["h"]="6df5d9",["n"]="Clarofluvial",["s"]="Clarofluvial. Clarofluvial es un valle fluvial en disputa situado al este de Las Estepas Ardientes y Tierras Inhóspitas, reclamado históricamente por el Reino de Ventormenta. Invadida por la Horda Antigua durante la Primera Guerra y abandonada en gran medida por la corona, la región sigue siendo un campo de batalla mientras los leales humanos locales se enfrentan a los puestos de avanzada de la Horda moderna y a la fauna local. Limita con las Montañas Crestagrana al suroeste, el Pantano de las Penas al sur y mira hacia Tanaris al otro lado del mar. Históricamente parte del Reino de Ventormenta, Clarofluvial quedó en ruinas durante la Primera Guerra cuando la Horda Antigua arrasó la región. Su asentamiento central, Clarosol, fue saqueado por los orcos, quienes perdonaron su torre de magos únicamente para estudiar la hechicería humana antes de esclavizar a los aldeanos supervivientes. Aunque los soldados de Ventormenta hicieron un esfuerzo por liberar a los cautivos y reconstruir, el reino finalmente dio por perdido todo el valle y desvió recursos para defender los territorios centrales. Durante años, la región permaneció prácticamente aislada del apoyo formal de la corona.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance soldiers find old wounds laid bare in the Riverglades, where remnants of the Brotherhood of the Horse continue an unsung crusade to take back land Stormwind abandoned during the First War.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, establishing outposts like Rog'mar ensures a secure coastal foothold and keeps pressure on old human strongholds lingering east of Redridge.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers witness a tragic chapter of their own heritage in Sunnyglade, a reminder of the First War's heavy toll on the eastern frontier of their kingdom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Riverglades is a contested region lying east of the Badlands and Burning Steppes, fronting the Forbidding Sea. Once a flourishing territory of Stormwind, it is now an active frontier contested by the Alliance at Farholde Keep and the Horde at Rog'mar.",["al"]={"riverglades overview","what is this zone","about riverglades"},["q"]="What is the Riverglades?"},{["a"]="Sunnyglade was raided and destroyed by the Old Horde during the First War. The orcs captured the surviving villagers as slaves and kept a local mage tower intact to decipher human magic. Although Stormwind soldiers freed the captives and tried to rebuild, the kingdom ultimately abandoned the area to focus on its western borders.",["al"]={"sunnyglade history","fall of sunnyglade","what happened to the town"},["q"]="What happened to Sunnyglade?"},{["a"]="Farholde Keep is held by Alliance loyalists led by Knight Commander Demar Brant of the Brotherhood of the Horse. His forces have spent years fighting to reclaim the Riverglades after Stormwind originally wrote the territory off as lost.",["al"]={"who leads farholde","alliance in riverglades","brotherhood of the horse"},["q"]="Who controls Farholde Keep?"},{["a"]="A coastal boat runs regularly between Powderfuse Port on the eastern shore of the Riverglades and Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris, offering a direct naval link across the sea.",["al"]={"boat to tanaris","powderfuse port boat","how to get to tanaris"},["q"]="How do you reach Tanaris from the Riverglades?"},{["a"]="You can travel southwest through Redridge Pass to reach the Redridge Mountains, or cross south directly toward the Swamp of Sorrows. To the west, Blackrock Pass leads past the Bristle Hills to the Burning Steppes, while the trails north of Twilight's Shroud run directly into the Badlands.",["al"]={"how to get to redridge","passes from riverglades","exits from riverglades"},["q"]="What passes lead into other zones?"},{["a"]="Krol'dok Stronghold is a fortified dungeon complex in the Riverglades, representing a major seat of hostile power in the contested territory.",["al"]={"kroldok stronghold","riverglades dungeon","what dungeon is here"},["q"]="What is Krol'dok Stronghold?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock pass","brotherhood of the horse","demar brant","farholde keep","krol'dok stronghold","powderfuse port","redridge pass","riverglades","rog'mar","sunnyglade"},["n"]="Riverglades",["s"]="The Riverglades is a contested river valley east of the Burning Steppes and Badlands, historically claimed by the Kingdom of Stormwind. Overrun by the Old Horde during the First War and largely abandoned by the crown, the region remains a battleground as local human loyalists clash with modern Horde outposts and local wildlife. It borders Redridge Mountains to the southwest, Swamp of Sorrows to the south, and faces Tanaris across the sea.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Historically part of the Kingdom of Stormwind, the Riverglades fell into ruin during the First War when the Old Horde swept through the region. Its central settlement, Sunnyglade, was sacked by the orcs, who spared its mage tower solely to study human sorcery before enslaving the surviving townsfolk. Though Stormwind soldiers mounted an effort to liberate the captives and rebuild, the kingdom eventually deemed the entire valley lost and diverted resources toward defending the core homelands. For years, the region remained largely cut off from formal crown support.",["t"]="A Forgotten Borderland"},{["b"]="Despite being left behind by Stormwind's higher leadership, the human defenders never fully surrendered their homeland. Under Knight Commander Demar Brant of the legendary Brotherhood of the Horse, the remaining loyalists hold Farholde Keep as a bastion against the wilderness and hostile invaders. Meanwhile, the modern Horde maintains their own strong presence nearby at outposts like Rog'mar and Bolder'ok, ensuring that the ancient conflict over the glades continues to smolder.",["t"]="The Struggle for Farholde"},{["b"]="Stretching along the coast of the Forbidding Sea, the Riverglades is flanked by mountainous terrain and winding waterways. Travelers on foot can cross west through Blackrock Pass to the Burning Steppes, wind southwest through Redridge Pass toward the Redridge Mountains, navigate south into the Swamp of Sorrows, or trek northwest past Twilight's Shroud into the Badlands. On the coast, Powderfuse Port provides sea passage connecting directly across the ocean to Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris.",["t"]="Geography and Travel"}}}}}
